1
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:05,640
The birds chirping sounds peaceful.

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:06,870
Why is the weather so nice?

3
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:08,110
- It's making me sad.
- The weather is indeed nice.

4
00:00:08,110 --> 00:00:10,980
I wish we had a few days of peace.

5
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:12,080
Right?

6
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:17,050
Here's an announcement from
the Community Center.

7
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:20,090
Starting today, a new team
will be joining Community Town.

8
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:23,320
- Team Gold.
- Silent.

9
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:24,530
- What?
- She just said Gold.

10
00:00:24,530 --> 00:00:27,330
- What?
- Team Gold holds...

11
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:29,430
- a new form of currency, gold.
- He was right.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,970
On the final day,

13
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:36,070
residents will receive prize money
only in the currency...

14
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:38,040
selected through a vote.

15
00:00:38,470 --> 00:00:39,710
- What was that?
- What?

16
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:41,680
- It's a battle of resources.
- A battle of resources.

17
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,010
On Day Nine, when everything has ended,

18
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:45,950
the residents will receive...

19
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:49,020
the final prize in only 1 of 2 currencies,
selected by vote,

20
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:51,020
diamonds or gold.

21
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:53,820
However,
the team that issues the currency...

22
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:56,690
cannot receive the prize...

23
00:00:56,690 --> 00:00:58,790
if the other team's currency is selected.

24
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:01,900
In other words, if diamonds are selected,

25
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,970
Team Gold cannot receive the prize,

26
00:01:04,970 --> 00:01:06,900
even if they hold diamonds.

27
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,540
If gold is selected,

28
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:12,410
Team White cannot receive the prize,

29
00:01:12,410 --> 00:01:14,480
even if they hold gold.

30
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:18,510
From this point on,
all residents will begin a game...

31
00:01:18,510 --> 00:01:21,280
to decide
which currency they will receive...

32
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,580
their final prize in on the last day.

33
00:01:31,890 --> 00:01:33,230
Everyone is new.

34
00:01:33,590 --> 00:01:36,360
- That's the new team.
- It's Luna.

35
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:38,900
- It's Luna.
- No way.

36
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,340
Looks like everyone is gathered.

37
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,710
They look happy.

38
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,210
- I'm nervous.
- It'll be okay.

39
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:55,350
Shall we all stand here?

40
00:02:06,490 --> 00:02:08,200
Luna was standing there.

41
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:20,640
From now on, we'll have Team Gold
introduce themselves...

42
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,840
- to the existing residents.
- I knew it.

43
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,050
They'll introduce themselves.

44
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:26,180
I know someone in that team.

45
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,950
I know him, and we're close.

46
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:31,450
Right. I've been selected as...

47
00:02:31,450 --> 00:02:33,720
Team Gold's leader,

48
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,690
so I'll be introducing myself first.

49
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:38,260
My name is Reboot.

50
00:02:38,290 --> 00:02:42,700
I came here wanting to open the door
to a new era.

51
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:43,930
I'm in your care from now on.

52
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:46,130
I'll do my best
and have fun along the way.

53
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:47,370
I look forward to working with everyone.

54
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:52,810
Reboot.
He and I have known each other for years.

55
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:55,180
He's a weekly guest...

56
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:57,510
on a show I'm on.

57
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:59,980
What's more,
I know he's an admirable person.

58
00:03:00,110 --> 00:03:02,050
"Reboot. He's here."

59
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:06,550
Hi. My name is Shin In Kyu.

60
00:03:06,550 --> 00:03:10,290
I currently work as a practicing attorney.

61
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:13,090
I've also been appearing on various shows,

62
00:03:13,090 --> 00:03:14,860
especially on current affairs shows.

63
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:18,130
I've been involved in politics
for about seven years now.

64
00:03:18,130 --> 00:03:19,700
I want to change this country.

65
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,670
I've always felt that...

66
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:24,210
Korean society needs...

67
00:03:24,210 --> 00:03:27,510
a major transformation
that breaks from the past,

68
00:03:27,510 --> 00:03:30,140
and I really connected with
the word "reboot."

69
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:31,610
That's why I chose Reboot.

70
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:35,550
I first entered politics with
the conservative People Power Party.

71
00:03:35,550 --> 00:03:38,720
I eventually came to feel that I could
no longer continue doing politics...

72
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:42,490
within the party I belonged to,
so I left the party in 2023.

73
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:44,030
Were you the spokesperson for...

74
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:46,190
- the People Power Party?
- Yes, during the presidential election.

75
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:48,560
- The presidential election?
- Were you selected as the spokesperson?

76
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,560
Yes, I was the first.

77
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,700
If you were chosen through an audition,
you must be good with words.

78
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:54,170
You popped up quite often.

79
00:03:54,270 --> 00:03:55,970
- On your algorithm?
- Yes, you were on my algorithm.

80
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:57,570
- Our algorithm must be similar.
- Right?

81
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:59,740
How many shows are you on?

82
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,780
I do about 20 shows a week.

83
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,010
- Twenty?
- Twenty?

84
00:04:03,010 --> 00:04:04,050
As a fixed guest.

85
00:04:04,050 --> 00:04:05,210
What makes me different is that...

86
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:07,180
I don't approach
through partisan thinking.

87
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,720
It's an advantage and a disadvantage.

88
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:09,780
Both sides criticize me.

89
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:12,890
Even when I say,
"I'm a conservative politician,"

90
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:14,290
some people on my own side say,

91
00:04:14,290 --> 00:04:16,720
"You're not a conservative."

92
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:20,800
There are times
when I get criticized from both sides,

93
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,430
but I define my own political identity...

94
00:04:23,430 --> 00:04:25,230
as conservative.

95
00:04:25,230 --> 00:04:27,570
People usually go into politics
because they have...

96
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:31,370
the will to wield power
to create the world they want.

97
00:04:31,370 --> 00:04:34,480
There's obviously an element of
competition in politics as well.

98
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:37,550
In that sense,
I also think of myself as someone...

99
00:04:37,550 --> 00:04:39,580
who's competitive.

100
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,850
- The leader selection...
- Let's decide on a leader quickly.

101
00:04:41,850 --> 00:04:44,520
- I think Reboot should do it.
- Yes, Reboot.

102
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:46,220
Hoping that everyone
will help me out a lot,

103
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,120
- I'll give it my all.
- Okay.

104
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:50,630
- We're in your care.
- We're in your care.

105
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,560
My teammates said...

106
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:56,660
they wanted the leader to be me.

107
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:59,130
I don't think the essence of leadership...

108
00:04:59,130 --> 00:05:01,740
changes that much
depending on the situation.

109
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:05,110
Just like my name suggests,
I want to open the door...

110
00:05:05,110 --> 00:05:08,440
to a new world and create a new model...

111
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,680
of leadership.

112
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:14,350
(Reboot is clearly idealistic.)

113
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,950
Hi, I'm Mokgye of Team Gold.

114
00:05:18,990 --> 00:05:21,320
It means wooden rooster. Nice to meet you.

115
00:05:22,890 --> 00:05:23,990
Nice to meet you.

116
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:26,690
They're all famous. I know them well.

117
00:05:26,690 --> 00:05:29,800
I've played against her
on a different survival show.

118
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,030
Actress Lee See Won.

119
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:33,330
Mokgye? I knew who she was.

120
00:05:33,330 --> 00:05:35,340
I watched the show she was on.

121
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:37,040
I was very much aware of her existence.

122
00:05:38,410 --> 00:05:41,140
Hi, I'm Actress Lee See Won.

123
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:43,610
My nickname is Mokgye.

124
00:05:43,610 --> 00:05:45,350
It comes from "Mokgyejideok."

125
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:47,180
Mokgye represents...

126
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,580
a state of unwavering composure...

127
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:52,850
in which you can win without fighting.

128
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:56,590
This marks my third survival show.

129
00:05:56,590 --> 00:05:59,730
Honestly, educational background
has a huge influence.

130
00:05:59,730 --> 00:06:02,060
It's a good credential to lead with.

131
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:04,570
A good educational background
makes you look smart...

132
00:06:04,570 --> 00:06:06,100
on survival shows.

133
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:09,770
I wrote a paper about game theory.

134
00:06:09,770 --> 00:06:11,310
Game theory is based on the idea that...

135
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:14,080
my choices can change
depending on the other person's strategy,

136
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:16,640
rather than being based
solely on my own strategy.

137
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:20,110
The most well-known example is
probably the Prisoner's Dilemma.

138
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:23,680
Black has a monopoly right now.

139
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,520
Black has all the authority right now.

140
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,720
I'm sure people are unhappy about it.

141
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:31,590
Show them that gold is a way out,

142
00:06:31,590 --> 00:06:33,730
and they'll come to our side on their own.

143
00:06:33,830 --> 00:06:36,600
Ultimately,
the best strategy is Tit-for-Tat.

144
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:40,470
It's a strategy of simply mirroring
the other person's strategy.

145
00:06:40,470 --> 00:06:42,100
An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth.

146
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:46,510
That's been shown to be
the optimal strategy in game theory.

147
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:47,880
I'm going to do the same.

148
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:50,640
While others become fighting roosters,
spilling each other's blood,

149
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:53,180
I'll survive as a wooden rooster.

150
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:54,420
(Consequence: 1, Ability: 2, Meaning: 2)

151
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:58,690
(A consequentialist
who values Meaning and Ability)

152
00:06:59,050 --> 00:07:02,420
Hi. I'm Ugong of Team Gold.

153
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:05,090
- Nice to meet you.
- Who was he? The guy in the middle.

154
00:07:05,090 --> 00:07:06,290
"The Genius."

155
00:07:06,790 --> 00:07:08,100
- Nice to meet you.
- The oriental doctor.

156
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:13,500
I enjoyed the show Ugong was on.

157
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,540
His playing style is quite aggressive...

158
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:17,610
and yet very intelligent.

159
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:19,140
Was it Ugong?

160
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:21,810
I knew he was smart,
but seeing him in person,

161
00:07:21,810 --> 00:07:24,550
I got the feeling that
the team might consist of...

162
00:07:24,550 --> 00:07:26,010
only clever people.

163
00:07:26,010 --> 00:07:27,650
I recognized him the moment I saw him.

164
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:31,450
Ugong's strong impression
and playing style.

165
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:32,920
I remember them all.

166
00:07:32,990 --> 00:07:34,820
"He's joining us? My gosh."

167
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:40,090
My name is Choe Yeon Seung.

168
00:07:40,090 --> 00:07:41,430
Being an oriental doctor is my main job.

169
00:07:41,430 --> 00:07:43,830
I've always liked watching...

170
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:46,700
survival shows as a viewer.

171
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:49,740
I appeared on the survival show,
"The Genius..."

172
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:51,410
and ended in third place.

173
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,610
When I appeared on Season One of
"Bloody Game,"

174
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:55,280
I ended in second place.

175
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,950
My name is Ugong.

176
00:07:57,950 --> 00:08:01,920
It comes from the four-character idiom,
ugongyisan.

177
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:04,950
It's an idiom about
how even a foolish old man can move...

178
00:08:04,950 --> 00:08:08,390
a great mountain
through hard work and action.

179
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:12,790
I chose Ugong because
I keep moving forward steadily,

180
00:08:12,790 --> 00:08:14,600
even if I take things slowly.

181
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:19,700
(Ugong analyzed the game more than anyone
after entering the house.)

182
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:24,970
If there's a game where I can
structurally create eliminations,

183
00:08:24,970 --> 00:08:27,710
I'd lean toward playing in a way
that leads to eliminations.

184
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:30,040
But only as long as I'm guaranteed
to be safe.

185
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:33,480
This team needs as many lives as possible.

186
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:36,980
Even if we give them lives,
there's no guarantee they'll vote for us.

187
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:38,750
Rather than giving lives,

188
00:08:38,750 --> 00:08:40,720
it's better to starve them to death.

189
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:41,990
- True.
- It makes more sense to reduce...

190
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:43,120
Team Red's numbers...

191
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:46,490
before giving them lives, because then,
the prize money per person goes up.

192
00:08:46,490 --> 00:08:49,460
When there are three of them,
there's no need to give it to them.

193
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:52,230
We can give it to them when there are two,

194
00:08:52,230 --> 00:08:54,000
in the spirit of reciprocity.

195
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,740
Someone getting eliminated...

196
00:08:55,740 --> 00:09:00,470
means my expected payoff rises.

197
00:09:00,570 --> 00:09:03,280
Depending on the situation,
elimination might be the answer.

198
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:07,550
Hi. I'm Maetel of Team Gold.
Nice to meet you.

199
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:11,050
Her first impression was very strong.

200
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:13,790
It felt like she could see
right through me,

201
00:09:13,790 --> 00:09:16,390
so I avoided eye contact.

202
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:17,790
She was simply scary.

203
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:21,700
The combination of that aura she has...

204
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,730
and all was quite scary.

205
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:25,030
I'm beyond surprised.

206
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:27,500
She's my senior from college.

207
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:29,400
Maetel was known for...

208
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:32,170
her quick thinking even in college.

209
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:34,010
She's a very cynical person.

210
00:09:34,010 --> 00:09:35,380
She's the number one person to watch.

211
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,710
Hi. I'm Lee So Ra.

212
00:09:38,710 --> 00:09:40,920
I'm currently living near San Francisco...

213
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:43,020
in California, the US.

214
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:45,020
I balance several jobs.

215
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:48,120
I'm the CEO of a skincare product brand.

216
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:50,290
I'm also the founder of...

217
00:09:50,290 --> 00:09:52,330
a K-beauty-related marketing agency.

218
00:09:52,490 --> 00:09:54,960
In the past, I used to work for
Netflix, Meta, and TikTok.

219
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,530
It helped me build connections
with people...

220
00:09:56,530 --> 00:09:58,500
in the entertainment
and advertising industries.

221
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:00,800
So I'm doing various things, including PR.

222
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:03,770
I majored in political science.

223
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:06,210
I once even dreamed of
becoming a politician.

224
00:10:06,210 --> 00:10:08,980
I graduated from UC Berkeley
in California.

225
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:12,410
It's said to be
the most progressive school in the US.

226
00:10:12,410 --> 00:10:16,150
So I'd say my views are
quite socially progressive.

227
00:10:16,150 --> 00:10:19,250
We must circulate the rumor that
gold is good.

228
00:10:19,250 --> 00:10:20,290
Marketing.

229
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:22,290
- Marketing.
- I even wrote a book about it.

230
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:24,090
There are always people
whom everyone likes, right?

231
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:27,230
We need to get those people
to encourage others to use gold.

232
00:10:27,490 --> 00:10:29,600
Ultimately,
I think being good at politics means...

233
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,170
understanding...

234
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:33,370
what the other side wants,

235
00:10:33,370 --> 00:10:35,770
figuring out
where their goals align with yours,

236
00:10:35,770 --> 00:10:37,740
and acting accordingly.

237
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:41,610
Watching Maetel in
the "Galaxy Express 999..."

238
00:10:41,610 --> 00:10:43,680
manga and film series,

239
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:46,710
I got the impression that
she's a quiet but strong person.

240
00:10:46,710 --> 00:10:50,220
I felt that her role
as a very motherly protector...

241
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:53,020
of Tetsuro Hoshino was...

242
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:54,820
similar to mine.

243
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:57,220
Black is also my personal color.

244
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:58,430
(A pragmatic personality,
much like her personal color)

245
00:10:58,430 --> 00:10:59,430
Hence the nickname.

246
00:11:00,690 --> 00:11:02,100
(Luna, Maetel, Ugong, Mokgye, Reboot)

247
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:06,770
(Team Gold is strongly driven by
Consequences and Ability.)

248
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,170
- No.
- No.

249
00:11:09,170 --> 00:11:10,440
- It's okay.
- No.

250
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:12,170
Hi. I'm...

251
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,780
the spy for Team Gold,

252
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:17,910
- What?
- Luna, and an ex-member of Team White...

253
00:11:17,910 --> 00:11:19,810
until yesterday.

254
00:11:19,810 --> 00:11:21,780
- Was she always a spy?
- Was she always a spy?

255
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:23,520
- What?
- Did she start as a spy?

256
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:25,250
- She was a spy.
- That's why she wanted to leave.

257
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:26,590
Yes, I was a spy.

258
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,420
- I told you she could be a spy.
- Wait.

259
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:30,820
- You guys are so innocent.
- I cried...

260
00:11:30,820 --> 00:11:32,230
I told you she could be a spy.

261
00:11:32,230 --> 00:11:35,060
- How could you let her be your leader?
- I told you.

262
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:37,730
- My gosh.
- I told you she could be a spy.

263
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:40,270
- Hey.
- Remember what we talked about?

264
00:11:40,270 --> 00:11:41,640
- Hey, this isn't right.
- I said she could be a spy.

265
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,370
- Bring back our tears.
- Hey.

266
00:11:43,670 --> 00:11:45,570
I would like to point something out
in my defense.

267
00:11:45,570 --> 00:11:48,910
I was only informed
that I was a spy for Team Gold.

268
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:51,380
I found out the rest of the information
only today.

269
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:53,550
Is that why you were determined
to get eliminated yesterday?

270
00:11:56,750 --> 00:11:58,150
- Probably.
- Probably.

271
00:11:58,150 --> 00:11:59,590
- Why even think about it? That was it.
- Yes.

272
00:11:59,890 --> 00:12:01,590
For the past five days,

273
00:12:02,090 --> 00:12:04,220
I praised her for her leadership skills...

274
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:06,590
and her character.

275
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:08,930
I trusted her blindly
and followed her lead.

276
00:12:08,930 --> 00:12:10,960
But it turned out that she was a spy.

277
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:12,470
What about everything she did so far?

278
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:15,640
What about her kindness toward us
and all those nice things she did?

279
00:12:15,870 --> 00:12:16,970
Was everything a joke?

280
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:20,640
Every time she saw me,
she asked me if I was a spy.

281
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:22,110
But she was a spy for Gold.

282
00:12:23,210 --> 00:12:24,750
I was confused when I saw Luna.

283
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:26,110
And she said she was a spy.

284
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:29,050
She should've saved herself
and sent three of them home.

285
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:32,090
It seemed Teams Gold and White
had to oppose each other.

286
00:12:32,190 --> 00:12:35,020
But she decided to eliminate herself.

287
00:12:35,390 --> 00:12:37,320
Had she not eliminated herself,

288
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:40,030
Team White would have only had
two people once she switched over today.

289
00:12:40,030 --> 00:12:42,860
Then it could've weakened
Team White's power even more.

290
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:45,800
I didn't understand
why she didn't do that.

291
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,970
No. I could have saved myself.

292
00:12:47,970 --> 00:12:50,100
Let me offer my two cents here.

293
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:53,170
Honestly,
she didn't do a great job as a spy.

294
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:55,610
If she was a good spy,

295
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:58,150
she would've eliminated one more of you
and saved herself.

296
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:00,110
- Then she should've switched over to us.
- Yes, she should've done that.

297
00:13:00,110 --> 00:13:02,550
- But she sacrificed herself.
- Right.

298
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:05,920
- She had grown too fond of White.
- It's...

299
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:08,060
We did critique her decision.

300
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:09,590
I see.

301
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:13,090
Despite our circumstances,
I was so happy to see her again.

302
00:13:13,090 --> 00:13:16,460
But she was the official strategist
of our team.

303
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:18,300
She knows how we think...

304
00:13:18,630 --> 00:13:19,970
and the rules precisely.

305
00:13:19,970 --> 00:13:23,540
I thought it wouldn't be easy.

306
00:13:24,810 --> 00:13:26,570
So far, I've been with White.

307
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,840
I did my best for them.

308
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:33,810
But once I'm with Team Gold,

309
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:37,550
I have no problem working for my team
100 percent as far as I know.

310
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:43,620
This time around, I'm going to...

311
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:46,790
prioritize my tasks for Team Gold.

312
00:13:51,470 --> 00:13:52,870
- We have a lot of questions.
- Right.

313
00:13:52,870 --> 00:13:54,770
Yes, I know.

314
00:13:54,770 --> 00:13:56,300
- It's crazy she has a document envelope.
- So...

315
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:57,570
Gosh, look at those documents.

316
00:13:57,740 --> 00:14:00,170
I'm going to do my best
to organize my thoughts...

317
00:14:00,470 --> 00:14:02,210
and share all the information.

318
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:04,650
Let me go over
some of the most important takeaways.

319
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:07,110
On the first day,
this was Team White's stance.

320
00:14:07,110 --> 00:14:08,820
"We're not going to jack up
the inflation rate."

321
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:10,750
"We won't devalue the currency."

322
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:12,220
"So give us enough lives."

323
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:13,820
Then...

324
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:17,120
the team didn't reveal how many diamonds
they issued to the other teams, right?

325
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:18,790
Right. That information isn't revealed.

326
00:14:18,790 --> 00:14:21,090
- That's the power Team White has.
- Okay.

327
00:14:21,090 --> 00:14:24,870
Does it mean
they issued 200 more diamonds?

328
00:14:24,970 --> 00:14:27,300
How many did Team White have?

329
00:14:27,470 --> 00:14:28,970
Blue and Red didn't have...

330
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:30,640
- a lot of diamonds, right?
- No, they didn't.

331
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:31,670
- All of them, right?
- Right.

332
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:34,310
- So the teams have been exchanging...
- I see.

333
00:14:34,310 --> 00:14:36,280
their resources. Team Blue...

334
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:40,350
Meeting my new team isn't...

335
00:14:40,350 --> 00:14:41,750
so important right now.

336
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:45,490
Helping them catch up with the history
that's happened so far,

337
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:48,020
learning the rules for Team Gold,

338
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:50,290
and going over the rules with them
were at the top of my list.

339
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:53,530
I was giving them too much information
all at once.

340
00:14:53,690 --> 00:14:56,430
I did my best. But it was difficult.

341
00:14:57,530 --> 00:14:58,900
They don't have a lot of diamonds,
to begin with.

342
00:14:58,900 --> 00:15:01,200
- If we give those four some gold,
- Right.

343
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,570
- We can give them...
- they might lean this way.

344
00:15:02,570 --> 00:15:04,500
- a little bit, so they get a taste of it.
- Yes.

345
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,470
- By those four, do you mean them?
- That way...

346
00:15:06,470 --> 00:15:07,470
Yes. Blue and Red.

347
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:09,180
- Let me erase unnecessary bits here.
- Then...

348
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:11,610
We should...

349
00:15:12,110 --> 00:15:14,580
They were very different from Team White.

350
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:18,020
With Team White,
it felt like I was getting to know people.

351
00:15:18,020 --> 00:15:21,520
With Team Gold,
it felt like I was meeting colleagues.

352
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:23,520
Everyone behaved like a player in a game.

353
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:26,630
On the first day,
it was called Mystery Paper.

354
00:15:26,790 --> 00:15:29,260
For example, we were given a map.

355
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,470
Then we had to name the individual...

356
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:35,240
who drafted the first map in English.

357
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,900
Isn't that Father Kim Tae Gon?

358
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:39,210
Father Kim Tae Gon?

359
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:41,780
It doesn't mean anything. Okay.

360
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:44,310
First of all, they were so professional.

361
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:46,280
It felt like I had to do a better job
at explaining everything.

362
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:48,080
That was the pressure I had.

363
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:52,390
Gold is a new currency in Community Town.

364
00:15:52,850 --> 00:15:54,450
Just like the diamonds,

365
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:56,990
this resource is paid out
as the final prize.

366
00:15:57,690 --> 00:15:59,790
Gold is a transparent resource.

367
00:16:00,190 --> 00:16:02,530
The total gold issued by Team Gold...

368
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:06,070
will be disclosed
to all residents simultaneously.

369
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:10,070
Currently, the Platform acts
as the shop in the Community Town.

370
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:12,910
Only diamonds can be used for trading.

371
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:16,280
The Platform cannot receive gold
for trading.

372
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:19,150
The existing Trading Station
has been closed.

373
00:16:19,510 --> 00:16:21,320
Starting on Day Six, which is tomorrow,

374
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:23,580
when gold, the new currency, is used,

375
00:16:23,750 --> 00:16:26,720
the existing Trading Station
can be reactivated.

376
00:16:27,090 --> 00:16:28,260
- It's about the Trading Station.
- Yes.

377
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:30,720
That's where we traded our resources
in the beginning.

378
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:33,390
Submit one credit to the credit box...

379
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:35,400
at the Trading Station...

380
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:38,270
and submit gold
from one side of the Trading Station.

381
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:40,000
Then the teams can make trades.

382
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:44,270
In other words,
by depositing gold and diamonds...

383
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:46,770
into the opposite sides of the station,

384
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:49,640
having gold on one side
allows the trade...

385
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,240
to complete.

386
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:54,820
It means we can exchange
the diamonds we have...

387
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:56,980
- into gold.
- Right.

388
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:58,850
You do have competition now.

389
00:16:58,850 --> 00:17:00,490
I definitely have competition now.

390
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:03,090
Then we should balance
the amount of diamonds...

391
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:04,930
and gold from now on.

392
00:17:04,930 --> 00:17:06,490
- Right.
- We don't know which one might win.

393
00:17:06,790 --> 00:17:08,200
We're in trouble.

394
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:11,870
Two products could be equally competitive.

395
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,840
But people are drawn to new products.

396
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:17,100
We have to win over Team Red.

397
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:18,840
Red is the casting vote.

398
00:17:18,970 --> 00:17:21,840
Blue and Black can side with us.

399
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:25,010
But it all comes down to
which side Red picks.

400
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:28,780
It's clear that their decision
would affect the outcome.

401
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:32,020
The total amount of gold issued by them
will be disclosed.

402
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:34,390
Team Gold is going to compete
against us...

403
00:17:34,390 --> 00:17:36,290
while offering transparency?

404
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:38,030
We're in big trouble.

405
00:17:38,030 --> 00:17:39,630
They were definitely a major threat.

406
00:17:39,630 --> 00:17:43,130
It became a match between White and Gold.

407
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:44,600
When I roughly thought about it,

408
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:47,130
I was convinced that
Gold would be able to win.

409
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:48,640
The prize money is important,

410
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:50,600
but it's over once they run out of lives.

411
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:53,070
So it's important for them
to buy lives too.

412
00:17:53,210 --> 00:17:55,610
Actually, we have an upper hand.

413
00:17:55,610 --> 00:17:57,810
- The lives...
- Yes, we have enough lives.

414
00:17:57,810 --> 00:18:00,910
I can't say much for the other teams,
but they must be holding by a thread.

415
00:18:00,910 --> 00:18:03,180
Then we have such a big advantage,
don't we?

416
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:05,220
We do, and that's because
we joined the game late.

417
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:07,750
Here's what I think.
This is a game, after all.

418
00:18:07,750 --> 00:18:10,220
Looking at the current structure,

419
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:11,930
it's not balanced at all.

420
00:18:12,230 --> 00:18:14,290
I'm saying that
if there's anything we missed,

421
00:18:14,290 --> 00:18:15,860
we have to figure out what it is.

422
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:17,660
The total number of diamonds
issued by Team White...

423
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:19,870
isn't disclosed to the residents.

424
00:18:20,030 --> 00:18:23,740
I'm sure everyone was unhappy about that.

425
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:25,410
They don't have a lot of diamonds,
to begin with.

426
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:26,910
Of course, they'll switch over.

427
00:18:26,910 --> 00:18:28,810
Then the majority would side with us.

428
00:18:28,810 --> 00:18:30,580
We have enough lives for five days.

429
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:32,250
We could help out Team Red...

430
00:18:32,250 --> 00:18:34,610
by giving them
all the extra lives we have.

431
00:18:34,850 --> 00:18:36,420
They're going to run out soon.

432
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:39,320
Then it would be over, wouldn't it?
That's how I evaluated the situation.

433
00:18:39,650 --> 00:18:40,820
It's finally happening.

434
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:42,490
We're the only ones...

435
00:18:42,490 --> 00:18:43,820
who would choose gold.

436
00:18:43,820 --> 00:18:46,230
If we choose gold, Gold will win.

437
00:18:46,230 --> 00:18:48,500
If we choose diamonds, White will win.

438
00:18:48,630 --> 00:18:51,800
I wasn't sure what to do
because information was limited.

439
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:54,570
I wanted to think more about this
before making a decision.

440
00:18:55,370 --> 00:18:57,270
Team Gold will begin...

441
00:18:57,270 --> 00:18:59,370
their Gold Speech soon.

442
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:02,510
Residents, please take a seat.

443
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:10,780
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)

444
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:16,720
(Episode 7: Panic)

445
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:19,430
- Hello.
- Hello. Nice to meet you.

446
00:19:19,430 --> 00:19:20,730
- Hello.
- Hi.

447
00:19:20,790 --> 00:19:24,100
As I introduced myself earlier,
my nickname is Reboot.

448
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:26,270
I heard several issues came up...

449
00:19:26,270 --> 00:19:28,440
regarding the rules in the Community...

450
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,870
and currency issuance.

451
00:19:30,970 --> 00:19:33,540
I'd like you to look at gold...

452
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:37,040
as this new currency we're introducing.

453
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:40,050
It's open to all, fair to all,

454
00:19:40,210 --> 00:19:41,820
and transparent to all.

455
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:45,220
So we brought this new currency, gold.

456
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:47,290
I hope you show a lot of interest
in our currency.

457
00:19:47,290 --> 00:19:48,790
And I'd want nothing more than...

458
00:19:48,790 --> 00:19:51,020
to get along with each other
for the remaining time here.

459
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:53,590
I'd like to promise you...

460
00:19:53,590 --> 00:19:56,230
with full confidence that...

461
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:58,170
we'll stay transparent and fair...

462
00:19:58,170 --> 00:20:00,400
while fulfilling our missions.

463
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,470
Thank you.

464
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:04,300
He's such a great speaker.

465
00:20:05,770 --> 00:20:09,340
Did they tell you how much prize money
we have left so far?

466
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:11,240
- Yes, we're aware.
- How much did they tell you?

467
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:12,650
- We heard it was 100,000 dollars.
- Right.

468
00:20:12,650 --> 00:20:14,280
We burned some of it.
We're sorry about that.

469
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:15,750
- It's a pity.
- Yes.

470
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:17,480
- Absolutely.
- It's heartbreaking that...

471
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,850
some people had to go home.

472
00:20:18,850 --> 00:20:21,790
I'd like to ask you one more question.

473
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:23,220
We'd like to know...

474
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:25,930
how much gold has been issued so far.

475
00:20:26,090 --> 00:20:28,430
We have 200 gold pieces so far.

476
00:20:28,430 --> 00:20:29,700
- Would you like to see them?
- Yes.

477
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:30,900
- We...
- Let's show them.

478
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:33,670
- We'll be transparent. Open them up.
- All of a sudden?

479
00:20:33,870 --> 00:20:35,300
- I bet this is part of their performance.
- There.

480
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:37,470
We brought everything.

481
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:39,910
- That's so cool.
- That's all 200 of them.

482
00:20:39,910 --> 00:20:44,180
We're not afraid of disclosing our gold...

483
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:46,510
- Right. That's the total amount.
- because...

484
00:20:46,510 --> 00:20:49,080
our currency is transparent.

485
00:20:49,420 --> 00:20:51,550
So far, you've been trading
with your eyes closed.

486
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:55,390
It's the same as dealing in the darkness.

487
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:58,190
How much longer will you put up with this?

488
00:20:58,630 --> 00:21:00,890
How much longer will you tolerate...

489
00:21:00,890 --> 00:21:04,530
the uncertainty of what you're giving away
versus gaining?

490
00:21:05,370 --> 00:21:08,170
We're not afraid of disclosing
what we have.

491
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:10,700
- She's good.
- Thank you.

492
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:12,110
"This is an amazing currency."

493
00:21:12,110 --> 00:21:14,310
That's all you need to take away
from this.

494
00:21:14,310 --> 00:21:16,280
- Sure, one more question.
- I have a question.

495
00:21:16,280 --> 00:21:18,810
I'd like to know
if you guys received lives...

496
00:21:18,910 --> 00:21:21,350
- Yes, we did.
- and if you guys need more.

497
00:21:21,350 --> 00:21:24,480
It's not that
we don't have any lives at all.

498
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:26,390
We're willing...

499
00:21:26,390 --> 00:21:28,460
to share the lives we've acquired.

500
00:21:29,090 --> 00:21:30,890
- I see.
- There are a lot of us here.

501
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:37,860
If we wanted to get lives,
where could we get them?

502
00:21:37,860 --> 00:21:40,470
You can buy them through the Platform.

503
00:21:40,530 --> 00:21:41,770
- Okay.
- You can come to me.

504
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:45,170
You can buy the resources
I have such as credits and lives...

505
00:21:45,170 --> 00:21:47,070
with diamonds.

506
00:21:47,210 --> 00:21:48,640
But you don't have any diamonds.

507
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:51,880
We can negotiate the relative value...

508
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:54,280
of diamonds and gold...

509
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:56,250
in order to make these trades.

510
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:59,520
I'm sorry to interrupt.
According to my knowledge,

511
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:02,220
these trades won't be possible.

512
00:22:02,390 --> 00:22:03,690
- We can't?
- Right.

513
00:22:03,690 --> 00:22:04,720
- It's the rule.
- Let me explain.

514
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:06,290
- That sounds about right.
- Gold can't be used...

515
00:22:06,290 --> 00:22:08,430
- at the Platform.
- Right.

516
00:22:08,430 --> 00:22:10,400
We can't trade with you, Vector.

517
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:12,770
- I see. They can't trade with each other.
- There will be another trading station?

518
00:22:12,770 --> 00:22:14,000
- You guys are competitors.
- Right.

519
00:22:14,270 --> 00:22:16,100
- I see.
- Then...

520
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:18,440
he won't be able to hold any gold.

521
00:22:20,310 --> 00:22:22,980
Then how should we play this?

522
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:24,210
Here's what's most important.

523
00:22:24,210 --> 00:22:27,250
We have to take half of the lives
Vector has.

524
00:22:27,250 --> 00:22:30,020
We need to sit tight
and watch how it pans out.

525
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:31,850
That's the safest and surest approach
we can take.

526
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:33,920
We need to think about
how we want to play this out.

527
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,190
- I don't know what's what now.
- Yes.

528
00:22:35,190 --> 00:22:37,090
We need to review the information first.

529
00:22:37,090 --> 00:22:38,990
I'd like to ask something to Blue...

530
00:22:38,990 --> 00:22:39,990
- and Red.
- Sure.

531
00:22:39,990 --> 00:22:43,160
You've been making trades
through the Platform so far.

532
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:45,900
Did you always think
the prices were reasonable?

533
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,800
As for Team Red,

534
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:51,270
I believe we were treated terribly.

535
00:22:52,110 --> 00:22:53,110
But...

536
00:22:53,110 --> 00:22:55,680
We don't have a particular strength.

537
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:57,010
But...

538
00:22:57,010 --> 00:23:00,150
if a new trade window opens,

539
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:02,280
what's needed...

540
00:23:02,450 --> 00:23:05,020
is not Black. It's the new credit.

541
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:09,020
I'm very happy about Team Gold joining.

542
00:23:10,420 --> 00:23:13,090
The wall code next to the TV
keeps lingering in front of my eyes.

543
00:23:13,090 --> 00:23:14,230
Right.

544
00:23:14,830 --> 00:23:16,560
- Which one?
- Did you enter the room?

545
00:23:16,730 --> 00:23:18,130
Was there a code...

546
00:23:18,130 --> 00:23:19,330
on the wall next to the TV?

547
00:23:25,110 --> 00:23:26,410
We are the ones to solve it.

548
00:23:26,410 --> 00:23:27,410
- Right.
- Right.

549
00:23:27,410 --> 00:23:29,380
- Only we know the answer.
- Right.

550
00:23:29,380 --> 00:23:30,540
- That is, if we don't reveal it.
- But...

551
00:23:30,780 --> 00:23:32,310
Do you happen to be good at acting?

552
00:23:33,050 --> 00:23:34,110
I'm asking all of you.

553
00:23:34,810 --> 00:23:36,420
- I can make myself act.
- I must if I have to.

554
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:39,090
If we all gather together,

555
00:23:39,090 --> 00:23:40,290
they will ask about it.

556
00:23:40,290 --> 00:23:41,920
We'll say we have...

557
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,190
- so many rules to remember.
- Right.

558
00:23:43,390 --> 00:23:45,690
Unless someone brings it up,

559
00:23:45,690 --> 00:23:47,430
- we won't talk about it.
- We won't talk about it.

560
00:23:47,430 --> 00:23:48,860
- We'll pretend not to know.
- We'll pretend not to know.

561
00:23:48,860 --> 00:23:50,730
All of us will say we didn't see it.

562
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:52,830
- Was there a code...
- The wall.

563
00:23:52,830 --> 00:23:53,970
on the wall next to the TV?

564
00:23:53,970 --> 00:23:55,170
There wasn't a TV.

565
00:23:55,170 --> 00:23:56,800
- Was there no code?
- Come here.

566
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:57,800
Was there no code?

567
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:58,810
Is there no reason for them to reveal it?

568
00:23:58,810 --> 00:24:01,010
Right.

569
00:24:01,010 --> 00:24:02,910
We... The plug?

570
00:24:02,980 --> 00:24:05,280
- No. On the wall...
- Gosh, that's too much!

571
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:07,310
- They already came up with a plan!
- Come on!

572
00:24:07,310 --> 00:24:09,220
Why bring actors?

573
00:24:09,220 --> 00:24:10,780
- We already have actors!
- Hold on!

574
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:12,950
They might not know what it is.
Let's wait for them.

575
00:24:12,950 --> 00:24:14,620
It hasn't been long since they came.

576
00:24:14,850 --> 00:24:16,420
There's no way they won't know about it
when Luna is here.

577
00:24:16,420 --> 00:24:18,690
- There's no way she won't know about it.
- She definitely knows about it.

578
00:24:18,990 --> 00:24:21,800
There's the wall code...

579
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:23,900
that can reveal
the weapon dealer's identity.

580
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,200
Team Gold joined.

581
00:24:26,370 --> 00:24:29,200
There might be a code hidden
somewhere in their dormitory.

582
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:32,070
If that gets solved,

583
00:24:32,070 --> 00:24:34,870
I will lose all of the prize money
I've collected.

584
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:39,010
I run the Platform,
and I can only deal with diamonds.

585
00:24:39,010 --> 00:24:40,710
I couldn't deal with gold.

586
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:44,320
That finally meant that
Black had an enemy.

587
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:47,120
There was a team that threatened Black.

588
00:24:47,390 --> 00:24:49,920
That was why I worked really hard...

589
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:52,390
to make myself
on the original residents' side.

590
00:24:53,090 --> 00:24:56,400
Black becomes the nice guy
he originally was, starting from today.

591
00:24:56,630 --> 00:24:58,870
He monopolized everything.

592
00:24:59,100 --> 00:25:01,600
I didn't understand
this person's kindness toward us at first.

593
00:25:01,730 --> 00:25:03,470
But I understand it now.

594
00:25:03,470 --> 00:25:06,040
To prepare for the future...

595
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:08,170
and to make his own team,

596
00:25:08,580 --> 00:25:11,880
he had to show kindness,

597
00:25:12,150 --> 00:25:14,380
and many of his charges were cleared.

598
00:25:15,380 --> 00:25:17,750
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

599
00:25:18,220 --> 00:25:20,520
Today's trade is the Gold Rush.

600
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:24,020
The Gold Rush takes place
in the Community Center.

601
00:25:24,220 --> 00:25:28,600
A trade between gold
and existing resources is permitted.

602
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:31,900
No credits are needed in the Gold Rush.

603
00:25:32,530 --> 00:25:36,400
Team Gold's resources
can be freely traded...

604
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:38,740
with the resources of the existing teams.

605
00:25:39,610 --> 00:25:41,510
"No credits are needed in the Gold Rush."

606
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:42,610
Credits are trash.

607
00:25:42,980 --> 00:25:46,350
During the Gold Rush,

608
00:25:46,450 --> 00:25:48,980
all teams must negotiate with Team Gold.

609
00:25:50,420 --> 00:25:51,580
It's fine...

610
00:25:51,580 --> 00:25:54,490
even if no trade occurs
after the negotiations.

611
00:25:55,620 --> 00:25:57,020
- We must go.
- We're urged to negotiate.

612
00:25:57,490 --> 00:25:59,530
- They will try to persuade us.
- Right.

613
00:25:59,990 --> 00:26:02,000
During Day Five with the Gold Rush,

614
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:04,000
a war cannot be declared.

615
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:05,900
War cannot be declared today.

616
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,830
War cannot be declared today.

617
00:26:10,970 --> 00:26:12,610
- Team Red...
- During negotiations,

618
00:26:12,610 --> 00:26:14,470
- all residents including the leaders...
- Do you wish to talk?

619
00:26:14,470 --> 00:26:15,810
- may freely participate.
- Yes.

620
00:26:15,810 --> 00:26:16,880
- Let's go.
- RIght.

621
00:26:20,650 --> 00:26:24,080
We all have to negotiate with Team Gold.

622
00:26:24,080 --> 00:26:25,080
Right.

623
00:26:25,080 --> 00:26:27,650
- Let's go and talk.
- Team Gold,

624
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:30,890
- please head to the Community Center.
- We need to get going now.

625
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:33,030
Shall we start moving first?

626
00:26:33,030 --> 00:26:35,660
- See you later.
- See you.

627
00:26:35,660 --> 00:26:36,760
- See you.
- Right.

628
00:26:36,760 --> 00:26:38,500
The total amount of gold is shown there.

629
00:26:39,230 --> 00:26:40,330
It's 200.

630
00:26:40,330 --> 00:26:41,400
(The total amount of gold
can be seen right away.)

631
00:26:42,570 --> 00:26:43,800
"From now on,"

632
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:46,410
"credits won't be needed
for the Gold Rush!"

633
00:26:46,410 --> 00:26:49,380
"Don't miss out!"
It felt like a grand opening.

634
00:26:50,210 --> 00:26:52,750
That was why I wanted to meet up with...

635
00:26:53,050 --> 00:26:55,880
the other teams except for Team Gold.

636
00:26:56,080 --> 00:26:58,690
Black would've definitely
felt the need for that as well.

637
00:26:58,690 --> 00:27:00,820
With those rules,

638
00:27:01,050 --> 00:27:03,190
there was nothing Black could do.

639
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:06,390
"They're a lot tighter than I thought."

640
00:27:06,690 --> 00:27:09,660
I heard that there were people
who got eliminated.

641
00:27:09,900 --> 00:27:11,700
After going through that kind of hardship,

642
00:27:11,700 --> 00:27:13,830
people tend to get closer.

643
00:27:14,230 --> 00:27:16,440
I thought, "It won't be easy
to get through them."

644
00:27:16,840 --> 00:27:19,870
They all seem to have a great bond.

645
00:27:19,870 --> 00:27:22,410
- They've been together for five days.
- Right.

646
00:27:22,410 --> 00:27:25,040
We joined in the middle,

647
00:27:25,040 --> 00:27:26,710
