744
00:31:21,910 --> 00:31:23,680
He offered to give everything he had,

745
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:26,120
and that felt so off.

746
00:31:26,690 --> 00:31:28,720
There's another method.

747
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:31,520
We can trust Team Red
and give them our full support.

748
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:33,490
I'll give my skill...

749
00:31:34,030 --> 00:31:35,390
to Team Red today.

750
00:31:35,390 --> 00:31:37,030
- Then, they'll use it.
- They'll use it today.

751
00:31:37,030 --> 00:31:38,530
- Before the productive activities.
- Right away.

752
00:31:38,530 --> 00:31:39,900
(Let's use Team Red's bomb right away.)

753
00:31:40,170 --> 00:31:42,000
This is the best method thought of...

754
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:44,000
for diamonds to win.

755
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:47,010
That way, we can survive
for a longer period of time.

756
00:31:47,010 --> 00:31:49,410
- I'll share my thoughts.
- Right.

757
00:31:50,040 --> 00:31:52,410
The survival of Team Red is my priority.

758
00:31:52,410 --> 00:31:53,980
- Right.
- But what's the problem?

759
00:31:54,610 --> 00:31:57,720
There aren't many lives left.

760
00:31:58,320 --> 00:31:59,390
Right.

761
00:31:59,390 --> 00:32:01,750
If we don't get enough food to survive,

762
00:32:01,750 --> 00:32:03,720
we have to produce lives.

763
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:05,220
- Listen to this.
- But...

764
00:32:05,220 --> 00:32:07,230
- During the remaining three days,
- Right.

765
00:32:07,390 --> 00:32:08,430
We can all survive.

766
00:32:08,430 --> 00:32:09,960
- we just need to produce six.
- Right.

767
00:32:10,300 --> 00:32:12,830
It's 6 times 4. We need 24.

768
00:32:13,730 --> 00:32:15,000
- Right now...
- We have 18.

769
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:16,640
We have 18.

770
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:17,670
(Platform 14, White 2, Red 2)

771
00:32:17,670 --> 00:32:19,170
We just need to produce six more.

772
00:32:19,170 --> 00:32:20,240
(They need 6 more lives
for all of them to survive.)

773
00:32:20,470 --> 00:32:23,080
- We have three teams that can produce.
- Right.

774
00:32:23,240 --> 00:32:25,040
The credit team...

775
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:26,650
can produce lives instead of credits.

776
00:32:26,650 --> 00:32:29,220
All we have to do
is sweep away the remaining lives.

777
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:32,590
Do you all agree that my method...

778
00:32:32,720 --> 00:32:34,290
is possible?

779
00:32:34,290 --> 00:32:36,620
- I don't agree.
- You don't?

780
00:32:36,620 --> 00:32:38,120
- Why not?
- This is why.

781
00:32:38,620 --> 00:32:40,790
I'll agree if we have 12 lives
in our inventory.

782
00:32:41,530 --> 00:32:43,230
(The amount needed for all 3 members
of Team Red to survive until the end)

783
00:32:43,230 --> 00:32:45,430
I'll agree if I have 12 lives in my hands.

784
00:32:46,330 --> 00:32:48,200
- I'm serious. But it's not a guarantee.
- Right.

785
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:49,200
Nobody can be sure.

786
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,670
- Nobody can guarantee that.
- Right.

787
00:32:50,670 --> 00:32:51,970
That's ten more.

788
00:32:52,340 --> 00:32:53,570
- Right.
- Right.

789
00:32:53,710 --> 00:32:56,010
But if they declare war after that,

790
00:32:56,010 --> 00:32:57,310
- it's a huge loss.
- Right.

791
00:32:57,310 --> 00:32:59,080
That is why we must use
the weapon quickly.

792
00:32:59,150 --> 00:33:00,810
We should kill one of them
with our weapon.

793
00:33:00,980 --> 00:33:03,320
They will become less productive
after losing one.

794
00:33:03,750 --> 00:33:04,920
Isn't it funny?

795
00:33:04,920 --> 00:33:07,320
We called out for peace yesterday.

796
00:33:07,490 --> 00:33:09,620
"We won't harm anyone."

797
00:33:09,620 --> 00:33:12,630
But all of a sudden,
"Can't we use the bomb right away?"

798
00:33:12,630 --> 00:33:15,190
"Won't that kill someone?"

799
00:33:15,330 --> 00:33:17,500
They became war freaks.

800
00:33:17,730 --> 00:33:20,570
Whenever a new powerful nation appears,

801
00:33:20,570 --> 00:33:23,000
the originally dominant nation...

802
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:24,840
suppresses that new nation.

803
00:33:25,300 --> 00:33:28,340
I often thought, "That is unjust."

804
00:33:28,340 --> 00:33:29,910
But after being in that position,

805
00:33:30,310 --> 00:33:31,640
I understood why they were like that.

806
00:33:31,880 --> 00:33:33,510
I felt really urgent.

807
00:33:33,510 --> 00:33:36,250
I felt desperate at that moment.

808
00:33:36,550 --> 00:33:38,420
Three people got eliminated yesterday.

809
00:33:38,420 --> 00:33:40,650
If they decide to team up with Team Gold,

810
00:33:41,250 --> 00:33:42,990
there's nothing we can do.

811
00:33:43,220 --> 00:33:47,490
Our team was on the verge
of getting wiped out.

812
00:33:47,730 --> 00:33:50,100
That was why I had to persuade them
in any way possible.

813
00:33:50,100 --> 00:33:52,470
I got worked up at that moment.

814
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:56,040
I have the supermarket rights.

815
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:57,440
I won't sell food starting today.

816
00:33:58,800 --> 00:34:01,040
- Hold on.
- Hold on. Then...

817
00:34:01,040 --> 00:34:03,110
Can't you eliminate them all
with just two blows?

818
00:34:03,110 --> 00:34:05,310
- This just crossed my mind.
- Yes?

819
00:34:05,410 --> 00:34:07,750
They've joined this community...

820
00:34:07,750 --> 00:34:08,880
- as new residents.
- Right.

821
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,680
But the eight of us...

822
00:34:10,680 --> 00:34:12,790
are already discussing
getting rid of them.

823
00:34:12,790 --> 00:34:14,820
We're not sure...

824
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:17,890
what their goal is...

825
00:34:17,890 --> 00:34:19,990
or what direction they'll take to survive.

826
00:34:20,090 --> 00:34:22,290
Without even listening to them,

827
00:34:22,290 --> 00:34:23,900
we're already discussing going nuclear...

828
00:34:23,900 --> 00:34:25,930
just to eliminate the new people.

829
00:34:25,930 --> 00:34:27,600
We should think about whether...

830
00:34:27,600 --> 00:34:29,170
- that's the right way to go.
- To me,

831
00:34:29,170 --> 00:34:30,970
it's pretty clear.

832
00:34:30,970 --> 00:34:32,910
We aren't playing this game...

833
00:34:32,910 --> 00:34:34,440
for the greater good.

834
00:34:34,440 --> 00:34:36,340
- We're trying to win a prize.
- We're trying to determine...

835
00:34:36,340 --> 00:34:38,610
which currencies are valuable...

836
00:34:38,610 --> 00:34:40,280
and which ones we should stick to.

837
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:41,450
- Now...
- That's it.

838
00:34:41,450 --> 00:34:43,680
Currently,
we're leaning toward diamonds...

839
00:34:43,680 --> 00:34:45,520
as our main currency,

840
00:34:45,520 --> 00:34:47,950
while the other side
is promising transparency.

841
00:34:47,950 --> 00:34:49,720
But who do we have on our team?

842
00:34:49,720 --> 00:34:50,890
Black, right?

843
00:34:50,890 --> 00:34:52,220
There's another way.

844
00:34:52,220 --> 00:34:54,390
We don't need credits
to trade at the Platform.

845
00:34:54,390 --> 00:34:55,930
- Right.
- The other team does.

846
00:34:55,930 --> 00:34:57,800
Let's say we used up all the credits.

847
00:34:57,800 --> 00:35:00,430
Then no one will be able to betray anyone,
even if they wanted to.

848
00:35:00,430 --> 00:35:01,730
The simplest way...

849
00:35:01,730 --> 00:35:03,700
is to never trade with Team Gold.

850
00:35:03,700 --> 00:35:05,270
Exactly. Just chat with them.

851
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:08,170
- That's the simplest way.
- It is.

852
00:35:08,170 --> 00:35:09,240
But for instance,

853
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:11,240
- Wait!
- at the very end...

854
00:35:11,240 --> 00:35:12,980
- I'm sorry, but let me say one thing.
- Okay.

855
00:35:12,980 --> 00:35:15,210
There are eight of us here,

856
00:35:15,210 --> 00:35:16,850
and you two are doing most of the talking.

857
00:35:16,850 --> 00:35:18,320
However, the final decision
heavily depends...

858
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:19,650
- on Red and Blue.
- That's right.

859
00:35:19,650 --> 00:35:22,460
But the two of you
talking at such length...

860
00:35:22,460 --> 00:35:24,420
doesn't really help us...

861
00:35:24,420 --> 00:35:26,330
reach a decision.

862
00:35:26,890 --> 00:35:28,930
It looks like you two are trying...

863
00:35:28,930 --> 00:35:30,800
to sell us on an idea,

864
00:35:30,800 --> 00:35:33,800
like going nuclear,
sending everyone packing,

865
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:35,900
and starting an all-out war.

866
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:37,740
But we need...

867
00:35:37,740 --> 00:35:39,040
to get a clear picture...

868
00:35:39,040 --> 00:35:40,040
- of what's happening first.
- You want the bigger picture.

869
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:42,240
That's why they arranged Gold Rush,

870
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:45,440
giving Team Gold a chance
to explain their position to us.

871
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:48,010
We should take some time...

872
00:35:48,010 --> 00:35:49,980
to assess the situation first.

873
00:35:50,420 --> 00:35:53,220
How are we going to use the gold?

874
00:35:53,220 --> 00:35:55,290
Are we going to weigh our options with it,

875
00:35:55,290 --> 00:35:57,020
or maybe do something else?

876
00:35:57,020 --> 00:35:59,790
We don't have a clear idea on that yet.

877
00:35:59,790 --> 00:36:02,390
Team Gold has joined the community now...

878
00:36:02,390 --> 00:36:03,700
and is living here,

879
00:36:03,700 --> 00:36:06,770
so is it fair or right to attack them
on their first day...

880
00:36:06,770 --> 00:36:09,740
without even hearing them out?

881
00:36:09,740 --> 00:36:12,510
Are we only here to start and win wars?

882
00:36:12,510 --> 00:36:14,740
That thought crossed my mind.

883
00:36:14,740 --> 00:36:16,080
Given our position,

884
00:36:16,080 --> 00:36:18,610
we can go with gold if it benefits us,

885
00:36:18,610 --> 00:36:21,010
or pick diamonds
if that turns out to be better.

886
00:36:21,010 --> 00:36:23,220
The key factor for us
is what brings us the most benefit.

887
00:36:23,380 --> 00:36:25,380
The casting vote belongs...

888
00:36:25,780 --> 00:36:27,950
- Team Red.
- to Team Red. Why?

889
00:36:27,950 --> 00:36:29,420
Black and White...

890
00:36:29,420 --> 00:36:30,820
favor diamonds.

891
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:32,220
There's no other choice for us.

892
00:36:32,220 --> 00:36:34,830
You're right. It's 5 versus 3.

893
00:36:34,830 --> 00:36:36,860
- They hold the power.
- These three have the casting vote.

894
00:36:36,860 --> 00:36:39,100
Wait, why aren't you considering me?

895
00:36:39,270 --> 00:36:40,370
Hold on a second.

896
00:36:40,570 --> 00:36:42,100
- These 4.
- Yes, us 4.

897
00:36:42,100 --> 00:36:43,900
- It's four of them.
- Right.

898
00:36:43,900 --> 00:36:45,170
That being said...

899
00:36:46,310 --> 00:36:47,740
Team Blue will head over...

900
00:36:47,740 --> 00:36:49,610
- to the Community Center...
- Me?

901
00:36:49,610 --> 00:36:52,210
- Team Blue. Blue?
- to participate in the Gold Rush.

902
00:36:52,340 --> 00:36:55,380
(Luna explained how the members
of Team Blue were eliminated.)

903
00:36:55,610 --> 00:36:58,120
This might be hard for you to understand,

904
00:36:58,120 --> 00:36:59,820
but the choice was impulsive.

905
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:01,720
Pitou made the decision...

906
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:02,890
to save only herself.

907
00:37:03,090 --> 00:37:05,520
(Pitou designated herself
as the sole survivor on Team Blue.)

908
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:08,090
(She doesn't seem like
a trustworthy ally to have.)

909
00:37:08,190 --> 00:37:09,200
We should hear her out.

910
00:37:09,200 --> 00:37:11,300
Is she the strong-willed
and opinionated one?

911
00:37:11,300 --> 00:37:12,400
- Who?
- Team Blue's...

912
00:37:12,400 --> 00:37:14,630
- No, she was the youngest member.
- Right?

913
00:37:14,630 --> 00:37:16,140
- The sole survivor.
- The sole survivor.

914
00:37:16,140 --> 00:37:17,840
When she arrives,

915
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:19,440
let's show empathy
for how hard her journey has been,

916
00:37:19,440 --> 00:37:20,940
- telling her that everything is fine now,
- You're right.

917
00:37:20,940 --> 00:37:22,470
and she can make a comeback
by joining forces with us.

918
00:37:22,470 --> 00:37:24,180
- We need to say that.
- Yes, that's necessary.

919
00:37:25,140 --> 00:37:27,050
- So...
- Wait, what was that again?

920
00:37:27,150 --> 00:37:30,320
Isn't the Platform operational again?

921
00:37:30,320 --> 00:37:31,980
Yes, trades can be made.

922
00:37:31,980 --> 00:37:33,220
- I can trade...
- Just so that...

923
00:37:33,220 --> 00:37:34,690
I can protect the team with diamonds,

924
00:37:34,690 --> 00:37:36,520
I can't give you any lives.

925
00:37:38,420 --> 00:37:39,630
She doesn't need any more lives.

926
00:37:39,630 --> 00:37:40,690
We gave you those to keep safe for us.

927
00:37:40,690 --> 00:37:42,030
- Hold on.
- Is that so?

928
00:37:42,030 --> 00:37:43,100
That's wrong.

929
00:37:43,100 --> 00:37:45,100
Please consider yielding
for the benefit of our community.

930
00:37:45,100 --> 00:37:46,230
If he was really
just holding onto them for you,

931
00:37:46,230 --> 00:37:48,200
your teammates
wouldn't have gotten eliminated yesterday.

932
00:37:48,200 --> 00:37:49,200
- That's right.
- Right?

933
00:37:49,300 --> 00:37:52,000
- That part of the rule is a bit strange.
- I told you this morning.

934
00:37:52,040 --> 00:37:53,710
No one is just holding onto that for you.

935
00:37:54,040 --> 00:37:56,110
- The same thing happened to us.
- We gave him our credit to hold onto.

936
00:37:56,110 --> 00:37:57,440
- We asked him to hold onto our credit.
- He just took it for himself.

937
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:58,540
- Exactly.
- That concept doesn't exist.

938
00:37:58,540 --> 00:38:00,650
To be honest, it stung a little.

939
00:38:00,650 --> 00:38:02,680
What everyone needed from me...

940
00:38:02,680 --> 00:38:04,350
were lives,

941
00:38:04,350 --> 00:38:06,350
but instead of having them in my hands,

942
00:38:06,350 --> 00:38:08,050
I had someone else hold onto them.

943
00:38:08,050 --> 00:38:10,190
I would've felt more secure...

944
00:38:10,190 --> 00:38:13,590
keeping some of it as insurance,

945
00:38:13,590 --> 00:38:16,560
but Black said he couldn't return
any of it.

946
00:38:16,660 --> 00:38:18,200
My emotions got the better of me,

947
00:38:18,200 --> 00:38:21,900
and I couldn't help wondering
why he'd do that to me.

948
00:38:22,030 --> 00:38:24,900
- I'm thinking of the team.
- That's right.

949
00:38:24,900 --> 00:38:26,810
I'm sorry about all this.

950
00:38:26,810 --> 00:38:28,640
- Sure. Anyway, I'll get going.
- I'm really sorry.

951
00:38:28,910 --> 00:38:31,080
- Take your resource bag with you.
- It's fine.

952
00:38:31,080 --> 00:38:32,480
- It's fine.
- Take your bag.

953
00:38:32,480 --> 00:38:34,050
- It's fine.
- I'm really sorry.

954
00:38:35,050 --> 00:38:36,850
But I don't have a choice.

955
00:38:41,520 --> 00:38:44,090
Let's try appealing to her emotions first.

956
00:38:44,090 --> 00:38:45,120
You're right.

957
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:48,390
- She's here.
- Hello.

958
00:38:48,630 --> 00:38:50,630
- Hi.
- Hi.

959
00:38:50,630 --> 00:38:52,330
- Goodness, hello.
- Hi.

960
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:53,500
Hello.

961
00:38:55,300 --> 00:38:56,840
It was a rough night, wasn't it?

962
00:38:56,840 --> 00:38:59,170
- It was, and I'm here all alone.
- Oh, dear.

963
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:02,810
We heard you were
Team Blue's sole survivor.

964
00:39:02,810 --> 00:39:04,280
- Right.
- Things must be tough.

965
00:39:04,440 --> 00:39:05,440
It is.

966
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:07,710
On top of that, you're the youngest here.

967
00:39:07,710 --> 00:39:08,750
The baby sister.

968
00:39:08,750 --> 00:39:10,520
Yes, I probably am.

969
00:39:10,520 --> 00:39:11,680
Right, so...

970
00:39:11,680 --> 00:39:16,060
Anyway, we're here to reform...

971
00:39:16,060 --> 00:39:17,760
the existing currency system.

972
00:39:17,990 --> 00:39:19,890
Since we really...

973
00:39:19,890 --> 00:39:24,260
want you to side with us,

974
00:39:24,260 --> 00:39:27,800
we'd like to trade our gold with you.

975
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:30,170
We need diamonds anyway,

976
00:39:30,170 --> 00:39:32,400
so we'd like to swap our gold
for your diamonds.

977
00:39:33,110 --> 00:39:35,410
If gold becomes...

978
00:39:35,410 --> 00:39:37,140
the main currency,

979
00:39:37,140 --> 00:39:39,480
those diamonds you have will be worthless.

980
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:41,750
And because of us,

981
00:39:41,750 --> 00:39:43,980
Team Red's credits will go up in value,

982
00:39:44,120 --> 00:39:46,320
so there's a strong chance we'll team up.

983
00:39:46,490 --> 00:39:48,250
I'm aware of the situation.

984
00:39:48,250 --> 00:39:51,320
Those four over there are strong allies,

985
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:53,290
and the five of you are a complete team.

986
00:39:53,290 --> 00:39:58,030
That means only Team Red and I
are really in a position to flip.

987
00:39:58,200 --> 00:40:01,030
That's why I'm still debating it.

988
00:40:01,030 --> 00:40:03,300
My position basically forces me...

989
00:40:03,300 --> 00:40:05,040
to side with Red every time.

990
00:40:05,040 --> 00:40:08,970
Earlier, I noticed Black
and Team White doing...

991
00:40:08,970 --> 00:40:11,480
a lot of the talking.

992
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:13,910
They'll probably do whatever they can...

993
00:40:13,910 --> 00:40:16,720
to get you on their side.

994
00:40:17,050 --> 00:40:18,120
However,

995
00:40:18,120 --> 00:40:20,290
from what I can tell,

996
00:40:20,550 --> 00:40:23,320
the reason you lost your teammates is...

997
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:26,490
because you were egged on
by the people around you.

998
00:40:26,490 --> 00:40:27,590
- To be honest.
- Right.

999
00:40:27,890 --> 00:40:30,960
You were heavily influenced
by those around you...

1000
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:32,660
and were fooled.

1001
00:40:35,130 --> 00:40:36,600
Even now,

1002
00:40:36,740 --> 00:40:39,810
with no one left to lean on,

1003
00:40:39,810 --> 00:40:42,610
you seem to be
in a very vulnerable position.

1004
00:40:43,180 --> 00:40:44,780
So rather than that,

1005
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:48,250
- You should be more independent.
- you should think for yourself.

1006
00:40:48,250 --> 00:40:50,550
I believe that's best for you as well.

1007
00:40:50,550 --> 00:40:51,650
In my opinion,

1008
00:40:51,650 --> 00:40:53,950
- you don't have to think about others.
- Not at all.

1009
00:40:53,950 --> 00:40:56,120
- Just hold onto both options.
- You should have both...

1010
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:58,020
and benefit from whichever becomes...

1011
00:40:58,020 --> 00:40:59,630
- the currency.
- That's right.

1012
00:40:59,630 --> 00:41:02,390
That voting right is yours to exercise
at the last second.

1013
00:41:02,390 --> 00:41:03,700
- Right, but...
- It's best to hold onto them.

1014
00:41:03,700 --> 00:41:05,360
I understand the situation,

1015
00:41:05,360 --> 00:41:07,700
but you should know...

1016
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:11,140
I don't own a lot of diamonds right now.

1017
00:41:11,170 --> 00:41:14,870
I had someone hold onto my team's lives,

1018
00:41:15,140 --> 00:41:17,840
but he just told me...

1019
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:19,040
he couldn't return them.

1020
00:41:19,040 --> 00:41:20,810
You don't need lives
if you're the sole survivor.

1021
00:41:20,810 --> 00:41:23,120
- I don't, but...
- She needs them to trade.

1022
00:41:23,120 --> 00:41:24,850
- For trading.
- You need to earn gold or diamonds,

1023
00:41:24,850 --> 00:41:27,090
but you no longer have anything
to trade with.

1024
00:41:27,090 --> 00:41:28,190
- Right.
- That's why...

1025
00:41:28,190 --> 00:41:31,320
you should team up with us
and just earn gold.

1026
00:41:31,320 --> 00:41:33,590
We have credits as well,

1027
00:41:33,590 --> 00:41:35,890
so you can get those from us tomorrow.

1028
00:41:35,890 --> 00:41:38,030
Like I said, I came here
while their conversation...

1029
00:41:38,030 --> 00:41:39,630
- was still going on.
- Right.

1030
00:41:39,630 --> 00:41:41,900
It's not like I want to hear
what they have to say.

1031
00:41:42,230 --> 00:41:43,670
It's simply that...

1032
00:41:43,670 --> 00:41:45,970
I have nothing left after giving up 14...

1033
00:41:45,970 --> 00:41:47,370
of our team's lives.

1034
00:41:48,740 --> 00:41:50,040
You let him hold onto 14 lives?

1035
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:52,010
- Why did you do that?
- Yes, that's the case.

1036
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:54,710
I'm being transparent here
because I thought I should be.

1037
00:41:54,710 --> 00:41:56,450
- I...
- Why did you hand them over?

1038
00:41:56,450 --> 00:41:57,750
Probably to declare war.

1039
00:41:57,750 --> 00:42:00,390
- You were worried about losing them.
- Yes.

1040
00:42:00,450 --> 00:42:02,250
But he betrayed you.

1041
00:42:02,290 --> 00:42:03,920
- Fourteen...
- Yes, that's how it is.

1042
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:05,920
- You shouldn't trade with them anymore.
- Fourteen.

1043
00:42:05,920 --> 00:42:07,390
- No wonder Black said he had a lot.
- You can...

1044
00:42:07,390 --> 00:42:08,990
be fooled once.

1045
00:42:08,990 --> 00:42:11,000
But only a fool gets tricked twice.

1046
00:42:13,270 --> 00:42:15,800
- I still think I need...
- Fourteen lives?

1047
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:17,700
- to think about this.
- Hold on.

1048
00:42:17,700 --> 00:42:19,100
What we can offer is...

1049
00:42:20,870 --> 00:42:24,040
I assumed it was around 7 or 8 lives,

1050
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:26,140
but it turns out Team Blue had 14.

1051
00:42:26,140 --> 00:42:27,380
(Luna, Influencer)

1052
00:42:27,380 --> 00:42:29,010
Hearing that made me furious...

1053
00:42:29,010 --> 00:42:31,680
as someone who used to be on Team White.

1054
00:42:32,050 --> 00:42:33,520
It's in the past,

1055
00:42:33,520 --> 00:42:35,490
and I'm not even on Team White anymore,

1056
00:42:35,850 --> 00:42:38,520
but it was still just wrong.

1057
00:42:38,620 --> 00:42:42,260
I could really picture how furious
Genie and Salt must've been.

1058
00:42:42,260 --> 00:42:45,330
They were sitting on enough lives
to easily last a few days.

1059
00:42:45,460 --> 00:42:47,530
I was slightly impressed...

1060
00:42:47,530 --> 00:42:49,970
they didn't bother to use those lives.

1061
00:42:50,700 --> 00:42:52,870
- You can come back to talk, right?
- Right.

1062
00:42:52,870 --> 00:42:53,910
Then,

1063
00:42:53,910 --> 00:42:55,440
- why don't you sit on it?
- Yes.

1064
00:42:55,440 --> 00:42:58,280
I hope you take that time...

1065
00:42:58,280 --> 00:43:02,750
to really think about
what you're actually doing here.

1066
00:43:02,750 --> 00:43:04,280
If I may speak...

1067
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:06,490
We still have several days left.

1068
00:43:06,490 --> 00:43:09,620
Are you making decisions
based on what others think?

1069
00:43:09,620 --> 00:43:11,520
From my perspective,

1070
00:43:11,520 --> 00:43:13,290
holding both gold and diamonds...

1071
00:43:13,290 --> 00:43:14,630
is the smartest move,

1072
00:43:14,630 --> 00:43:17,160
- Yes, I agree.
- so aiming for that...

1073
00:43:17,160 --> 00:43:19,400
will prove how clever you are.

1074
00:43:20,600 --> 00:43:22,200
Right now,

1075
00:43:22,200 --> 00:43:24,200
I'm not thinking about who to side with.

1076
00:43:24,200 --> 00:43:26,100
- You're not siding with anyone.
- It's not that.

1077
00:43:26,100 --> 00:43:27,770
- Think for yourself.
- Instead of leaving with nothing,

1078
00:43:27,770 --> 00:43:29,710
you should consider the expected value...

1079
00:43:29,710 --> 00:43:30,710
- even if it's not much.
- Hold on.

1080
00:43:30,710 --> 00:43:32,380
The five of us are ganging up on her.

1081
00:43:32,380 --> 00:43:33,850
- I know.
- We can stop talking now.

1082
00:43:33,850 --> 00:43:35,680
She's heard everything she needs to.

1083
00:43:35,680 --> 00:43:37,880
Please don't fall for their gaslighting.

1084
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:39,920
All we're saying is that
you should diversify.

1085
00:43:40,720 --> 00:43:41,850
I see. Got it.

1086
00:43:41,850 --> 00:43:43,620
- Sure.
- Right, please think about it.

1087
00:43:45,390 --> 00:43:46,690
She wanted to get away from us.

1088
00:43:52,330 --> 00:43:53,770
I think we made her mad.

1089
00:43:53,770 --> 00:43:54,900
- We didn't.
- Is it okay?

1090
00:43:54,900 --> 00:43:55,900
Yes.

1091
00:44:02,410 --> 00:44:04,440
(Unbelievable...)

1092
00:44:04,440 --> 00:44:05,910
(Sighing)

1093
00:44:06,810 --> 00:44:09,250
- Getting Red on our side is key.
- Right.

1094
00:44:09,250 --> 00:44:10,850
With just Team Red alone,

1095
00:44:10,850 --> 00:44:12,420
we'll win with seven people.

1096
00:44:12,420 --> 00:44:13,550
Then,

1097
00:44:13,720 --> 00:44:15,150
if Team White agrees,

1098
00:44:15,350 --> 00:44:16,620
I'll give them ten lives.

1099
00:44:16,920 --> 00:44:18,820
I should get Blue's consent,
which I feel guilty about,

1100
00:44:18,820 --> 00:44:20,430
but I can give them that.

1101
00:44:20,430 --> 00:44:21,890
You must know...

1102
00:44:21,890 --> 00:44:24,560
Team Red isn't facing any real threat
at this stage.

1103
00:44:24,700 --> 00:44:26,000
- Yes.
- Good.

1104
00:44:26,100 --> 00:44:28,130
That's what scares me.

1105
00:44:28,170 --> 00:44:29,230
- What do you mean?
- I see.

1106
00:44:29,230 --> 00:44:31,240
- You scare me.
- But if we don't trust Team Red...

1107
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:32,300
We're low on lives,

1108
00:44:32,300 --> 00:44:34,110
yet we're blowing...

1109
00:44:34,110 --> 00:44:35,670
four days' worth on Team Red...

1110
00:44:35,670 --> 00:44:37,240
- at this very moment.
- Right.

1111
00:44:37,240 --> 00:44:38,280
That scares me.

1112
00:44:38,280 --> 00:44:39,480
If we could think about this some more...

1113
00:44:39,480 --> 00:44:42,080
Are you worried
that we'll end up choosing gold?

1114
00:44:42,080 --> 00:44:43,350
- Or...
- That or...

1115
00:44:43,350 --> 00:44:45,320
If you're going to say that...

1116
00:44:45,320 --> 00:44:47,020
and keep doubting us,

1117
00:44:47,020 --> 00:44:48,820
there's not much more we can say.

1118
00:44:51,120 --> 00:44:54,230
Team Red will head over
to the Community Center...

1119
00:44:54,230 --> 00:44:56,130
- Then...
- to participate in the Gold Rush.

1120
00:44:56,130 --> 00:44:58,900
- Let's head out for now.
- Can't you trade credits before you go?

1121
00:44:58,900 --> 00:45:00,830
- Sure.
- Once you get back,

1122
00:45:00,830 --> 00:45:01,970
buy all the lives.

1123
00:45:01,970 --> 00:45:03,740
Let's hear Blue out first.

1124
00:45:03,740 --> 00:45:05,840
- Sure.
- They talked, right?

1125
00:45:06,340 --> 00:45:07,410
What's that face?

1126
00:45:07,410 --> 00:45:09,010
What's going on?

1127
00:45:09,910 --> 00:45:11,080
We need to get going.

1128
00:45:11,080 --> 00:45:12,110
- Right.
- We need to get going.

1129
00:45:12,110 --> 00:45:14,510
- You guys should talk.
- I was told to talk to you first.

1130
00:45:14,510 --> 00:45:15,550
Really?

1131
00:45:15,550 --> 00:45:17,180
- Red and Blue?
- Just us? Sure thing.

1132
00:45:17,180 --> 00:45:18,850
If something like this keeps happening,

1133
00:45:18,850 --> 00:45:20,890
- it'll be tough on us.
- We should be allowed to talk.

1134
00:45:20,890 --> 00:45:22,020
This...

1135
00:45:22,020 --> 00:45:23,520
is inevitable...

1136
00:45:23,520 --> 00:45:24,520
It's necessary.

1137
00:45:24,520 --> 00:45:25,690
given the current state of the game.

1138
00:45:25,690 --> 00:45:26,730
That's true,

1139
00:45:26,730 --> 00:45:29,130
but when more things happen
without being shared with us,

1140
00:45:29,130 --> 00:45:31,060
our anxiety just keeps growing.

1141
00:45:31,360 --> 00:45:33,200
It's not about sharing things.

1142
00:45:33,200 --> 00:45:36,470
We also need to get
our thoughts together as well.

1143
00:45:36,470 --> 00:45:38,100
- I mean...
- It's okay, Leia.

1144
00:45:38,100 --> 00:45:39,470
What I'm saying is,
when you talk with us...

1145
00:45:39,470 --> 00:45:41,570
and then have separate conversations
without us,

1146
00:45:41,570 --> 00:45:42,740
it leaves us feeling anxious.

1147
00:45:42,740 --> 00:45:43,780
It makes us anxious,

1148
00:45:43,780 --> 00:45:44,880
- but it can't be helped.
- No, wait.

1149
00:45:44,880 --> 00:45:46,850
But you can't stop it from happening.

1150
00:45:46,850 --> 00:45:49,680
- This isn't about me.
- We can't control that.

1151
00:45:49,680 --> 00:45:54,520
I don't think it would be respectful
to Team Gold.

1152
00:45:54,520 --> 00:45:55,950
- They're...
- I don't think...

1153
00:45:55,950 --> 00:45:58,090
you're in a situation
to be talking about respect.

1154
00:45:58,420 --> 00:46:00,090
But if we force this on them,

1155
00:46:00,090 --> 00:46:01,830
we could all end up with hurt feelings.

1156
00:46:01,830 --> 00:46:03,530
We're not forcing them.

1157
00:46:03,530 --> 00:46:05,600
I'm saying this because
I think that's how...

1158
00:46:05,600 --> 00:46:06,730
- we can build trust.
- First...

1159
00:46:06,730 --> 00:46:08,330
Would you like to head over first?

1160
00:46:08,330 --> 00:46:09,900
We have to go quickly.

1161
00:46:09,900 --> 00:46:11,500
- Please wait a moment.
- They can go and come back.

1162
00:46:11,500 --> 00:46:13,770
- Just trust us this once.
- Okay.

1163
00:46:15,310 --> 00:46:17,080
How are things going?

1164
00:46:17,080 --> 00:46:20,080
Was there anything discussed
while I was gone?

1165
00:46:20,080 --> 00:46:22,180
Let me be honest with you.
It's about the lives.

1166
00:46:22,180 --> 00:46:24,020
- We wanted more lives.
- We asked that we get...

1167
00:46:24,020 --> 00:46:25,420
the lives instead of Team White.

1168
00:46:25,420 --> 00:46:26,920
- Almost...
- We asked for enough lives...

1169
00:46:26,920 --> 00:46:28,450
to last us through the rest of the game.

1170
00:46:28,450 --> 00:46:29,450
- Yes.
- That's all.

1171
00:46:29,760 --> 00:46:31,620
- Are those three talking?
- Yes.

1172
00:46:31,620 --> 00:46:33,330
Since they keep going off
to talk among themselves...

1173
00:46:33,690 --> 00:46:35,790
- But they have to do that...
- That's how they should do it.

1174
00:46:35,790 --> 00:46:37,360
because if we stop them from talking,

1175
00:46:37,360 --> 00:46:39,200
they'll just do things
because they feel offended.

1176
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:42,370
Leia felt very anxious...

1177
00:46:42,370 --> 00:46:44,340
because she was our team leader...

1178
00:46:44,340 --> 00:46:46,510
and she didn't want to lose
any more members.

1179
00:46:46,510 --> 00:46:48,370
She really cares a lot about that.

1180
00:46:48,370 --> 00:46:50,680
I totally understand her,

1181
00:46:51,140 --> 00:46:52,610
but we must admit...

1182
00:46:52,610 --> 00:46:56,450
that we don't have the leverage
to influence Team Red.

1183
00:46:56,720 --> 00:46:58,450
Can we go get them?

1184
00:46:58,450 --> 00:46:59,550
Did they just leave?

1185
00:46:59,820 --> 00:47:01,390
Seeing them act like that...

1186
00:47:01,390 --> 00:47:03,720
makes me nervous
about handing over all 12 lives.

1187
00:47:03,720 --> 00:47:05,720
I know it's the only strategy,

1188
00:47:05,720 --> 00:47:07,290
but are we really going to
hand over everything...

1189
00:47:07,290 --> 00:47:09,490
and put our entire fate on the line?

1190
00:47:10,160 --> 00:47:12,400
The structure remains the same for me.

1191
00:47:12,400 --> 00:47:15,070
- But certainly...
- My goal right now...

1192
00:47:15,070 --> 00:47:16,940
is to take advantage of all this chaos
and make sure...

1193
00:47:16,940 --> 00:47:17,940
- we get some lives today.
- That's right.

1194
00:47:17,940 --> 00:47:20,770
- That's right.
- I thought you were a negotiation genius.

1195
00:47:20,770 --> 00:47:23,180
You just called four dollars here.

1196
00:47:23,580 --> 00:47:25,410
- Four dollars.
- Four dollars.

1197
00:47:25,810 --> 00:47:27,110
How did the conversations go?

1198
00:47:27,110 --> 00:47:29,680
Did you come
to an agreement with Team Red?

1199
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:30,680
If we guarantee Team Red...

1200
00:47:30,680 --> 00:47:34,050
enough lives to last until the end,

1201
00:47:34,050 --> 00:47:36,120
they'll support the diamond team.

1202
00:47:39,220 --> 00:47:41,390
Even if I join them,
it's still 6 against 7, right?

1203
00:47:41,390 --> 00:47:42,390
That's right.

1204
00:47:45,730 --> 00:47:47,730
Of course, Team Red matters the most,

1205
00:47:47,730 --> 00:47:49,870
but if you join us,

1206
00:47:50,170 --> 00:47:52,470
we're overwhelmingly ahead in numbers.

1207
00:47:52,470 --> 00:47:53,740
You don't die anyway.

1208
00:47:54,110 --> 00:47:56,440
The only variable for you
is the prize money.

1209
00:47:56,440 --> 00:47:58,980
Since that's the only thing,
it's better to have the prize money.

1210
00:47:58,980 --> 00:48:03,420
I know I'd benefit from siding
with the bigger team,

1211
00:48:03,420 --> 00:48:05,620
but honestly, whether I side
with them or side with you,

1212
00:48:05,620 --> 00:48:08,520
it doesn't really decide who wins.

1213
00:48:08,520 --> 00:48:10,220
So basically, it's just about
whether you make nothing...

1214
00:48:10,220 --> 00:48:11,620
or at least make some money.

1215
00:48:11,620 --> 00:48:13,490
That's the only difference.

1216
00:48:13,490 --> 00:48:15,790
What I'm upset about is that...

1217
00:48:15,790 --> 00:48:18,700
you don't really care
about the trust with me.

1218
00:48:18,700 --> 00:48:20,270
Let me tell you about that.

1219
00:48:20,270 --> 00:48:22,200
We haven't made any trades yet.

1220
00:48:22,200 --> 00:48:24,740
Honestly, we could have excluded you
if we wanted to.

1221
00:48:24,740 --> 00:48:26,970
But we said that wouldn't be
the right thing to do...

1222
00:48:26,970 --> 00:48:28,910
- and...
- That's why we waited.

1223
00:48:28,910 --> 00:48:30,480
I said I can't give it out
without Blue's consent.

1224
00:48:30,480 --> 00:48:31,880
That's right. That's why...

1225
00:48:31,880 --> 00:48:34,110
we waited thinking
it was the right thing to do.

1226
00:48:34,110 --> 00:48:35,750
- We'll keep giving you credits...
- Yes.

1227
00:48:35,750 --> 00:48:37,520
- and diamonds.
- We'll also give you diamonds.

1228
00:48:37,520 --> 00:48:38,950
We'll take inflation into account,

1229
00:48:38,950 --> 00:48:40,890
and I'll even give you my share.

1230
00:48:40,890 --> 00:48:42,990
Right. You could even enjoy the game.
So...

1231
00:48:42,990 --> 00:48:45,720
- What we talked about in the morning...
- Blue...

1232
00:48:45,720 --> 00:48:48,290
was that if the supermarket
didn't give out enough food,

1233
00:48:48,290 --> 00:48:50,230
- we were going to spend our resources.
- Right.

1234
00:48:50,230 --> 00:48:52,660
We even said we should get
some food and take care of you.

1235
00:48:52,660 --> 00:48:54,570
Don't cry. Take a seat here.

1236
00:48:54,570 --> 00:48:56,300
- Take a seat.
- I'm just...

1237
00:48:56,770 --> 00:48:59,540
having a hard time today...

1238
00:48:59,540 --> 00:49:00,710
You felt upset. I get that.

1239
00:49:00,710 --> 00:49:02,710
- Come here.
- Before I left,

1240
00:49:02,710 --> 00:49:04,180
you kept saying you couldn't give me
any lives,

1241
00:49:04,180 --> 00:49:06,750
so I went there
and came back empty-handed.

1242
00:49:06,750 --> 00:49:09,810
But over there, they were telling me,

1243
00:49:09,810 --> 00:49:11,980
"You need to be a woman who takes charge."

1244
00:49:12,750 --> 00:49:14,050
That's all they can say.

1245
00:49:14,050 --> 00:49:15,120
That's right. Goodness.

1246
00:49:15,120 --> 00:49:16,120
I'm sorry.

1247
00:49:16,450 --> 00:49:17,820
It's not that we can't give you lives.

1248
00:49:17,820 --> 00:49:19,290
For the sake of our team...

1249
00:49:19,490 --> 00:49:22,630
- For the sake of our team...
- I don't need lives anyway.

1250
00:49:22,630 --> 00:49:24,200
That doesn't matter.

1251
00:49:24,200 --> 00:49:25,660
Since it's come to the point...

1252
00:49:25,660 --> 00:49:28,670
where I'd have nothing to say
even if you excluded me,

1253
00:49:28,800 --> 00:49:30,640
- I was scared...
- No.

1254
00:49:30,640 --> 00:49:33,070
That's why I said I just wanted
to have something.

1255
00:49:33,070 --> 00:49:35,710
But when I went to them,

1256
00:49:36,840 --> 00:49:39,140
they said, "You need to make
your own choice."

1257
00:49:39,140 --> 00:49:41,650
"Getting fooled twice would be stupid."

1258
00:49:41,650 --> 00:49:43,980
When they said that, I got scared
because I started wondering...

1259
00:49:43,980 --> 00:49:46,050
- if I was actually being stupid.
- That's not true.

1260
00:49:46,820 --> 00:49:49,250
- I was scared.
- You had no one to talk to as well.

1261
00:49:49,250 --> 00:49:51,290
- I had no one to talk to.
- That's right.

1262
00:49:51,790 --> 00:49:55,490
I want you to stop blaming yourself...

1263
00:49:55,490 --> 00:49:57,160
for what you've done up until yesterday.

1264
00:49:57,160 --> 00:50:01,000
It's true that we can't completely
trust you in the current situation.

1265
00:50:01,000 --> 00:50:03,200
But we need you,

1266
00:50:03,440 --> 00:50:05,800
and you can't be on your own either.

1267
00:50:05,800 --> 00:50:08,440
What we were always trying to do
was to find a way for everyone to benefit.

1268
00:50:09,110 --> 00:50:10,810
You have to trust us as well.

1269
00:50:11,080 --> 00:50:13,450
I think the past matters
when it comes to trust,

1270
00:50:13,450 --> 00:50:14,450
but once you've decided to trust someone,

1271
00:50:14,450 --> 00:50:16,650
you have to go on with that.

1272
00:50:17,550 --> 00:50:20,750
We hope you could choose...

1273
00:50:21,150 --> 00:50:23,990
to share some of what was yours with us.

1274
00:50:24,290 --> 00:50:28,030
And of course, we'll give you something
in return.

1275
00:50:28,030 --> 00:50:31,400
I think that would be
our first interaction.

1276
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:35,130
So giving us lives...

1277
00:50:35,130 --> 00:50:36,970
also means...

1278
00:50:37,270 --> 00:50:41,010
guaranteeing that you won't trade
with Gold.

1279
00:50:41,140 --> 00:50:43,010
Just know that it would be safer
for everyone...

1280
00:50:43,010 --> 00:50:45,610
if I kept the lives,

1281
00:50:45,610 --> 00:50:49,350
because it would prevent
any deal with Gold altogether.

1282
00:50:49,350 --> 00:50:51,320
But I'm okay with giving it all to you.

1283
00:50:53,590 --> 00:50:56,520
Maybe I trust Vector too much,

1284
00:50:56,520 --> 00:51:00,230
but I didn't think he would take it...

1285
00:51:00,330 --> 00:51:04,360
without a plan and just refuse
to give it back.

1286
00:51:04,730 --> 00:51:07,700
He must have had a plan,

1287
00:51:07,700 --> 00:51:10,700
and there would be a reason
why he couldn't explain it to us now.

1288
00:51:10,700 --> 00:51:15,640
So I think I just want
to keep things going the way they are.

1289
00:51:15,640 --> 00:51:18,710
I don't want to betray anyone anymore.

1290
00:51:21,380 --> 00:51:23,180
- There are chairs.
- This is cool.

1291
00:51:23,520 --> 00:51:25,050
- Hello.
- Hello.

1292
00:51:25,050 --> 00:51:26,580
- Hello.
- Hello.

1293
00:51:26,580 --> 00:51:28,890
- Nice to meet you.
- Sorry to keep you waiting.

1294
00:51:28,890 --> 00:51:29,890
It's okay.

1295
00:51:29,890 --> 00:51:33,530
(They're basically the only team
Team Gold can negotiate with.)

1296
00:51:33,730 --> 00:51:35,890
So, what should we talk about?

1297
00:51:35,890 --> 00:51:38,200
First, we'd like...

1298
00:51:38,200 --> 00:51:40,770
to be transparent with the gold pieces,

1299
00:51:40,770 --> 00:51:45,570
lay out the advantages of that, and have
a discussion about a possible deal.

1300
00:51:45,570 --> 00:51:48,240
We also wanted to hear your thoughts too.

1301
00:51:48,240 --> 00:51:51,210
There is one thing
we're a little concerned about.

1302
00:51:51,210 --> 00:51:52,840
We fully agree that, at this point,
gold is a currency...

1303
00:51:52,840 --> 00:51:56,780
people can trust
because of its limited issuance.

1304
00:51:56,780 --> 00:52:00,620
But does it have that much of a benefit?

1305
00:52:00,620 --> 00:52:03,320
Team Black and Team White
are fully on the same side now.

1306
00:52:03,320 --> 00:52:08,130
They're both parties that require us
to use diamonds as a currency.

1307
00:52:08,130 --> 00:52:10,200
If the four of them join forces and say,

1308
00:52:10,200 --> 00:52:13,400
"We'll reveal the amount issued,"

1309
00:52:13,400 --> 00:52:16,200
there's not much difference
between diamonds and gold...

1310
00:52:16,200 --> 00:52:17,700
when it comes to trust.

1311
00:52:17,700 --> 00:52:20,570
But Black has a supermarket.

1312
00:52:20,570 --> 00:52:22,270
He has a platform.

1313
00:52:22,270 --> 00:52:23,610
He gives us food.

1314
00:52:23,610 --> 00:52:24,840
What I'm most worried about is,

1315
00:52:24,840 --> 00:52:26,540
the five of you just got here,

1316
00:52:26,540 --> 00:52:27,850
and you must be hungry.

1317
00:52:27,850 --> 00:52:29,050
How are you going to eat?

1318
00:52:29,410 --> 00:52:30,750
From the same perspective,

1319
00:52:30,750 --> 00:52:34,520
if we choose to keep gold,

1320
00:52:34,520 --> 00:52:38,020
we need to coexist with those four,

1321
00:52:38,020 --> 00:52:40,130
or we'll have to starve starting tomorrow.

1322
00:52:40,130 --> 00:52:43,830
I'm really curious about the advantages
of having gold in such a situation.

1323
00:52:43,830 --> 00:52:47,230
That's something we'll have to work out
with Black.

1324
00:52:47,230 --> 00:52:49,170
From Team Red's perspective,

1325
00:52:49,170 --> 00:52:51,670
based on the amount of prize money
you could take home,

1326
00:52:51,670 --> 00:52:54,940
we can make it so that you'd get more
by choosing gold...

1327
00:52:54,940 --> 00:52:57,210
than you would by choosing diamonds.

1328
00:52:57,680 --> 00:52:59,740
I'm not sure.

1329
00:52:59,740 --> 00:53:02,980
I can't speak for the other members,

1330
00:53:03,180 --> 00:53:05,920
but rather than the amount of money
you just mentioned,

1331
00:53:05,920 --> 00:53:09,890
I think the priority should be
whether our survival is guaranteed.

1332
00:53:09,890 --> 00:53:10,890
That's because...

1333
00:53:11,120 --> 00:53:14,090
if we can't survive,
the currency has no value.

1334
00:53:14,730 --> 00:53:17,000
So what I'm wondering is...

1335
00:53:17,000 --> 00:53:18,800
whether the gold you have
will be enough...

1336
00:53:18,800 --> 00:53:21,870
to sustain all five of you
for the remaining days.

1337
00:53:21,870 --> 00:53:25,800
Even if just two people
drop out of Team Gold,

1338
00:53:25,800 --> 00:53:28,270
the people left here
wouldn't be enough to win.

1339
00:53:28,270 --> 00:53:31,610
So that's why I wanted
to be honest with you earlier...

1340
00:53:32,010 --> 00:53:34,510
that we don't want to give out
the information.

1341
00:53:34,510 --> 00:53:36,410
- Actually, I want the eight...
- That's...

1342
00:53:36,410 --> 00:53:37,520
Let's not talk about that now.

1343
00:53:37,520 --> 00:53:38,750
No, I think this is the right thing to do.

1344
00:53:38,750 --> 00:53:41,220
- They're really worried.
- No.

1345
00:53:41,220 --> 00:53:45,320
The information that we have
a lot of lives...

1346
00:53:45,320 --> 00:53:49,630
could give them a reason
to go to war with us.

1347
00:53:49,630 --> 00:53:52,960
It's one of the few pieces
of information that gives us an advantage.

1348
00:53:52,960 --> 00:53:56,230
So it's something we could talk about
in a more informal setting.

1349
00:53:56,230 --> 00:53:57,800
Luna is quick to make decisions.

1350
00:53:57,800 --> 00:53:59,670
Since she figured we'd make
the trade that day,

1351
00:53:59,670 --> 00:54:02,470
she wanted to be open about it
and tie us together as a team.

1352
00:54:02,470 --> 00:54:05,410
But since the trade
hasn't been finalized yet,

1353
00:54:05,410 --> 00:54:07,950
I don't think we should share
that information yet.

1354
00:54:07,950 --> 00:54:10,250
What if they're closer to that side,

1355
00:54:10,250 --> 00:54:11,450
and we just end up
having our information leaked out?

1356
00:54:11,450 --> 00:54:14,550
That means we'll be at war tomorrow.

1357
00:54:14,790 --> 00:54:16,250
- No.
- We...

1358
00:54:16,250 --> 00:54:17,820
We're...

1359
00:54:17,820 --> 00:54:21,490
not exactly affluent...

1360
00:54:21,890 --> 00:54:23,290
when it comes to lives and survival,

1361
00:54:23,290 --> 00:54:25,060
but we're confident we can make it.

1362
00:54:25,060 --> 00:54:27,570
We have no intention
of using up Team Red's lives.

1363
00:54:27,570 --> 00:54:30,030
In fact, if we can,
you're the one we have to keep alive most.

1364
00:54:30,030 --> 00:54:32,340
You're the team we should
give lives to, even for free.

1365
00:54:32,340 --> 00:54:34,640
If I may explain,

1366
00:54:34,640 --> 00:54:36,040
that's only natural.

1367
00:54:36,040 --> 00:54:38,680
- They issue credits every day.
- Yes.

1368
00:54:38,680 --> 00:54:40,810
Then we need to make sure
they have enough lives.

1369
00:54:41,780 --> 00:54:44,120
We won't lose anyone...

1370
00:54:44,120 --> 00:54:45,720
- until the end.
- Right.

1371
00:54:45,720 --> 00:54:48,050
That means you started
with enough lives, right?

1372
00:54:48,050 --> 00:54:49,820
That's right. We won't run out of lives.

1373
00:54:49,820 --> 00:54:50,820
We plan to give you lives...

1374
00:54:50,820 --> 00:54:51,890
- Also,
- as soon as we get them.

1375
00:54:51,890 --> 00:54:53,320
- we need to put everything we can...
- We plan to give them to you.

1376
00:54:53,320 --> 00:54:55,090
into production and give you
all the lives...

1377
00:54:55,090 --> 00:54:56,390
- as soon as we get them.
- We'll give them all to you.

1378
00:54:56,390 --> 00:54:58,100
- Because the lives...
- That way, we're the larger team.

1379
00:54:58,100 --> 00:55:00,830
- Having more people...
- We have five members...

1380
00:55:00,830 --> 00:55:04,170
Yes, and for that,
we need lots of credits.

1381
00:55:04,470 --> 00:55:06,000
So all the lives we get...

1382
00:55:06,000 --> 00:55:08,970
We plan to give them to you for free.

1383
00:55:10,640 --> 00:55:13,040
Everyone's more of a talker...

1384
00:55:13,040 --> 00:55:14,410
than a listener.

1385
00:55:14,980 --> 00:55:16,310
That applies to me as well.

1386
00:55:16,310 --> 00:55:19,880
I'm a talker, not a listener.

1387
00:55:19,880 --> 00:55:22,650
I know
what they're really worried about...

1388
00:55:22,650 --> 00:55:24,720
and what they're asking.

1389
00:55:24,720 --> 00:55:27,390
So I wanted to hear what they wanted.

1390
00:55:27,390 --> 00:55:29,630
I wanted to know the conditions...

1391
00:55:29,630 --> 00:55:31,360
that would make them
switch over to our side.

1392
00:55:31,360 --> 00:55:33,400
That's what I wanted to talk about.

1393
00:55:33,400 --> 00:55:34,800
Honestly,

1394
00:55:34,800 --> 00:55:39,040
I think our members
kept repeating the same words.

1395
00:55:39,040 --> 00:55:40,740
I was a bit frustrated by that.

1396
00:55:40,940 --> 00:55:43,440
What was frustrating
to watch from the side was...

1397
00:55:43,440 --> 00:55:45,940
they kept trying to persuade them...

1398
00:55:45,940 --> 00:55:50,450
using the same logic
we discussed in our meeting room.

1399
00:55:50,850 --> 00:55:54,090
So I felt like we should've focused...

1400
00:55:54,090 --> 00:55:57,790
on understanding what they needed,

1401
00:55:57,790 --> 00:56:00,730
rather than pushing our proposal to them.

1402
00:56:00,730 --> 00:56:02,890
While all these things
were being brought up,

1403
00:56:02,890 --> 00:56:06,100
there was something
that kept bothering me.

1404
00:56:06,100 --> 00:56:08,130
I felt like...

1405
00:56:08,130 --> 00:56:09,500
there were a lot of comments that,

1406
00:56:09,500 --> 00:56:12,800
if I were the ones listening,
would make me feel offended enough...

1407
00:56:12,800 --> 00:56:16,970
that I wouldn't want to do the deal.

1408
00:56:16,970 --> 00:56:18,240
That troubled me.

1409
00:56:18,240 --> 00:56:20,950
It wouldn't matter if I was alone.

1410
00:56:20,950 --> 00:56:22,310
But since it's a team,

1411
00:56:23,050 --> 00:56:25,650
it's quite tough. I find it hard.

1412
00:56:26,220 --> 00:56:28,750
We were thinking that maybe...

1413
00:56:28,750 --> 00:56:31,320
we should take the gold we have now...

1414
00:56:31,320 --> 00:56:34,290
and distribute it as evenly as possible...

1415
00:56:34,290 --> 00:56:36,390
among the eight of us,
and look at the bigger picture.

1416
00:56:36,390 --> 00:56:38,000
- We've already settled that.
- All right.

1417
00:56:38,000 --> 00:56:39,500
Yes, we understood.

1418
00:56:40,100 --> 00:56:42,070
Do you perhaps have a code on the wall
in your dorm?

1419
00:56:42,770 --> 00:56:44,340
Have you been to the dormitory?

1420
00:56:44,570 --> 00:56:47,370
Should we talk once we form an alliance?

1421
00:56:47,370 --> 00:56:49,340
I'm the only one who knows everything.

1422
00:56:49,340 --> 00:56:51,710
Let's form an alliance and then talk,

1423
00:56:51,710 --> 00:56:52,740
since we're a team.

1424
00:56:52,740 --> 00:56:54,010
Okay. Sounds good.

1425
00:56:54,010 --> 00:56:55,980
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1426
00:56:55,980 --> 00:56:57,180
- Let's go.
- Okay.

1427
00:56:58,380 --> 00:56:59,520
I'm worried.

1428
00:57:02,450 --> 00:57:03,550
Things got troublesome.

1429
00:57:03,550 --> 00:57:05,720
Seriously. We have to decide everything.

1430
00:57:05,720 --> 00:57:08,490
- We just...
- Both sides want to help us out.

1431
00:57:08,490 --> 00:57:10,090
- We became the protectors of balance.
- Exactly.

1432
00:57:11,800 --> 00:57:13,330
For all four days,

1433
00:57:13,330 --> 00:57:15,630
we thought, "We have no rights."

1434
00:57:15,630 --> 00:57:18,040
"We don't have resources, like credits."

1435
00:57:18,040 --> 00:57:20,100
"The whole situation is bad for us."

1436
00:57:20,100 --> 00:57:21,570
We were complaining like that.

1437
00:57:21,740 --> 00:57:23,240
In one day,

1438
00:57:23,240 --> 00:57:25,810
Gold, White, and Black came to us.

1439
00:57:25,810 --> 00:57:28,080
They're all looking to us.
They're offering us everything.

1440
00:57:28,080 --> 00:57:31,380
Now we can weigh the two options...

1441
00:57:31,380 --> 00:57:33,990
and make them compete freely.

1442
00:57:33,990 --> 00:57:35,620
The pro-diamond people said...

1443
00:57:35,620 --> 00:57:38,890
they'd give us ten lives
if we joined their side.

1444
00:57:39,090 --> 00:57:42,330
If so, we can live comfortably
until the last day.

1445
00:57:42,330 --> 00:57:45,560
I do want to own some gold,

1446
00:57:45,560 --> 00:57:48,570
but if we take some gold,
it'll show up on Black's monitor, right?

1447
00:57:49,070 --> 00:57:50,800
Then we'll become traitors, right?

1448
00:57:51,370 --> 00:57:54,170
Until we get lives,

1449
00:57:54,170 --> 00:57:55,570
we can't get on anyone's wrong side.

1450
00:57:57,910 --> 00:57:59,540
You seem very conflicted.

1451
00:57:59,540 --> 00:58:01,010
Yes, I'm very tired.

1452
00:58:01,010 --> 00:58:02,650
The reason the discussion was long
is simple.

1453
00:58:02,650 --> 00:58:04,520
I asked a lot of useless questions.

1454
00:58:04,520 --> 00:58:06,320
"Does Team Yellow have the wall code?"

1455
00:58:06,320 --> 00:58:07,490
What did they say?

1456
00:58:07,490 --> 00:58:09,650
They didn't tell me.

1457
00:58:09,650 --> 00:58:11,420
Also...

1458
00:58:11,720 --> 00:58:13,220
- Anything else?
- What I was told...

1459
00:58:13,220 --> 00:58:15,790
They have no other choice.

1460
00:58:15,790 --> 00:58:17,200
In this game, they have to...

1461
00:58:17,200 --> 00:58:18,700
(Donkey quietly signals to Vector
to talk.)

1462
00:58:18,700 --> 00:58:20,100
Luna just has to make a decision.

1463
00:58:20,100 --> 00:58:22,700
Exactly. Once she decides...

1464
00:58:22,870 --> 00:58:24,770
I think they will definitely solve
the wall code.

1465
00:58:25,200 --> 00:58:27,240
Luna knows it.

1466
00:58:27,240 --> 00:58:30,540
She's saying she'll tell us
if we come on her side.

1467
00:58:31,180 --> 00:58:32,410
We have to say we won't team up with Luna.

1468
00:58:32,410 --> 00:58:34,850
But Maillard has been wanting...

1469
00:58:34,850 --> 00:58:36,680
to solve that from the beginning,

1470
00:58:36,680 --> 00:58:38,720
so I think he'll find it
even if he needs to trade for it.

1471
00:58:38,720 --> 00:58:39,750
He can't.

1472
00:58:39,750 --> 00:58:40,850
- Exactly.
- We have to stop him.

1473
00:58:41,250 --> 00:58:42,590
We'll lose 100,000 dollars.

1474
00:58:43,120 --> 00:58:44,490
- There is another way.
- Instead...

1475
00:58:44,620 --> 00:58:46,220
We could get rid of 100,000 dollars...

1476
00:58:46,520 --> 00:58:48,190
and keep starting wars again.

1477
00:58:49,330 --> 00:58:52,600
I want you to stop Maillard.

1478
00:58:52,660 --> 00:58:54,870
- From doing what?
- From joining that side.

1479
00:58:54,970 --> 00:58:57,030
I mean, it doesn't matter if we go.

1480
00:58:57,030 --> 00:58:58,870
I don't think he'll join that side.

1481
00:58:58,870 --> 00:59:00,270
It doesn't matter if he does.

1482
00:59:00,270 --> 00:59:02,240
It doesn't affect our prize at all.

1483
00:59:02,240 --> 00:59:04,210
- Diamonds don't mean anything.
- Right.

1484
00:59:04,210 --> 00:59:06,980
But it's not like they can
avoid trading forever.

1485
00:59:06,980 --> 00:59:09,850
- Right.
- They need some credits too.

1486
00:59:09,850 --> 00:59:12,050
We need to let White know...

1487
00:59:12,050 --> 00:59:14,620
that there will be some minimal trading.

1488
00:59:14,620 --> 00:59:17,090
If White doesn't acknowledge that,

1489
00:59:17,090 --> 00:59:19,220
declares us the enemy
as soon as we give them something,

1490
00:59:19,220 --> 00:59:22,590
talks to Black right away, and goes
into "Don't give them food" stance,

1491
00:59:22,730 --> 00:59:24,460
it would put us in a bit of a pickle.

1492
00:59:26,100 --> 00:59:27,700
If you take too firm of a stance,

1493
00:59:27,700 --> 00:59:30,430
- all they'll have left is war.
- Exactly.

1494
00:59:30,430 --> 00:59:32,740
There are still four days left.

1495
00:59:32,740 --> 00:59:34,710
Since we're prioritizing survival,

1496
00:59:34,710 --> 00:59:37,170
the biggest threat to us...

1497
00:59:37,170 --> 00:59:38,810
is Gold waging war against us.

1498
00:59:39,040 --> 00:59:41,080
- So I...
- Team White,

1499
00:59:41,080 --> 00:59:43,850
- head to the Community Center...
- I want to ask about that.

1500
00:59:43,850 --> 00:59:46,520
- and participate in the Gold Rush.
- We have a general picture now.

1501
00:59:46,820 --> 00:59:50,250
Would it be better for us to give them...

1502
00:59:50,250 --> 00:59:52,790
enough to eat, for ethical reasons?

1503
00:59:53,420 --> 00:59:54,790
Team White will probably be...

1504
00:59:54,790 --> 00:59:57,400
the most hostile toward us.

1505
00:59:57,400 --> 01:00:00,530
In my opinion,
we have to listen as much as possible.

1506
01:00:00,530 --> 01:00:01,530
Okay.

1507
01:00:01,530 --> 01:00:03,970
- Instead of talking...
- There's nothing we can do anyway.

1508
01:00:03,970 --> 01:00:05,900
- Shall we hear them out?
- If we take too firm of a stance,

1509
01:00:05,900 --> 01:00:07,540
it could make them more so.

1510
01:00:07,540 --> 01:00:09,440
- Hello.
- Hello.

1511
01:00:09,440 --> 01:00:10,640
Hello.

1512
01:00:10,640 --> 01:00:12,010
They're sitting in the center.

1513
01:00:12,380 --> 01:00:14,110
- Hello.
- You've been working hard.

1514
01:00:14,110 --> 01:00:15,180
Yes.

1515
01:00:16,650 --> 01:00:19,080
- Hi, Luna.
- Hello.

1516
01:00:19,080 --> 01:00:20,550
It feels like seeing an ex.

1517
01:00:21,550 --> 01:00:22,650
There's a special...

1518
01:00:22,650 --> 01:00:24,020
We had a good breakup.

1519
01:00:24,020 --> 01:00:25,320
- "A good breakup."
- Right.

1520
01:00:25,320 --> 01:00:27,590
We only have good memories of her.

1521
01:00:27,830 --> 01:00:28,830
Yes.

1522
01:00:28,830 --> 01:00:30,290
Today will feel like meeting...

1523
01:00:30,290 --> 01:00:33,160
- the parents for the first time.
- You're right.

1524
01:00:33,160 --> 01:00:35,070
So first,

1525
01:00:35,070 --> 01:00:38,540
there's nothing we particularly need
at the moment.

1526
01:00:38,540 --> 01:00:41,570
So we don't know if it'd be good...

1527
01:00:41,570 --> 01:00:44,340
to mix our currencies together...

1528
01:00:44,340 --> 01:00:47,480
when we don't know
what effect that'll have.

1529
01:00:47,480 --> 01:00:49,850
Anyway, we've decided together...

1530
01:00:49,850 --> 01:00:52,250
not to do any of that, right?

1531
01:00:52,250 --> 01:00:54,720
So, at least for today,

1532
01:00:54,720 --> 01:00:57,050
we'll buy your meal.

1533
01:00:57,360 --> 01:00:58,920
- What?
- Yes. So...

1534
01:00:58,920 --> 01:01:01,590
But we also don't want
to mix our currencies.

1535
01:01:01,590 --> 01:01:04,000
- We're worried about mixing credits...
- Yes.

1536
01:01:04,000 --> 01:01:06,200
- and diamonds.
- She's so cool.

1537
01:01:06,430 --> 01:01:08,970
With our diamonds,

1538
01:01:08,970 --> 01:01:11,040
we'll buy food you can buy.

1539
01:01:11,040 --> 01:01:13,700
We want to show you...

1540
01:01:13,700 --> 01:01:15,670
that we want to have...

1541
01:01:15,670 --> 01:01:18,340
civil discussions with you going forward.

1542
01:01:18,340 --> 01:01:20,040
Thank you so much.

1543
01:01:20,040 --> 01:01:23,350
Since Leader Leia here...

1544
01:01:23,350 --> 01:01:26,620
made a big decision for the greater good,

1545
01:01:26,620 --> 01:01:28,790
let's give her a round of applause
for her generosity.

1546
01:01:28,790 --> 01:01:29,890
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1547
01:01:29,890 --> 01:01:30,960
We like it.

1548
01:01:32,390 --> 01:01:34,530
She was so generous.

1549
01:01:34,530 --> 01:01:36,090
Honestly, I was quite surprised.

1550
01:01:36,090 --> 01:01:40,330
I felt she was a very gentle person.

1551
01:01:40,330 --> 01:01:42,470
I didn't want to play around with food.

1552
01:01:42,800 --> 01:01:44,570
It's only a fair competition...

1553
01:01:44,570 --> 01:01:46,640
when everyone is fed.

1554
01:01:46,640 --> 01:01:51,210
It's not cool to starve people.

1555
01:01:51,810 --> 01:01:54,050
And I don't think...

1556
01:01:54,410 --> 01:01:55,610
eating will greatly change...

1557
01:01:56,350 --> 01:01:58,250
their war power.

1558
01:01:59,220 --> 01:02:01,020
Let's do some business.

1559
01:02:01,750 --> 01:02:05,320
If we protect ourselves
and isolate the enemy,

1560
01:02:05,320 --> 01:02:07,320
we can win.

1561
01:02:07,320 --> 01:02:10,090
We have a winning strategy.

1562
01:02:10,090 --> 01:02:12,030
So I persuaded my team with the idea...

1563
01:02:12,030 --> 01:02:14,300
that we have to form an alliance.

1564
01:02:14,630 --> 01:02:16,270
And for that situation,

1565
01:02:16,630 --> 01:02:19,600
I needed some collateral
to keep this alliance together.

1566
01:02:20,100 --> 01:02:21,870
I'm saying we should just use all 400...

1567
01:02:21,870 --> 01:02:23,340
and give out 100 to each person.

1568
01:02:24,010 --> 01:02:26,280
They're going off of the assumption
that there'll be another issuance.

1569
01:02:26,280 --> 01:02:28,350
Even if there's another issuance,

1570
01:02:28,350 --> 01:02:30,920
though we don't have much today,

1571
01:02:30,920 --> 01:02:32,120
we'll keep going like that.

1572
01:02:32,450 --> 01:02:35,920
We first had
to divide up the diamonds evenly.

1573
01:02:36,250 --> 01:02:38,520
The real issue was lives.

1574
01:02:38,520 --> 01:02:41,390
We asked to receive right away
the number of lives...

1575
01:02:41,390 --> 01:02:43,530
required to survive until the last day.

1576
01:02:43,530 --> 01:02:46,800
Red did have reasons to break off...

1577
01:02:46,800 --> 01:02:48,570
and leave the alliance.

1578
01:02:48,570 --> 01:02:51,400
It really is an all-or-nothing gamble.

1579
01:02:52,270 --> 01:02:54,000
- Are you fine with giving out lives?
- Yes.

1580
01:02:54,000 --> 01:02:55,870
Okay, if so, here's ten for you.

1581
01:02:55,870 --> 01:02:57,070
(Black sold 10 lives to Team Red.)

1582
01:02:57,240 --> 01:02:59,910
Everyone has agreed...

1583
01:02:59,910 --> 01:03:03,610
to give Team Red 12 lives,
the number of lives they need...

1584
01:03:03,610 --> 01:03:06,080
to survive until the eighth day.

1585
01:03:06,220 --> 01:03:07,690
Give four to White as well?

1586
01:03:07,690 --> 01:03:09,090
- Four, right? Okay.
- Yes, go ahead.

1587
01:03:09,420 --> 01:03:11,920
We're finally all getting to enjoy
the bountiful resources.

1588
01:03:12,820 --> 01:03:13,920
This really isn't easy.

1589
01:03:14,330 --> 01:03:17,090
We've never had so much before.
I feel so anxious...

1590
01:03:17,800 --> 01:03:19,000
that someone will take it from us.

1591
01:03:20,200 --> 01:03:22,870
Until now, we've had so few resources.

1592
01:03:22,870 --> 01:03:25,870
Nobody bought our credits.
Nobody cared about us.

1593
01:03:26,200 --> 01:03:28,370
We finally acquired...

1594
01:03:28,370 --> 01:03:31,380
the most stable amount of resources
we've ever had.

1595
01:03:31,610 --> 01:03:35,510
We've never been treated like this
in the past four days.

1596
01:03:35,510 --> 01:03:38,120
We have never had more than 50 diamonds.

1597
01:03:38,120 --> 01:03:39,850
We're actually overwhelmed now.

1598
01:03:39,850 --> 01:03:42,590
Our storage is so full now.

1599
01:03:42,590 --> 01:03:44,520
Since we received ten lives today,

1600
01:03:44,520 --> 01:03:46,420
we have enough lives...

1601
01:03:46,420 --> 01:03:49,090
unless we lose in a war.

1602
01:03:49,090 --> 01:03:50,690
Considering the number of people,

1603
01:03:50,690 --> 01:03:53,400
there is a very high possibility...

1604
01:03:53,400 --> 01:03:55,300
that things will go the way we choose.

1605
01:03:55,300 --> 01:03:57,900
If Gold says to us,
"We'll give you most of our gold."

1606
01:03:57,900 --> 01:04:00,910
"With most of our gold,
you can expect much more...."

1607
01:04:00,910 --> 01:04:02,910
"than what you can get with diamonds,"

1608
01:04:03,570 --> 01:04:05,740
we really don't have a reason
not to consider it.

1609
01:04:06,010 --> 01:04:07,910
We only kept one resource each...

1610
01:04:07,910 --> 01:04:09,310
for future trades.

1611
01:04:09,750 --> 01:04:10,880
Both White and I did.

1612
01:04:10,880 --> 01:04:11,880
(Black and White kept 1 diamond each
for future trades.)

1613
01:04:11,880 --> 01:04:13,720
- If not, we can't trade.
- Right.

1614
01:04:13,950 --> 01:04:17,520
(Blue received 100 diamonds
from the equal distribution.)

1615
01:04:18,420 --> 01:04:20,320
Actually, as the weapon dealer,

1616
01:04:20,320 --> 01:04:22,830
I mined enough prize money already.

1617
01:04:22,830 --> 01:04:25,830
Whether gold gets issued
or diamonds get issued....

1618
01:04:25,830 --> 01:04:27,130
isn't really my concern.

1619
01:04:27,530 --> 01:04:29,870
Whether a war breaks out or not
is most important.

1620
01:04:30,170 --> 01:04:34,070
Between Gold and White's power struggle,

1621
01:04:34,070 --> 01:04:36,070
I'm keeping a neutral stance...

1622
01:04:36,070 --> 01:04:38,510
and giving power to one team.

1623
01:04:38,510 --> 01:04:41,750
If so, I think the other team
will feel threatened...

1624
01:04:41,750 --> 01:04:44,850
and end up thinking the only way
to survive is through war.

1625
01:04:49,020 --> 01:04:50,550
- Oh, you're here.
- Oh, he's here?

1626
01:04:50,650 --> 01:04:53,220
- Hello.
- Hello.

1627
01:04:53,220 --> 01:04:54,230
(Black has finished his deals
with the pro-diamond side.)

1628
01:04:54,590 --> 01:04:55,890
You're working so hard.

1629
01:04:55,890 --> 01:04:58,130
Apparently, there's not much I can do,

1630
01:04:58,130 --> 01:04:59,900
- but I came to see you.
- But...

1631
01:04:59,900 --> 01:05:03,700
But doing this with food is a bit mean.

1632
01:05:03,700 --> 01:05:05,000
Oh, but...

1633
01:05:05,000 --> 01:05:06,870
You have much more experience than me.

1634
01:05:06,870 --> 01:05:08,840
You're all very smart.

1635
01:05:08,840 --> 01:05:10,770
You're also someone I admire.

1636
01:05:11,340 --> 01:05:13,880
I know how much war power you have.

1637
01:05:13,880 --> 01:05:16,410
The only way to physically weaken...

1638
01:05:16,410 --> 01:05:18,320
your war power is this.

1639
01:05:18,450 --> 01:05:19,850
That's my thought.

1640
01:05:20,180 --> 01:05:21,650
I get all of that.

1641
01:05:21,650 --> 01:05:24,320
It's fine that we don't get to buy things.

1642
01:05:24,320 --> 01:05:26,890
We can handle that, and we respect that.

1643
01:05:26,890 --> 01:05:31,100
But it sounded like you were saying
you also wouldn't sell...

1644
01:05:31,100 --> 01:05:33,300
- We heard you said you wouldn't sell.
- to the others...

1645
01:05:33,300 --> 01:05:36,670
We were wondering if you could reconsider.

1646
01:05:36,670 --> 01:05:38,070
That sounds like a good idea.

1647
01:05:39,040 --> 01:05:40,240
Thank you for the tip.

1648
01:05:43,540 --> 01:05:47,010
After starving for one day,
we lost our minds.

1649
01:05:47,010 --> 01:05:48,580
So they know how scary it is...

1650
01:05:48,580 --> 01:05:50,180
to starve for a day.

1651
01:05:51,150 --> 01:05:52,380
- So...
- So are you saying you'll keep...

1652
01:05:52,380 --> 01:05:54,220
So you're thinking to keep it up...

1653
01:05:54,220 --> 01:05:55,390
- going forward?
- It's the only power I have.

1654
01:05:55,390 --> 01:05:56,690
It's the only power I have.

1655
01:05:56,690 --> 01:05:58,890
I have no choice
but to leverage this power.

1656
01:05:58,890 --> 01:06:00,420
I'd appreciate it if you could understand.

1657
01:06:02,290 --> 01:06:05,100
To be honest, he was a bit disagreeable.

1658
01:06:05,600 --> 01:06:07,200
He was very disagreeable.

1659
01:06:07,200 --> 01:06:09,500
By talking as if he wasn't planning to...

1660
01:06:09,500 --> 01:06:13,670
but willing to do so because we said so,

1661
01:06:13,670 --> 01:06:16,610
he's shifting the blame
of his evil actions onto us.

1662
01:06:16,610 --> 01:06:19,040
That's very cowardly and underhanded.

1663
01:06:19,440 --> 01:06:21,710
Black was so cool.

1664
01:06:21,810 --> 01:06:24,050
He is so evil. So evil.

1665
01:06:24,050 --> 01:06:26,980
He will make this game more fun.

1666
01:06:26,980 --> 01:06:29,720
I'll have to find a way to kill him.

1667
01:06:29,720 --> 01:06:31,320
It'll be so fun to kill him.

1668
01:06:31,720 --> 01:06:36,090
It was different from the Vector I knew.

1669
01:06:36,090 --> 01:06:37,800
That gave me even more assurance.

1670
01:06:37,800 --> 01:06:41,500
Gold does have the advantage,
as I thought.

1671
01:06:41,830 --> 01:06:44,070
If Black really did have the advantage,

1672
01:06:44,070 --> 01:06:47,710
as he was saying,
if he did have the winning strategy,

1673
01:06:47,710 --> 01:06:49,540
he wouldn't act like that.

1674
01:06:49,540 --> 01:06:51,410
I think he's really worried right now.

1675
01:06:51,410 --> 01:06:54,310
A bomb has really been dropped on Black.

1676
01:06:54,310 --> 01:06:56,980
I don't think that strategy...

1677
01:06:56,980 --> 01:07:00,150
is very helpful to Vector either.

1678
01:07:00,320 --> 01:07:03,090
He also could circulate
the gold currency together,

1679
01:07:03,090 --> 01:07:05,620
compete, and gain more power...

1680
01:07:05,620 --> 01:07:08,430
through that competition.

1681
01:07:08,690 --> 01:07:10,890
To me, it felt a bit...

1682
01:07:10,890 --> 01:07:12,500
penny-wise and pound-foolish,

1683
01:07:12,500 --> 01:07:15,000
his extreme stance...

1684
01:07:15,000 --> 01:07:18,770
of blocking currency circulation
all together.

1685
01:07:18,770 --> 01:07:20,800
I'm very disappointed about that.

1686
01:07:22,270 --> 01:07:24,110
This is all we can talk about for today.

1687
01:07:24,580 --> 01:07:26,340
I can't have gold.

1688
01:07:26,780 --> 01:07:29,210
So I honestly don't know...

1689
01:07:29,210 --> 01:07:30,480
what we're supposed to talk about.

1690
01:07:33,650 --> 01:07:36,090
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

1691
01:07:36,990 --> 01:07:40,320
The Gold Rush has ended.

1692
01:07:40,790 --> 01:07:44,500
It felt like he was being very defensive.

1693
01:07:44,500 --> 01:07:46,560
On the first day,
we didn't get as many resources...

1694
01:07:46,560 --> 01:07:47,730
as we wanted, but...

1695
01:07:47,730 --> 01:07:51,870
We'll definitely make a deal
with Red tomorrow.

1696
01:07:51,870 --> 01:07:53,500
We just need to get the majority.

1697
01:07:53,500 --> 01:07:55,640
This is a game you win
by getting the majority,

1698
01:07:55,640 --> 01:07:57,340
so this is the real deal.

1699
01:07:57,340 --> 01:07:59,310
This isn't about teams.

1700
01:07:59,310 --> 01:08:02,480
It's about who at the end
takes most of the prize.

1701
01:08:02,480 --> 01:08:06,050
That's exactly how Team White's logic
should've flowed from the very beginning.

1702
01:08:06,320 --> 01:08:08,420
I thought I had to watch
how the situation goes.

1703
01:08:08,420 --> 01:08:10,850
Regarding lives,

1704
01:08:10,850 --> 01:08:13,490
fourteen lives were left yesterday.

1705
01:08:13,490 --> 01:08:16,030
Black probably sold some of those.

1706
01:08:16,030 --> 01:08:19,960
So, what matters now
is how many of those are actually left.

1707
01:08:20,060 --> 01:08:21,170
Here it is.

1708
01:08:21,730 --> 01:08:22,830
I want to look.

1709
01:08:23,870 --> 01:08:25,100
Shall I put in two of these
at the same time?

1710
01:08:25,940 --> 01:08:29,970
Team Gold must return the actual gold bars
you have to the return slot...

1711
01:08:30,340 --> 01:08:33,940
and pick up the vouchers for use
from the central box.

1712
01:08:33,940 --> 01:08:35,050
Thank you.

1713
01:08:35,210 --> 01:08:39,120
You can use trading vouchers after filling
in the numbers and submitting them.

1714
01:08:39,920 --> 01:08:41,620
Let's go.

1715
01:08:41,620 --> 01:08:42,750
Thank you for your work.

1716
01:08:42,750 --> 01:08:44,320
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1717
01:08:44,820 --> 01:08:45,990
(Ugong is left alone...)

1718
01:08:45,990 --> 01:08:47,090
Wait a minute.

1719
01:08:47,090 --> 01:08:48,290
(and searches the Community Center.)

1720
01:08:49,590 --> 01:08:50,830
What's this?

1721
01:08:52,100 --> 01:08:54,330
Is this the secret room?

1722
01:08:55,100 --> 01:08:56,970
The first box...

1723
01:08:56,970 --> 01:08:58,700
- Tell...
- These are all different.

1724
01:08:59,070 --> 01:09:01,040
these words...

1725
01:09:01,170 --> 01:09:02,870
And the third one is white.

1726
01:09:02,970 --> 01:09:04,240
Placed within.

1727
01:09:04,610 --> 01:09:06,110
And the third one is red.

1728
01:09:06,110 --> 01:09:08,080
Was it "secret room of center"?

1729
01:09:08,080 --> 01:09:09,580
We think this means...

1730
01:09:09,580 --> 01:09:12,280
the Secret Room of the Community Center.

1731
01:09:12,380 --> 01:09:13,980
That's interesting.

1732
01:09:14,550 --> 01:09:16,150
Then where's the Secret Room?

1733
01:09:16,150 --> 01:09:18,720
Nobody knows that at this moment.
No one has found it yet.

1734
01:09:18,820 --> 01:09:20,290
Could it be Jouju's Secret Room?

1735
01:09:20,290 --> 01:09:21,990
Then shall we solve this first?

1736
01:09:21,990 --> 01:09:23,190
- Yes.
- All right.

1737
01:09:23,590 --> 01:09:25,860
So, we need to think of a word...

1738
01:09:25,860 --> 01:09:28,630
we can guess from the beginning
and the end, and fix it.

1739
01:09:29,300 --> 01:09:30,830
It's so tough even after dividing it.

1740
01:09:31,170 --> 01:09:33,840
Tree hand. Can we say branch for a tree?

1741
01:09:33,840 --> 01:09:35,170
Fortune of the wheel?

1742
01:09:35,470 --> 01:09:36,910
End.

1743
01:09:36,910 --> 01:09:38,380
(Team Gold hasn't solved
the codes on the wall.)

1744
01:09:39,780 --> 01:09:41,350
Doesn't this turn around?

1745
01:09:42,180 --> 01:09:44,850
(Ugong keeps searching for "secret room"
from the codes on the wall.)

1746
01:09:44,850 --> 01:09:46,220
Could that part only turn?

1747
01:09:47,520 --> 01:09:48,750
That's strange.

1748
01:09:54,990 --> 01:09:56,560
Team Red has gotten
very powerful now, as a matter of fact.

1749
01:09:56,690 --> 01:09:58,830
Right. Team Red has gotten quite strong.

1750
01:09:58,960 --> 01:10:02,230
The reason I got so sensitive...

1751
01:10:02,530 --> 01:10:05,000
- was because it got so risky.
- We might get swayed by them.

1752
01:10:05,000 --> 01:10:06,800
What I least want...

1753
01:10:07,000 --> 01:10:08,540
is that we can't decide our destiny...

1754
01:10:08,540 --> 01:10:10,370
- with our hands now.
- I understand.

1755
01:10:10,370 --> 01:10:12,680
Ever since I got stabbed in the back,
I've been traumatized.

1756
01:10:12,880 --> 01:10:14,440
I was terrified that if we lost
these people,

1757
01:10:14,440 --> 01:10:16,710
they'd end up doing something
with Team Gold.

1758
01:10:16,910 --> 01:10:18,720
So I kept on holding onto them
and trying to convince them.

1759
01:10:19,280 --> 01:10:22,820
I only thought about doing my best.

1760
01:10:23,020 --> 01:10:25,560
But you know when you try to do your best,

1761
01:10:25,720 --> 01:10:27,520
you feel like you're going to choke.

1762
01:10:27,890 --> 01:10:30,090
In fact, people who are left...

1763
01:10:30,490 --> 01:10:33,230
were not Leia, Siseon, and Paul,

1764
01:10:33,430 --> 01:10:36,170
but all six people.

1765
01:10:36,170 --> 01:10:38,200
That pressure felt immense.

1766
01:10:38,540 --> 01:10:41,640
But I'm not very strategic.

1767
01:10:41,840 --> 01:10:44,310
So I thought, "There's no way this is it."

1768
01:10:44,310 --> 01:10:45,710
"Am I missing something here?"

1769
01:10:45,880 --> 01:10:48,810
I felt anxious. I felt I was trapped
in a never-ending wheel of anxiety.

1770
01:10:49,150 --> 01:10:51,520
My teammates actually held me back.

1771
01:10:51,920 --> 01:10:54,990
They definitely must have noticed
that I was desperate.

1772
01:10:55,150 --> 01:10:56,490
They said, "Leia, you should calm down."

1773
01:10:56,720 --> 01:10:58,560
"Listen. You can do this."

1774
01:10:58,560 --> 01:11:01,830
That's how two of those
helped me so much today.

1775
01:11:08,300 --> 01:11:09,770
I know.

1776
01:11:09,900 --> 01:11:12,000
Guys, I finally pulled myself together.

1777
01:11:12,240 --> 01:11:13,340
- Great.
- Okay.

1778
01:11:13,570 --> 01:11:16,070
I wondered what made me do so today.

1779
01:11:16,270 --> 01:11:18,280
- You replayed it?
- I replayed it.

1780
01:11:18,280 --> 01:11:20,180
I think I had no room to breathe.

1781
01:11:20,180 --> 01:11:21,210
Right.

1782
01:11:21,210 --> 01:11:22,250
It's your first time.

1783
01:11:22,250 --> 01:11:24,250
Even though Luna was a spy,

1784
01:11:24,410 --> 01:11:25,880
I think she did her best...

1785
01:11:25,880 --> 01:11:27,780
- for our team.
- That's right.

1786
01:11:27,780 --> 01:11:29,550
I think I need to perform
as much as she did,

1787
01:11:29,550 --> 01:11:30,550
Right.

1788
01:11:30,550 --> 01:11:32,720
and keep these three survivors safe.

1789
01:11:32,720 --> 01:11:34,790
That thought is stuck in my head.

1790
01:11:34,990 --> 01:11:37,630
And the sacrifice of three people
from our team yesterday...

1791
01:11:38,100 --> 01:11:40,560
hit me too hard psychologically.

1792
01:11:40,560 --> 01:11:43,000
In fact, as I see, Leia worked hard.

1793
01:11:43,000 --> 01:11:44,130
- Right.
- She did her best.

1794
01:11:44,130 --> 01:11:45,900
I will give myself some room
to breathe from now on.

1795
01:11:45,900 --> 01:11:47,000
- Okay.
- Yes.

1796
01:11:47,000 --> 01:11:49,070
I'm sure there's a reason
that three of us survived.

1797
01:11:49,410 --> 01:11:51,510
You need to save your energy for yourself.

1798
01:11:51,510 --> 01:11:52,840
- Okay.
- Save your energy.

1799
01:11:52,940 --> 01:11:54,180
Thank you, everyone.

1800
01:11:54,650 --> 01:11:56,350
I got my head completely back
in the game now.

1801
01:11:57,780 --> 01:11:59,380
It's time for dinner.

1802
01:12:00,220 --> 01:12:01,920
Residents, please gather
at the Town Hall...

1803
01:12:01,920 --> 01:12:04,190
and enjoy your dinner.

1804
01:12:04,890 --> 01:12:06,720
- What should we do now?
- We should have dinner.

1805
01:12:06,720 --> 01:12:08,390
Can I look around without dinner?

1806
01:12:08,390 --> 01:12:09,630
Are we having dinner today?

1807
01:12:09,630 --> 01:12:10,830
We'll give you dinner.

1808
01:12:11,230 --> 01:12:12,500
Why isn't anyone here?

1809
01:12:12,700 --> 01:12:14,870
Now, they went in to leave
their resources there.

1810
01:12:15,130 --> 01:12:17,830
- I see.
- We just made a deal.

1811
01:12:18,300 --> 01:12:20,070
- But actually,
- Yes.

1812
01:12:20,370 --> 01:12:22,510
it's hard for outsiders
to settle down here.

1813
01:12:22,510 --> 01:12:24,440
They can't grasp the situation
in the middle.

1814
01:12:24,440 --> 01:12:27,310
However, they have
a whole lot of experience...

1815
01:12:27,310 --> 01:12:28,850
- and competence.
- That's right.

1816
01:12:28,850 --> 01:12:30,180
They might be holding
a massive plot twist up their sleeves.

1817
01:12:30,180 --> 01:12:31,380
- They must have something.
- Right.

1818
01:12:31,920 --> 01:12:34,520
- They're an all-star team.
- They're not background characters.

1819
01:12:34,890 --> 01:12:36,990
They gathered all-star-quality members.

1820
01:12:39,560 --> 01:12:40,590
This...

1821
01:12:50,470 --> 01:12:52,640
(Dinner)

1822
01:12:54,370 --> 01:12:55,740
Gosh, this smells really amazing.

1823
01:12:56,710 --> 01:13:00,240
(Maillard is called
every time they grill meat.)

1824
01:13:00,510 --> 01:13:03,480
Am I actually watching this now?

1825
01:13:06,820 --> 01:13:08,090
(Amazed)

1826
01:13:09,590 --> 01:13:10,850
We'll have five fried chickens too.

1827
01:13:11,560 --> 01:13:13,620
- We have a lot of food. Eat up.
- I'll eat all of these.

1828
01:13:13,620 --> 01:13:14,830
Today might be the last time we do this.

1829
01:13:14,830 --> 01:13:16,290
It's our first time to eat like this.

1830
01:13:16,890 --> 01:13:18,960
- Eat up.
- I hope we have another Team Catfish.

1831
01:13:19,400 --> 01:13:20,430
So you can eat a lot again?

1832
01:13:21,300 --> 01:13:22,770
I think I need to help.

1833
01:13:22,770 --> 01:13:25,570
- No, I'm fine.
- Never mind.

1834
01:13:25,570 --> 01:13:27,700
No.

1835
01:13:28,510 --> 01:13:30,240
I know. You must be hungry.

1836
01:13:30,240 --> 01:13:33,540
You must have left in the morning.

1837
01:13:33,580 --> 01:13:35,510
(That day, we realized
that even a country could go bankrupt.)

1838
01:13:35,880 --> 01:13:37,580
When I'm stressed, I don't have a meal.

1839
01:13:37,580 --> 01:13:40,150
Not because I'm hungry,
but because I need to use my brain.

1840
01:13:40,350 --> 01:13:41,590
I only needed the sugar from the food.

1841
01:13:41,590 --> 01:13:43,750
When I was in the basement
in the past, I only had Coke.

1842
01:13:43,820 --> 01:13:45,190
I didn't feel hungry,

1843
01:13:45,190 --> 01:13:47,920
but I had to keep my brain firing.

1844
01:13:47,920 --> 01:13:49,990
I didn't want to have a meal.

1845
01:13:49,990 --> 01:13:51,290
Do we have something like that?

1846
01:13:51,290 --> 01:13:52,560
I guess so.

1847
01:13:53,760 --> 01:13:54,830
Give me a hint.

1848
01:13:55,130 --> 01:13:56,170
We might have one.

1849
01:13:56,170 --> 01:13:57,770
- No, I can't.
- No?

1850
01:13:57,770 --> 01:14:00,240
No. I had such a hard time solving this.

1851
01:14:05,610 --> 01:14:09,610
He's relentless.

1852
01:14:09,610 --> 01:14:12,020
He just keeps digging.

1853
01:14:12,150 --> 01:14:15,490
When he finds a problem,
he has to solve it to the end.

1854
01:14:15,990 --> 01:14:19,420
Ugong tried to read the game quickly.

1855
01:14:19,420 --> 01:14:21,630
He asked questions in detail...

1856
01:14:21,630 --> 01:14:24,190
and tried to gather information.

1857
01:14:24,800 --> 01:14:27,600
I was excited, but at the same time,
I was low-key terrified.

1858
01:14:29,600 --> 01:14:31,700
(After Gold Speech)

1859
01:14:32,700 --> 01:14:35,440
I think that's what it's about.

1860
01:14:35,440 --> 01:14:37,170
- I see.
- You know,

1861
01:14:37,170 --> 01:14:38,980
something like the Great Depression.

1862
01:14:38,980 --> 01:14:41,510
- Black Monday.
- There's a book with the same content.

1863
01:14:41,510 --> 01:14:42,780
The title of the book is "Money."

1864
01:14:42,780 --> 01:14:46,950
Are numbers, year, and date
written on there?

1865
01:14:46,950 --> 01:14:48,690
Not in the title of the book.

1866
01:14:49,990 --> 01:14:50,990
(Udong came up with the solution
the moment he saw the problem.)

1867
01:14:50,990 --> 01:14:53,990
We don't have the problem yet,
so I wondered if we have any.

1868
01:14:55,560 --> 01:15:00,000
(Team Gold's skill is secured
from the beginning.)

1869
01:15:03,970 --> 01:15:05,270
Is everyone there except us?

1870
01:15:05,270 --> 01:15:06,400
- I guess so.
- That's right.

1871
01:15:06,400 --> 01:15:07,800
- My back ached so much.
- Today, it's so...

1872
01:15:07,800 --> 01:15:09,670
- The packed meal today is top-tier.
- Oh, my.

1873
01:15:09,670 --> 01:15:12,140
Thank you for feeding us.

1874
01:15:12,140 --> 01:15:13,210
Enjoy.

1875
01:15:13,210 --> 01:15:15,310
I really needed a meal.

1876
01:15:15,580 --> 01:15:18,720
When you were leaving yesterday,
your choice was to leave...

1877
01:15:18,720 --> 01:15:20,120
and you went around
with a smile on your face.

1878
01:15:20,120 --> 01:15:22,250
- You'll be alright.
- I knew I shouldn't smile...

1879
01:15:22,250 --> 01:15:23,520
- but I couldn't help it.
- When she was leaving at the end,

1880
01:15:23,520 --> 01:15:24,650
she left with that smile on her face.

1881
01:15:24,650 --> 01:15:27,220
What were you thinking
when I cried cooking ramyeon?

1882
01:15:27,220 --> 01:15:28,730
I know. She cried her eyes out.

1883
01:15:28,730 --> 01:15:31,390
That's why I thought it was so dramatic.

1884
01:15:31,390 --> 01:15:34,660
In fact, you could kill
and three of us before leaving.

1885
01:15:34,660 --> 01:15:36,730
You could. That actually could have been
the best choice from your perspective.

1886
01:15:36,730 --> 01:15:38,770
However, I was in Team White
until yesterday.

1887
01:15:38,770 --> 01:15:40,400
Then I couldn't have looked
at you with a smile today.

1888
01:15:40,500 --> 01:15:41,870
Yes, that's right.

1889
01:15:41,870 --> 01:15:44,270
Anyway, you've gone through a lot.
Let's do our best.

1890
01:15:46,080 --> 01:15:49,050
But Leia was just...

1891
01:15:49,410 --> 01:15:51,750
having a motherly smile on her face.

1892
01:15:51,750 --> 01:15:54,080
She smiled when I didn't expect it,
so I appreciated that.

1893
01:15:54,820 --> 01:15:56,350
Thank you so much for the food.

1894
01:15:56,350 --> 01:15:58,820
Go ahead. You haven't had a meal all day.

1895
01:16:02,190 --> 01:16:03,590
I don't have an appetite, though.

1896
01:16:06,260 --> 01:16:07,400
- The last supper.
- Yes.

1897
01:16:08,900 --> 01:16:11,000
We never know what will happen.

1898
01:16:11,000 --> 01:16:13,340
This might not be the last supper.
Tomorrow, something...

1899
01:16:13,340 --> 01:16:14,640
we didn't expect could happen.

1900
01:16:16,370 --> 01:16:18,170
I guess that would work.

1901
01:16:18,170 --> 01:16:19,680
Five people...

1902
01:16:20,810 --> 01:16:22,150
- Donkey.
- Yes.

1903
01:16:22,310 --> 01:16:23,480
Nice to meet you.

1904
01:16:24,210 --> 01:16:27,080
The one with long hair...

1905
01:16:27,280 --> 01:16:29,290
I enjoy watching your videos.

1906
01:16:29,290 --> 01:16:31,120
- Really?
- They show a lot on my algorithm.

1907
01:16:31,120 --> 01:16:32,720
Right. I see.

1908
01:16:33,120 --> 01:16:34,930
Thank you. I had no idea
you were watching them.

1909
01:16:35,230 --> 01:16:36,330
What was your major?

1910
01:16:36,560 --> 01:16:39,360
I studied industrial engineering
and management science.

1911
01:16:39,360 --> 01:16:42,430
That's why you grasp things quickly.

1912
01:16:42,700 --> 01:16:43,900
You went to a good school...

1913
01:16:44,230 --> 01:16:46,070
- No, I just...
- because you couldn't go to KAIST.

1914
01:16:46,070 --> 01:16:48,310
- Right. The local college in Korea.
- I watched that video.

1915
01:16:50,110 --> 01:16:51,270
I wasn't accepted at KAIST.

1916
01:16:51,270 --> 01:16:52,710
He went to UNIST.

1917
01:16:52,810 --> 01:16:54,010
I joked about it.

1918
01:16:54,010 --> 01:16:55,050
UNIST is a prestigious school.

1919
01:16:55,050 --> 01:16:56,510
It is, but he said...

1920
01:16:56,510 --> 01:16:58,210
that he went to UNIST
because he wasn't accepted at KAIST.

1921
01:16:58,520 --> 01:17:00,080
It's the Institute of Science
and Technology.

1922
01:17:00,250 --> 01:17:03,120
From the perspective of someone
who experienced a survival show,

1923
01:17:03,120 --> 01:17:06,820
the first and the second days here
means a lot of time.

1924
01:17:06,820 --> 01:17:08,690
And there was a massive web...

1925
01:17:08,690 --> 01:17:10,890
of complex power dynamics at play.

1926
01:17:11,060 --> 01:17:13,630
So I decided to approach them...

1927
01:17:13,630 --> 01:17:15,070
and get on their good side.

1928
01:17:15,070 --> 01:17:16,370
"I watched your videos."

1929
01:17:16,630 --> 01:17:18,800
"I watched that one, and I found it fun."

1930
01:17:19,070 --> 01:17:20,470
I talked about those things,

1931
01:17:20,470 --> 01:17:22,940
greeted them,

1932
01:17:22,970 --> 01:17:24,980
and kept saying a lot of things...

1933
01:17:24,980 --> 01:17:26,580
for ice breaking.

1934
01:17:26,580 --> 01:17:29,980
I tried my best to make a conversation.

1935
01:17:30,110 --> 01:17:31,980
Since this is a survival show,

1936
01:17:31,980 --> 01:17:34,450
we could change teams
and we never know what would happen.

1937
01:17:34,450 --> 01:17:35,850
They're in different teams now,

1938
01:17:35,850 --> 01:17:38,520
but later, the teams can be mixed up.

1939
01:17:38,520 --> 01:17:39,990
We never know.

1940
01:17:40,090 --> 01:17:42,090
I am doing my best, in my own way.

1941
01:17:43,060 --> 01:17:44,590
- I gave it some thought.
- Yes.

1942
01:17:45,400 --> 01:17:47,900
- I found how to keep our prize money.
- What is it?

1943
01:17:48,870 --> 01:17:51,030
- We can make Team Gold win.
- Is that so?

1944
01:17:51,030 --> 01:17:53,770
I can be a double spy.

1945
01:17:54,100 --> 01:17:55,540
I can go to Team Gold and say,

1946
01:17:55,540 --> 01:17:58,310
"I can help you if you don't solve
the problem on the wall."

1947
01:17:58,310 --> 01:18:01,010
I actually don't need diamonds.

1948
01:18:01,010 --> 01:18:03,950
When Team Gold opens it,
something might happen.

1949
01:18:04,210 --> 01:18:05,420
It can bring up curiosity.

1950
01:18:05,980 --> 01:18:07,920
But I can honestly say,

1951
01:18:08,120 --> 01:18:09,490
"If you solve it,"

1952
01:18:09,590 --> 01:18:11,150
"you're ruined.
You will lose no matter what."

1953
01:18:11,620 --> 01:18:13,060
"If you don't open it, I'll help you."

1954
01:18:13,060 --> 01:18:14,920
Then you can keep it.

1955
01:18:14,920 --> 01:18:16,330
I can keep it. Yes.

1956
01:18:16,630 --> 01:18:17,890
So, let's do that.

1957
01:18:17,890 --> 01:18:20,060
We can play nice and keep our prize money.

1958
01:18:20,060 --> 01:18:22,430
And we vote for our side.

1959
01:18:22,770 --> 01:18:24,630
- I see.
- Then we can win after all.

1960
01:18:25,000 --> 01:18:26,200
- I get it.
- Yes.

1961
01:18:26,340 --> 01:18:28,470
What do you think
about the double spy strategy?

1962
01:18:29,010 --> 01:18:30,070
I love that.

1963
01:18:30,670 --> 01:18:33,010
I think that's the only way.

1964
01:18:33,010 --> 01:18:34,040
I see.

1965
01:18:34,540 --> 01:18:37,910
(Luna and Mokgye are taking a rest.)

1966
01:18:37,910 --> 01:18:40,280
Can I join you here?

1967
01:18:42,320 --> 01:18:44,920
Don't you think odds are stacked
against Team Gold right now?

1968
01:18:46,090 --> 01:18:47,890
I don't think so, though.

1969
01:18:49,060 --> 01:18:50,830
- It's advantageous for Team Gold.
- Right.

1970
01:18:51,930 --> 01:18:54,060
- In the current situation?
- Not according to my calculations.

1971
01:18:54,060 --> 01:18:56,470
And what would you do
when they run out of lives?

1972
01:18:56,470 --> 01:18:57,770
We just need to hold out.

1973
01:18:57,770 --> 01:18:59,900
I'm not trying to hold out.

1974
01:19:00,740 --> 01:19:01,940
To be honest, I...

1975
01:19:02,210 --> 01:19:06,240
Today's Majority Rules Game
will soon begin.

1976
01:19:06,740 --> 01:19:07,880
I'll be honest with you.

1977
01:19:07,880 --> 01:19:10,610
I'm a double spy,

1978
01:19:10,610 --> 01:19:12,020
so I need to help Team Gold.

1979
01:19:12,020 --> 01:19:13,550
I'm helping Team Gold.

1980
01:19:13,880 --> 01:19:16,390
- I can't believe that.
- It's strange.

1981
01:19:16,390 --> 01:19:17,920
If you don't want to trust me,
you don't have to.

1982
01:19:17,920 --> 01:19:19,090
It's not that I don't trust you.

1983
01:19:19,090 --> 01:19:21,730
- Why should we do that?
- It doesn't make sense to me.

1984
01:19:22,060 --> 01:19:24,130
I don't need diamond or gold.

1985
01:19:24,290 --> 01:19:25,860
Then what do you want?

1986
01:19:25,860 --> 01:19:27,500
There's another way to earn money.

1987
01:19:27,500 --> 01:19:29,800
- What's that?
- I can't tell you.

1988
01:19:30,400 --> 01:19:31,800
Anyway, there's that.

1989
01:19:32,800 --> 01:19:35,910
So I don't need to help
Team White or Team Gold.

1990
01:19:36,110 --> 01:19:38,540
Now, well... Okay. So?

1991
01:19:38,540 --> 01:19:40,310
You can decide to trust me or not.

1992
01:19:40,380 --> 01:19:42,010
You'll need me at one point.

1993
01:19:43,110 --> 01:19:44,650
You'll need us at one point too.

1994
01:19:44,650 --> 01:19:46,050
I seriously won't.

1995
01:19:46,120 --> 01:19:48,350
I have enough lives. It won't go down.

1996
01:19:49,090 --> 01:19:51,860
- No, how many do you have?
- It's not enough.

1997
01:19:52,020 --> 01:19:53,120
It's more than enough.

1998
01:19:54,390 --> 01:19:55,390
- What?
- Well...

1999
01:19:55,390 --> 01:19:58,090
That's why they said they had no choice
but to risk a war.

2000
01:19:58,090 --> 01:20:00,760
- We...
- They did to make the first move.

2001
01:20:00,960 --> 01:20:02,800
If they don't, that's even better for us.

2002
01:20:02,800 --> 01:20:05,300
If neither side strikes, the game's over.

2003
01:20:05,540 --> 01:20:06,600
So...

2004
01:20:07,240 --> 01:20:09,110
the situation is really unfavorable.

2005
01:20:09,110 --> 01:20:13,110
But what are you really getting at
by saying that?

2006
01:20:13,180 --> 01:20:16,110
I just wanted you to know.

2007
01:20:16,410 --> 01:20:18,720
We can talk about it
at the negotiating table...

2008
01:20:19,820 --> 01:20:22,050
- You shouldn't have left it like that.
- later.

2009
01:20:22,050 --> 01:20:24,190
I think this could be a bluff.

2010
01:20:24,520 --> 01:20:25,790
Think as you wish.

2011
01:20:25,790 --> 01:20:27,560
(She was displeased with the attitude
shown during the Gold Rush.)

2012
01:20:27,560 --> 01:20:29,690
When I tried to play double agent
and said...

2013
01:20:30,130 --> 01:20:32,130
"Gold is at an absurdly..."

2014
01:20:32,130 --> 01:20:34,160
"big disadvantage,"

2015
01:20:34,800 --> 01:20:37,700
she actually got suspicious of me
and snapped back,

2016
01:20:38,270 --> 01:20:39,570
so there was nothing more I could say.

2017
01:20:39,670 --> 01:20:42,010
There was no way to persuade her.

2018
01:20:42,340 --> 01:20:45,440
If the weapon dealer code
got figured out and just exposed,

2019
01:20:45,810 --> 01:20:49,480
then I was thinking I'd just start
a couple of wars...

2020
01:20:49,610 --> 01:20:52,420
and leave with the minimum prize money.

2021
01:20:58,150 --> 01:21:01,990
Today's Majority Rules Game will begin.

2022
01:21:02,230 --> 01:21:04,730
Today's Majority Rules Game topic is...

2023
01:21:04,730 --> 01:21:06,130
"If I had the chance..."

2024
01:21:06,130 --> 01:21:08,200
"to hack into the account
of a corrupt company..."

2025
01:21:08,570 --> 01:21:11,130
"that routinely evades taxes
and donate the entire amount to cover..."

2026
01:21:11,130 --> 01:21:14,070
"a charity's operating costs,"

2027
01:21:14,070 --> 01:21:18,140
"I would go through with the hack
even if it meant breaking the law."

2028
01:21:18,370 --> 01:21:20,980
For one hour, Residents...

2029
01:21:21,280 --> 01:21:23,280
can freely express their opinions...

2030
01:21:23,280 --> 01:21:25,980
at the podium.

2031
01:21:27,050 --> 01:21:29,550
- Principle...
- I can't remember.

2032
01:21:29,720 --> 01:21:31,720
I think it's okay if we go differently.

2033
01:21:31,890 --> 01:21:33,590
It's okay. We just need to decide.

2034
01:21:35,330 --> 01:21:36,930
You can go out and say right away
if something comes to mind.

2035
01:21:36,930 --> 01:21:37,930
- Yes.
- Seriously?

2036
01:21:37,930 --> 01:21:39,560
Later on, it will get competitive.

2037
01:21:39,660 --> 01:21:41,200
Now, we have time.

2038
01:21:41,430 --> 01:21:42,930
Later, when we only have 5 to 10 minutes,

2039
01:21:42,930 --> 01:21:44,430
things will get busier.

2040
01:21:44,430 --> 01:21:45,670
Can we go multiple times?

2041
01:21:45,670 --> 01:21:47,340
- Yes, you can.
- Yes.

2042
01:21:48,440 --> 01:21:49,470
(The first speaker is Reboot.)

2043
01:21:49,470 --> 01:21:52,110
- The lawyer is here!
- Yes!

2044
01:21:54,140 --> 01:21:55,780
First of all, in my opinion,

2045
01:21:55,780 --> 01:21:58,450
justice is not a simple matter.

2046
01:21:58,450 --> 01:22:01,150
Punishing those who have committed
crimes is justice,

2047
01:22:01,350 --> 01:22:04,390
and at the same time,
protecting the human rights...

2048
01:22:04,520 --> 01:22:08,060
of the guilty and following
due legal process...

2049
01:22:08,060 --> 01:22:11,090
is also a crucial part of justice.

2050
01:22:11,230 --> 01:22:14,430
I have no intention
of siding with a tax evader.

2051
01:22:14,430 --> 01:22:17,170
However, as that proposition suggests,

2052
01:22:17,170 --> 01:22:19,070
to claim you'll establish justice...

2053
01:22:19,070 --> 01:22:21,570
through an illegal means like hacking...

2054
01:22:21,570 --> 01:22:23,210
is utterly absurd.

2055
01:22:23,210 --> 01:22:24,540
Donating money...

2056
01:22:24,570 --> 01:22:26,840
is a good purpose, but...

2057
01:22:26,940 --> 01:22:30,110
I believe that trying to achieve
one's goals...

2058
01:22:30,110 --> 01:22:32,980
through hacking as a means
will inevitably lead...

2059
01:22:32,980 --> 01:22:35,990
society down a vicious cycle...

2060
01:22:35,990 --> 01:22:38,320
that produces enormous chaos,

2061
01:22:38,320 --> 01:22:40,560
disorder, and even more crimes,

2062
01:22:40,560 --> 01:22:43,430
to the point where society can
no longer sustain itself.

2063
01:22:43,430 --> 01:22:45,700
Therefore, for something to be
called justice,

2064
01:22:45,700 --> 01:22:48,400
it goes without saying
that the end must be legitimate,

2065
01:22:48,400 --> 01:22:52,500
and the means and procedures
must also strictly conform to the law.

2066
01:22:53,200 --> 01:22:54,270
That was neat.

2067
01:22:55,140 --> 01:22:58,470
Reboot gave a great speech.

2068
01:22:58,570 --> 01:23:02,010
He has a job that requires one too.

2069
01:23:02,010 --> 01:23:05,180
His speaking pace was impressive too.

2070
01:23:05,280 --> 01:23:08,150
I think he'll get a lot of MVPs.

2071
01:23:08,480 --> 01:23:10,150
I loved Reboot.

2072
01:23:10,420 --> 01:23:12,720
When someone speaks well,

2073
01:23:12,720 --> 01:23:14,720
there's something behind their words.

2074
01:23:14,820 --> 01:23:16,130
In the end, that's logic.

2075
01:23:16,130 --> 01:23:19,160
The person who delivers that logic
is also important.

2076
01:23:19,200 --> 01:23:22,530
It felt like I was looking at an ideal
where everything aligns.

2077
01:23:24,630 --> 01:23:27,070
(The second speaker is Mokgye.)

2078
01:23:29,370 --> 01:23:33,040
Attempting to hack here
could itself become...

2079
01:23:33,280 --> 01:23:35,850
an opportunity to expose this company.

2080
01:23:36,110 --> 01:23:38,850
The fact that they can hack
means they have the skills.

2081
01:23:38,850 --> 01:23:40,320
So when you hack,

2082
01:23:40,320 --> 01:23:43,120
you might get caught, or you might not.

2083
01:23:43,650 --> 01:23:46,560
Even if I get caught,
I'm still going to hack.

2084
01:23:46,890 --> 01:23:48,990
I think the light punishment
I'd receive...

2085
01:23:49,190 --> 01:23:51,630
is very small compared
to the benefit society...

2086
01:23:51,890 --> 01:23:54,060
would gain.

2087
01:23:54,300 --> 01:23:55,870
The law exists to protect all of us...

2088
01:23:55,870 --> 01:23:58,330
and to protect the majority of good,

2089
01:23:58,330 --> 01:23:59,770
decent people.

2090
01:24:00,040 --> 01:24:02,970
How long must we keep
protecting this company...

2091
01:24:02,970 --> 01:24:05,010
that is violating it?

2092
01:24:05,010 --> 01:24:06,780
I believe we sometimes...

2093
01:24:07,110 --> 01:24:10,750
need to be like Don Quixote
and muster up some courage.

2094
01:24:10,810 --> 01:24:11,850
Thank you.

2095
01:24:11,850 --> 01:24:14,450
(True to her code,
she spoke through "Consequence")

2096
01:24:17,420 --> 01:24:19,590
When criminals decide...

2097
01:24:19,590 --> 01:24:22,130
whether or not to commit a crime...

2098
01:24:22,130 --> 01:24:24,690
I need some assistance in English,
expected value.

2099
01:24:24,790 --> 01:24:26,900
What kind of results are at play.

2100
01:24:26,900 --> 01:24:28,160
- Expected value.
- Expected value.

2101
01:24:28,670 --> 01:24:31,800
Criminals keep doing it because,
based on their expectations,

2102
01:24:31,800 --> 01:24:34,700
the gains from tax evasion are greater.

2103
01:24:34,700 --> 01:24:36,370
Recently in the US,

2104
01:24:36,370 --> 01:24:39,480
there was a young man named
Luigi Mangione...

2105
01:24:39,640 --> 01:24:43,450
who was hailed as a hero after shooting
a health insurance CEO.

2106
01:24:43,580 --> 01:24:46,080
He's getting a huge amount
of support in American society.

2107
01:24:46,380 --> 01:24:49,890
Among the homeless in the US,

2108
01:24:49,890 --> 01:24:51,550
there are a great many people...

2109
01:24:51,550 --> 01:24:54,690
who ended up on the streets
because of medical bills.

2110
01:24:54,690 --> 01:24:58,090
By shooting the CEO of
such a corrupt company, he's making...

2111
01:24:58,290 --> 01:25:01,060
other CEOs stop
and take a look at themselves.

2112
01:25:01,060 --> 01:25:02,670
"Are we doing the right thing here?"

2113
01:25:02,830 --> 01:25:05,940
If we do something like this,
word will get around.

2114
01:25:05,940 --> 01:25:08,910
We were hacked, and it looks like
it's because of our tax evasion.

2115
01:25:09,110 --> 01:25:12,810
Because word will get around,
I think there's a higher chance...

2116
01:25:12,980 --> 01:25:15,140
they'll evade taxes less
or cut back on it.

2117
01:25:15,140 --> 01:25:16,810
Since the social benefit is greater,

2118
01:25:16,810 --> 01:25:20,880
I cast my vote in favor of
carrying out the hack.

2119
01:25:22,050 --> 01:25:25,290
Compared to the impact they made
when Team Gold first appeared,

2120
01:25:25,290 --> 01:25:28,190
they actually seem like
very pure, innocent people.

2121
01:25:28,560 --> 01:25:31,790
They spoke with sincerity
when they made their point,

2122
01:25:31,790 --> 01:25:33,660
but I was hoping for sharper logic.

2123
01:25:34,300 --> 01:25:36,600
I don't know. It was passable.

2124
01:25:36,800 --> 01:25:39,170
Team Gold had a strong presence.

2125
01:25:39,170 --> 01:25:41,370
They all seem like impressive people.

2126
01:25:41,540 --> 01:25:43,410
Listening to their speech...

2127
01:25:43,410 --> 01:25:45,110
during Majority Rules Game...

2128
01:25:45,310 --> 01:25:47,080
made me realize they were all nervous...

2129
01:25:47,080 --> 01:25:48,980
because it's their first time.

2130
01:25:49,250 --> 01:25:50,910
I think we need to ask ourselves...

2131
01:25:51,110 --> 01:25:53,250
whether this is
truly the only opportunity...

2132
01:25:53,250 --> 01:25:55,620
to expose that corrupt company.

2133
01:25:55,620 --> 01:25:59,220
When asked whether we really
have to go that far to uphold the law,

2134
01:25:59,390 --> 01:26:01,420
let me give an extreme example.

2135
01:26:01,620 --> 01:26:03,790
In World War II,

2136
01:26:03,790 --> 01:26:05,290
even when Nazi war criminals
were captured,

2137
01:26:05,290 --> 01:26:07,100
we didn't just execute them on the spot.

2138
01:26:07,460 --> 01:26:10,400
We put them before
the International Court of Justice.

2139
01:26:10,600 --> 01:26:14,170
So they were punished through
due legal process.

2140
01:26:14,570 --> 01:26:15,670
Why was that?

2141
01:26:15,910 --> 01:26:17,740
The moment we condemn a team...

2142
01:26:17,740 --> 01:26:21,440
based purely on some pent up grudge,
that kind of emotion...

2143
01:26:21,580 --> 01:26:24,110
or the desire to punish them,
without any principles...

2144
01:26:24,110 --> 01:26:26,250
I believe that would open the door
to all forms of private retaliation...

2145
01:26:26,250 --> 01:26:28,050
being tolerated in the world.

2146
01:26:28,050 --> 01:26:29,820
(All we have to do right now is fire
a missile and kill one person.)

2147
01:26:30,250 --> 01:26:32,420
I think we also need to look for...

2148
01:26:32,420 --> 01:26:34,190
other ways to punish criminals...

2149
01:26:34,190 --> 01:26:36,630
within the boundaries of society.

2150
01:26:37,190 --> 01:26:39,000
We need to keep Team Gold in check.

2151
01:26:39,000 --> 01:26:42,230
I thought of tricking my code.

2152
01:26:42,230 --> 01:26:43,570
I'll talk the opposite.

2153
01:26:43,570 --> 01:26:45,130
The nuance is more like,

2154
01:26:45,130 --> 01:26:48,170
"Never mind the law.
Would you actually do it?"

2155
01:26:48,300 --> 01:26:52,010
I don't know how you all feel
about jaywalking,

2156
01:26:52,140 --> 01:26:54,010
but I'm a fan of it.

2157
01:26:55,410 --> 01:26:56,910
- You're a fan?
- To that extent?

2158
01:26:56,910 --> 01:26:58,980
- I do it frequently.
- "Frequently."

2159
01:26:58,980 --> 01:27:00,850
If I think about why,

2160
01:27:00,850 --> 01:27:03,850
when I went to London ten years ago,

2161
01:27:03,850 --> 01:27:06,520
there weren't many traffic lights,

2162
01:27:06,520 --> 01:27:08,220
and jaywalking was rampant.

2163
01:27:08,220 --> 01:27:10,560
So I asked the locals.

2164
01:27:10,690 --> 01:27:12,500
They called it not jaywalking...

2165
01:27:12,500 --> 01:27:14,560
but "autonomous crossing."

2166
01:27:14,560 --> 01:27:16,800
Why? If you have the capacity
to take responsibility for yourself,

2167
01:27:16,800 --> 01:27:18,230
if you judge on your own that...

2168
01:27:18,230 --> 01:27:20,340
you're aware of your surroundings...

2169
01:27:20,340 --> 01:27:22,000
and won't get hit by someone else's car,

2170
01:27:22,000 --> 01:27:23,570
and you cross then it's not jaywalking,

2171
01:27:23,570 --> 01:27:26,410
it's walking
under your own responsibility.

2172
01:27:26,410 --> 01:27:28,540
I was deeply struck by that idea.

2173
01:27:29,050 --> 01:27:32,220
In Korea, that's illegal.

2174
01:27:32,220 --> 01:27:35,620
But I, autonomously,
under my own judgment...

2175
01:27:35,620 --> 01:27:38,590
Maetel mentioned expected value.

2176
01:27:38,590 --> 01:27:40,420
I like that too. Why?

2177
01:27:40,420 --> 01:27:42,590
I work in finance too,

2178
01:27:42,730 --> 01:27:44,190
so I calculate expected values.

2179
01:27:44,190 --> 01:27:45,730
When I calculate the value of the fine...

2180
01:27:45,730 --> 01:27:47,600
or criminal penalty
I could get if I'm caught,

2181
01:27:47,600 --> 01:27:50,000
if the profit I can gain is...

2182
01:27:50,000 --> 01:27:51,530
far greater than...

2183
01:27:51,530 --> 01:27:54,900
the expected value I'd be punished,

2184
01:27:54,900 --> 01:27:56,710
then this is...

2185
01:27:56,710 --> 01:27:58,840
autonomous crossing.
There's no reason not to do it.

2186
01:27:59,640 --> 01:28:02,550
I thought his autonomous crossing logic
was perfect.

2187
01:28:02,880 --> 01:28:04,680
It was interesting to hear...

2188
01:28:04,680 --> 01:28:07,250
an example showing how that could work...

2189
01:28:07,250 --> 01:28:08,420
when you shift your perspective.

2190
01:28:08,550 --> 01:28:10,920
That kind of argument is
actually refreshing.

2191
01:28:10,920 --> 01:28:12,490
It may sound refreshing...

2192
01:28:12,490 --> 01:28:14,820
and seem to make sense.

2193
01:28:14,920 --> 01:28:16,190
But I think it's wrong.

2194
01:28:16,190 --> 01:28:19,400
You called it autonomous crossing. Fine.

2195
01:28:19,400 --> 01:28:22,000
But if that's the case,
then this could happen too.

2196
01:28:22,730 --> 01:28:24,070
Benevolent theft.

2197
01:28:24,230 --> 01:28:27,500
If I do it, it can become righteous theft.

2198
01:28:27,500 --> 01:28:31,110
The very concept of justice
cannot be made subjective.

2199
01:28:31,110 --> 01:28:34,310
If we end up in a world where
whatever you insist on becomes justice,

2200
01:28:34,480 --> 01:28:36,310
would we want to
live in a world like that?

2201
01:28:36,580 --> 01:28:39,720
And another thing. I believe
we should still follow the law,

2202
01:28:39,920 --> 01:28:41,880
and if the law is lacking,

2203
01:28:42,150 --> 01:28:45,860
we should change it through proper means.

2204
01:28:45,860 --> 01:28:47,990
We don't want to change the law.

2205
01:28:49,230 --> 01:28:50,890
I think it's right to do it.

2206
01:28:51,490 --> 01:28:52,960
Recently in the news,

2207
01:28:52,960 --> 01:28:55,100
a young daughter was sexually assaulted,

2208
01:28:55,200 --> 01:28:57,000
and the perpetrator
got a slap on the wrist.

2209
01:28:57,000 --> 01:28:59,900
So the mother killed him.

2210
01:29:00,040 --> 01:29:02,340
I would do the same if I were the mom.

2211
01:29:02,710 --> 01:29:04,640
But what I'm arguing isn't...

2212
01:29:04,770 --> 01:29:07,310
that we shouldn't punish those parents.

2213
01:29:07,310 --> 01:29:08,610
I'm just doing it.

2214
01:29:08,680 --> 01:29:10,780
Whether I get caught and go to prison,

2215
01:29:10,780 --> 01:29:12,650
like with autonomous crossing,

2216
01:29:12,650 --> 01:29:14,120
I'm willing to pay the price myself.

2217
01:29:14,120 --> 01:29:15,520
Because this is my conviction.

2218
01:29:15,750 --> 01:29:18,620
I think it's more or less a given...

2219
01:29:18,620 --> 01:29:20,520
that the hacking was done
to do something good.

2220
01:29:20,820 --> 01:29:23,690
But hacking itself is a crime.

2221
01:29:23,930 --> 01:29:26,530
If we allow an individual's crime...

2222
01:29:26,800 --> 01:29:29,100
in order to stop a team's crime...

2223
01:29:29,500 --> 01:29:32,640
since a team is formed by
individuals coming together,

2224
01:29:32,700 --> 01:29:35,770
I think the sentence itself
is contradictory.

2225
01:29:35,910 --> 01:29:39,980
So I'm voting to disagree.

2226
01:29:39,980 --> 01:29:41,010
Yes, for now.

2227
01:29:41,110 --> 01:29:44,480
When someone who doesn't properly
follow the law...

2228
01:29:44,480 --> 01:29:46,820
gets a slap on the wrist,

2229
01:29:46,820 --> 01:29:48,420
that outrage leads to vigilantism.

2230
01:29:48,420 --> 01:29:51,020
You can't necessarily
say that's a bad thing.

2231
01:29:51,020 --> 01:29:53,990
When we were kids,
if someone was being sleazy...

2232
01:29:54,120 --> 01:29:55,990
or cheating at the arcade,

2233
01:29:56,090 --> 01:29:57,530
the older guys would go over
and beat them up.

2234
01:29:58,030 --> 01:30:01,400
Socially, a kind of atmosphere was formed.

2235
01:30:01,460 --> 01:30:03,730
Being sleazy is bad,

2236
01:30:03,830 --> 01:30:06,040
and you have to show etiquette
when playing games.

2237
01:30:06,270 --> 01:30:09,440
But these days, kids who play
PC games never learned that.

2238
01:30:09,540 --> 01:30:10,640
They're out here cursing at people's moms,

2239
01:30:10,640 --> 01:30:12,680
asking, "Do you even have a mom or not?"

2240
01:30:13,140 --> 01:30:15,310
Can we send the kids to prison?

2241
01:30:15,310 --> 01:30:16,410
No, we can't.

2242
01:30:16,410 --> 01:30:18,010
We need those older guys...

2243
01:30:18,080 --> 01:30:20,280
who used to beat people up at the arcade.

2244
01:30:20,280 --> 01:30:22,080
I think that's what hackers are here.

2245
01:30:22,450 --> 01:30:24,120
Since the law
isn't doing its job properly,

2246
01:30:24,120 --> 01:30:26,390
isn't that why hackers resort...

2247
01:30:26,390 --> 01:30:28,220
to private retaliation through hacking?

2248
01:30:28,220 --> 01:30:31,590
I kept calculating and thinking about it,

2249
01:30:31,830 --> 01:30:33,660
and if an opportunity like this...

2250
01:30:33,660 --> 01:30:35,830
came to me right now, at this point,
I think I'd do it.

2251
01:30:36,630 --> 01:30:39,000
- Her eyes changed.
- I'll go with the consequence.

2252
01:30:39,000 --> 01:30:40,340
Reading this sentence,

2253
01:30:40,340 --> 01:30:42,710
I admit, I find it somewhat gratifying.

2254
01:30:42,710 --> 01:30:44,010
Even so,

2255
01:30:44,010 --> 01:30:45,810
what bothers me about this is...

2256
01:30:45,810 --> 01:30:48,240
Does this really make our society stable?

2257
01:30:48,240 --> 01:30:51,680
I think it violates our social contract.

2258
01:30:51,680 --> 01:30:54,480
If you hack an account and donate it all,

2259
01:30:54,480 --> 01:30:57,150
you may think you did a truly good deed.

2260
01:30:57,150 --> 01:30:58,420
But once you've gone that far,

2261
01:30:58,420 --> 01:31:00,120
there will always be a next step.

2262
01:31:00,120 --> 01:31:03,090
Then you'd decide
what makes a company corrupt,

2263
01:31:03,090 --> 01:31:05,430
and who must donate every last cent.

2264
01:31:05,430 --> 01:31:07,260
You'd decide all of that yourself.

2265
01:31:07,260 --> 01:31:09,330
Personal greed could creep in too.

2266
01:31:09,330 --> 01:31:10,970
So when we make an exception...

2267
01:31:10,970 --> 01:31:14,140
that begins with good intentions,

2268
01:31:14,140 --> 01:31:17,610
I think it will eventually do great harm
to society.

2269
01:31:17,610 --> 01:31:20,510
As for my public persona,

2270
01:31:20,510 --> 01:31:22,910
I'm pretty timid, honestly.

2271
01:31:22,910 --> 01:31:24,580
It's less about a sense of justice...

2272
01:31:24,580 --> 01:31:26,720
and more about wanting to become...

2273
01:31:26,720 --> 01:31:28,950
that kind of person deep down.

2274
01:31:28,950 --> 01:31:30,550
In reality,

2275
01:31:30,550 --> 01:31:32,520
I couldn't do it. I'm not capable either.

2276
01:31:32,520 --> 01:31:35,720
But if I could
do something socially meaningful...

2277
01:31:35,720 --> 01:31:37,530
outside the bounds of the law,

2278
01:31:37,530 --> 01:31:39,900
if I were ever in that position,

2279
01:31:39,900 --> 01:31:41,400
I might give it a try.

2280
01:31:41,500 --> 01:31:43,730
Ultimately, through an illegal act,

2281
01:31:43,730 --> 01:31:45,570
the hacker harmed this company.

2282
01:31:45,840 --> 01:31:49,170
But the ones who would pay the price...

2283
01:31:49,170 --> 01:31:51,270
are the employees below...

2284
01:31:51,270 --> 01:31:53,610
and their families. That's what I thought.

2285
01:31:53,880 --> 01:31:55,980
By that logic,

2286
01:31:55,980 --> 01:31:58,350
wouldn't other innocent citizens...

2287
01:31:58,350 --> 01:31:59,820
also be harmed?

2288
01:31:59,820 --> 01:32:02,050
But that harm...

2289
01:32:02,050 --> 01:32:04,220
isn't caused by the hacker.

2290
01:32:04,220 --> 01:32:06,720
It's because the company failed to pay...

2291
01:32:06,720 --> 01:32:08,720
the taxes it rightfully owed,

2292
01:32:08,720 --> 01:32:10,030
and because the owner...

2293
01:32:10,030 --> 01:32:11,990
and executives did wrong.

2294
01:32:11,990 --> 01:32:13,760
That's why those people are harmed.

2295
01:32:13,760 --> 01:32:15,560
It isn't the hacker's fault.

2296
01:32:15,560 --> 01:32:16,630
That's true.

2297
01:32:16,970 --> 01:32:19,740
Innocent people working there...

2298
01:32:19,840 --> 01:32:21,900
have no way of knowing whether...

2299
01:32:21,900 --> 01:32:25,010
the company profited from tax evasion...

2300
01:32:25,010 --> 01:32:26,710
or through legitimate business...

2301
01:32:26,710 --> 01:32:27,940
and paying their salaries with it.

2302
01:32:27,940 --> 01:32:30,010
So if this company is ultimately...

2303
01:32:30,010 --> 01:32:32,450
harmed by a white hat hacker,

2304
01:32:32,450 --> 01:32:34,920
and innocent people lose their jobs,

2305
01:32:35,280 --> 01:32:36,920
their suffering...

2306
01:32:36,920 --> 01:32:39,020
is worth as much as the money...

2307
01:32:39,220 --> 01:32:41,620
that would've funded a charity.

2308
01:32:41,620 --> 01:32:43,690
The people who lose their jobs,

2309
01:32:43,690 --> 01:32:45,690
and the pain their families endure...

2310
01:32:45,690 --> 01:32:47,800
You could calculate that value.

2311
01:32:47,800 --> 01:32:48,960
On the other hand,

2312
01:32:48,960 --> 01:32:50,600
because this much tax...

2313
01:32:50,600 --> 01:32:52,470
that should've gone to our country...

2314
01:32:52,470 --> 01:32:54,870
was never collected,

2315
01:32:54,900 --> 01:32:56,470
some people suffered as well.

2316
01:32:56,570 --> 01:32:58,710
There may be sick children in hospitals...

2317
01:32:58,710 --> 01:33:00,180
who receive no tax-funded support...

2318
01:33:00,180 --> 01:33:01,910
and may end up dying.

2319
01:33:01,910 --> 01:33:04,650
It's hard to say their lives matter less.

2320
01:33:04,650 --> 01:33:07,280
I like expected value too. However,

2321
01:33:07,450 --> 01:33:09,350
even within the bounds of the law,

2322
01:33:09,350 --> 01:33:11,450
you can prove this company is corrupt...

2323
01:33:11,450 --> 01:33:13,590
and committing tax evasion.

2324
01:33:13,590 --> 01:33:15,590
Laws are always changing,

2325
01:33:15,590 --> 01:33:17,490
and they have changed throughout history.

2326
01:33:17,490 --> 01:33:19,800
Even the principles we believe in...

2327
01:33:19,800 --> 01:33:23,430
may eventually change one day.

2328
01:33:23,470 --> 01:33:24,900
So,

2329
01:33:25,000 --> 01:33:26,670
what makes today's debate interesting...

2330
01:33:27,040 --> 01:33:30,670
is how much flexibility we should allow.

2331
01:33:30,670 --> 01:33:32,210
That's how I viewed the issue.

2332
01:33:32,210 --> 01:33:33,880
Flexibility is something...

2333
01:33:33,880 --> 01:33:35,010
we can apply in our thinking.

2334
01:33:35,010 --> 01:33:38,880
But if the law sets something,

2335
01:33:38,880 --> 01:33:40,420
we have no choice but to follow it.

2336
01:33:40,750 --> 01:33:42,450
Should we follow the law,

2337
01:33:42,450 --> 01:33:44,220
or should the law follow us?

2338
01:33:44,220 --> 01:33:45,490
The thing is,

2339
01:33:45,490 --> 01:33:48,220
the law already exists when we're born.

2340
01:33:48,220 --> 01:33:49,930
So I believe we should follow it.

2341
01:33:49,930 --> 01:33:51,290
As we abide by the law,

2342
01:33:51,290 --> 01:33:53,200
if innocent people keep getting hurt,

2343
01:33:53,200 --> 01:33:55,160
the issue will enter public debate.

2344
01:33:55,300 --> 01:33:57,170
Once we recognize there's a problem,

2345
01:33:57,170 --> 01:34:00,870
we should understand the law is...

2346
01:34:00,870 --> 01:34:03,440
naturally going through a transition.

2347
01:34:03,440 --> 01:34:04,610
You're not changing the law.

2348
01:34:04,610 --> 01:34:06,080
You're taking justice into your own hands.

2349
01:34:06,080 --> 01:34:08,540
That's right.
But you're still breaking the law.

2350
01:34:08,540 --> 01:34:10,650
If we allow that kind of flexibility,

2351
01:34:10,650 --> 01:34:13,950
it could lead to
far too many copycat crimes.

2352
01:34:13,950 --> 01:34:15,820
That's my concern.

2353
01:34:15,920 --> 01:34:17,390
It was fun.

2354
01:34:17,390 --> 01:34:19,360
We could secure food, after all.

2355
01:34:19,360 --> 01:34:21,320
One banana each time?

2356
01:34:21,320 --> 01:34:22,890
Let's eat plenty of bananas.

2357
01:34:22,890 --> 01:34:24,490
So I participated enthusiastically.

2358
01:34:24,490 --> 01:34:27,500
I think Vector fell for my strategy.

2359
01:34:27,630 --> 01:34:30,270
I may have looked worked up.

2360
01:34:30,270 --> 01:34:33,240
That probably made Team Black nervous.

2361
01:34:33,640 --> 01:34:35,800
(Majority Rules Game results)

2362
01:34:36,070 --> 01:34:37,910
Are we getting the results now?

2363
01:34:38,210 --> 01:34:41,280
- The Majority Rules Game results...
- Let's see.

2364
01:34:41,280 --> 01:34:43,110
- will now be announced.
- Drumroll, please.

2365
01:34:43,180 --> 01:34:44,310
Let's see.

2366
01:34:45,810 --> 01:34:47,580
(Principle wins the Majority Rules Game.)

2367
01:34:47,880 --> 01:34:49,820
- You really stood by your beliefs.
- Congratulations.

2368
01:34:49,820 --> 01:34:51,350
Two people switched sides.

2369
01:34:51,350 --> 01:34:53,190
Fewer people switched today, at least.

2370
01:34:53,190 --> 01:34:54,620
Because they're new.

2371
01:34:57,090 --> 01:35:00,060
In the Majority Rules Game, to score,

2372
01:35:00,060 --> 01:35:01,860
judging by these numbers...

2373
01:35:01,860 --> 01:35:03,300
there are a lot of principled voters.

2374
01:35:03,530 --> 01:35:04,900
I was a little disappointed.

2375
01:35:04,900 --> 01:35:07,600
I had a sense of how it would turn out,

2376
01:35:07,600 --> 01:35:09,100
but did I dig my heels in for no reason?

2377
01:35:09,240 --> 01:35:10,840
You can tell just by looking.

2378
01:35:10,840 --> 01:35:13,340
You can tell they stick to principles.

2379
01:35:13,340 --> 01:35:15,310
Would people like that change their vote?

2380
01:35:15,410 --> 01:35:17,080
Of course they wouldn't.

2381
01:35:17,250 --> 01:35:18,380
So,

2382
01:35:18,450 --> 01:35:20,350
following consequentialist principles,

2383
01:35:20,350 --> 01:35:21,420
I changed my vote.

2384
01:35:21,750 --> 01:35:26,790
(Principle: Disagree, Consequences: Agree)

2385
01:35:26,890 --> 01:35:28,320
Normally, if you're a consequentialist,

2386
01:35:28,320 --> 01:35:30,690
- isn't it natural to switch here?
- Today's MVP is...

2387
01:35:30,690 --> 01:35:32,190
Maillard.

2388
01:35:34,100 --> 01:35:35,630
Congratulations.

2389
01:35:35,860 --> 01:35:37,200
(Maillard, the casting voter, named MVP)

2390
01:35:37,200 --> 01:35:38,430
- Congratulations.
- That's incredible.

2391
01:35:38,430 --> 01:35:39,600
That's incredible.

2392
01:35:39,770 --> 01:35:41,300
I don't know how the points from...

2393
01:35:41,300 --> 01:35:43,210
the Majority Rules Game will be used,

2394
01:35:43,210 --> 01:35:46,310
but I didn't want them getting too many.

2395
01:35:46,310 --> 01:35:48,710
Our team discussed giving Maillard...

2396
01:35:48,710 --> 01:35:51,410
all our MVP votes.

2397
01:35:51,550 --> 01:35:53,450
When you coordinate votes,

2398
01:35:53,450 --> 01:35:55,150
it's incredibly easy to make someone MVP.

2399
01:35:55,150 --> 01:35:57,490
Maillard had never won MVP before,

2400
01:35:57,490 --> 01:35:59,090
so we decided to give him all our votes.

2401
01:35:59,320 --> 01:36:01,720
I'm grateful. I hadn't earned many points.

2402
01:36:01,720 --> 01:36:03,090
Thankfully,

2403
01:36:03,090 --> 01:36:04,130
I earned a few today.

2404
01:36:04,690 --> 01:36:06,130
Debate points...

2405
01:36:06,130 --> 01:36:08,030
as we get closer to the end,

2406
01:36:08,030 --> 01:36:09,670
might become a lifeline, don't you think?

2407
01:36:09,670 --> 01:36:12,570
So I think they're surprisingly important.

2408
01:36:14,370 --> 01:36:17,810
The Leader Negotiation will be held soon.

2409
01:36:18,070 --> 01:36:19,880
After the Leader Negotiation,

2410
01:36:19,880 --> 01:36:22,310
today's life submission will begin.

2411
01:36:22,340 --> 01:36:23,710
What do we have left now?

2412
01:36:23,980 --> 01:36:26,620
- One diamond?
- Team Red is too powerful now.

2413
01:36:26,780 --> 01:36:27,880
But still,

2414
01:36:27,880 --> 01:36:30,720
Maillard won MVP this time too.

2415
01:36:30,720 --> 01:36:31,790
That's right.

2416
01:36:32,220 --> 01:36:35,720
Team White seemed so kind,

2417
01:36:35,720 --> 01:36:37,590
but they suddenly changed...

2418
01:36:37,590 --> 01:36:42,300
and became extremely selfish. It was so...

2419
01:36:42,300 --> 01:36:43,430
- ridiculously funny.
- It was entertaining.

2420
01:36:43,430 --> 01:36:44,570
It's a comedy.

2421
01:36:45,600 --> 01:36:47,770
Then Black really...

2422
01:36:47,770 --> 01:36:49,610
has no one but Team White to rely on.

2423
01:36:49,710 --> 01:36:52,110
Their only option is turning diamonds
into prize money.

2424
01:36:52,410 --> 01:36:54,310
Black and Team White are allies now.

2425
01:36:54,310 --> 01:36:55,340
All of a sudden.

2426
01:36:55,340 --> 01:36:58,110
- They're allies, yet he wants them dead.
- He keeps saying they must die.

2427
01:36:58,350 --> 01:37:00,480
Why did Vector lose it today?

2428
01:37:00,580 --> 01:37:03,820
He's usually so calm and analytical.

2429
01:37:04,520 --> 01:37:06,050
- What got into him?
- Exactly.

2430
01:37:20,500 --> 01:37:22,200
They must be calling the leaders now.

2431
01:37:22,740 --> 01:37:24,740
All team leaders, please gather...

2432
01:37:24,740 --> 01:37:27,380
at the Community Center.

2433
01:37:28,980 --> 01:37:31,080
- Good luck.
- See you. Good luck.

2434
01:37:31,080 --> 01:37:33,020
- Good luck.
- We have nothing to trade, right?

2435
01:37:33,020 --> 01:37:34,850
- The agenda...
- Just listen carefully.

2436
01:37:34,850 --> 01:37:37,490
- Pretend you don't know much.
- It's the first day.

2437
01:37:37,490 --> 01:37:39,690
It's the first day, and we should...

2438
01:37:39,690 --> 01:37:42,020
- keep trying to bring Team Red in.
- Right?

2439
01:37:42,020 --> 01:37:43,730
- I'll just go and come back.
- Yes.

2440
01:37:52,670 --> 01:37:56,170
(Community Center)

2441
01:37:56,840 --> 01:37:59,840
- Stand in front of the yellow spot.
- Is that right?

2442
01:38:00,410 --> 01:38:02,640
So this happens every day.

2443
01:38:02,640 --> 01:38:03,750
That's right.

2444
01:38:06,250 --> 01:38:07,620
- Hello.
- Hello.

2445
01:38:07,620 --> 01:38:08,820
Hello.

2446
01:38:09,920 --> 01:38:11,250
Why did you bring diamonds?

2447
01:38:12,050 --> 01:38:13,290
- Just in case.
- We will now begin...

2448
01:38:13,290 --> 01:38:15,320
the Leader Negotiation.

2449
01:38:15,420 --> 01:38:18,190
First, here is Community Town's...

2450
01:38:18,190 --> 01:38:20,230
pollution index for today.

2451
01:38:20,300 --> 01:38:22,600
The pollution index over five days...

2452
01:38:22,600 --> 01:38:24,700
is 41 in total.

2453
01:38:25,270 --> 01:38:28,370
Please note. Once the index reaches 100,

2454
01:38:28,370 --> 01:38:30,310
the town will be considered saturated.

2455
01:38:30,440 --> 01:38:33,680
I should explain this pollution index.

2456
01:38:33,680 --> 01:38:35,210
The pollution index...

2457
01:38:35,210 --> 01:38:36,810
tracks credit usage.

2458
01:38:37,110 --> 01:38:40,120
Forty-one polluting credits were used.

2459
01:38:40,250 --> 01:38:43,390
Including the credits on the Platform,

2460
01:38:43,390 --> 01:38:45,050
we're in a somewhat dangerous situation.

2461
01:38:45,520 --> 01:38:47,320
If all of them enter circulation,

2462
01:38:47,320 --> 01:38:48,990
we could go slightly over 100.

2463
01:38:48,990 --> 01:38:50,630
So starting tomorrow,

2464
01:38:50,630 --> 01:38:54,760
we need to begin mining
pollution-free credits.

2465
01:38:54,830 --> 01:38:57,170
The maximum output is 20 a day.

2466
01:38:57,900 --> 01:39:00,740
I explained the pollution index.

2467
01:39:00,840 --> 01:39:03,910
I wanted to raise the value of credits.

2468
01:39:03,910 --> 01:39:07,380
Until now, we could mine up to 30 a day.

2469
01:39:07,380 --> 01:39:10,250
But now we must manage pollution,

2470
01:39:10,250 --> 01:39:12,450
so total output will fall.

2471
01:39:12,450 --> 01:39:14,250
A drop in total output...

2472
01:39:14,250 --> 01:39:17,490
means fewer credits to go around.

2473
01:39:17,590 --> 01:39:19,620
So even if we give them fewer,

2474
01:39:19,620 --> 01:39:23,130
I wanted them to understand
they should fetch a fair price.

2475
01:39:23,230 --> 01:39:24,830
That's why I brought it up.

2476
01:39:24,930 --> 01:39:29,160
Credits can harm the public,

2477
01:39:29,360 --> 01:39:32,630
so it would benefit all of us...

2478
01:39:32,630 --> 01:39:35,740
if everyone disclosed their holdings.

2479
01:39:35,740 --> 01:39:37,840
Could you tell us how many credits...

2480
01:39:37,840 --> 01:39:39,610
- How many credits we have?
- Yes.

2481
01:39:39,710 --> 01:39:42,840
Just listen and pretend you don't know.

2482
01:39:43,210 --> 01:39:46,280
I don't fully understand it yet.

2483
01:39:46,280 --> 01:39:49,020
- I see.
- I'll figure it out by tomorrow.

2484
01:39:49,020 --> 01:39:50,550
The number of credits.

2485
01:39:50,720 --> 01:39:53,790
- Luna probably understands it well.
- Yes.

2486
01:39:53,790 --> 01:39:55,490
I'm sure she'll agree.

2487
01:39:55,990 --> 01:39:58,030
Your first Leader Negotiation...

2488
01:39:58,030 --> 01:39:59,090
can be overwhelming.

2489
01:39:59,090 --> 01:40:01,160
A lot of things come at you at once.

2490
01:40:01,160 --> 01:40:03,370
The pollution index suddenly popped up,

2491
01:40:03,370 --> 01:40:04,670
so it must have been confusing.

2492
01:40:05,030 --> 01:40:06,230
- I'll look into it.
- Yes.

2493
01:40:07,600 --> 01:40:09,270
Here's the first agenda item.

2494
01:40:09,710 --> 01:40:11,540
This concerns introducing gold...

2495
01:40:11,540 --> 01:40:13,740
to the Platform and supermarket.

2496
01:40:13,840 --> 01:40:15,240
- What?
- Today,

2497
01:40:15,240 --> 01:40:18,450
a new team, Team Gold, moved in.

2498
01:40:18,710 --> 01:40:22,990
But Community Town's Platform...

2499
01:40:22,990 --> 01:40:25,090
and supermarket don't accept gold yet.

2500
01:40:25,650 --> 01:40:28,920
If 3 of the 5 leaders agree,

2501
01:40:29,220 --> 01:40:31,090
gold will be accepted...

2502
01:40:31,090 --> 01:40:33,500
on the Platform and at the supermarket.

2503
01:40:33,700 --> 01:40:36,200
Because today is Team Gold's first day,

2504
01:40:36,200 --> 01:40:38,970
this can only be discussed today.

2505
01:40:38,970 --> 01:40:40,540
If the negotiation fails,

2506
01:40:40,540 --> 01:40:42,370
it cannot be discussed again.

2507
01:40:42,400 --> 01:40:45,710
We want our new currency, gold,

2508
01:40:45,710 --> 01:40:47,910
to be accepted at the supermarket.

2509
01:40:47,910 --> 01:40:50,450
Today's decision is final.

2510
01:40:50,510 --> 01:40:52,550
As the issuer of diamonds,

2511
01:40:52,550 --> 01:40:55,220
another currency entering...

2512
01:40:55,220 --> 01:40:57,290
our exclusive Platform must be stopped.

2513
01:40:57,890 --> 01:41:00,320
I wanted it to pass.

2514
01:41:00,420 --> 01:41:02,290
Because without it,

2515
01:41:02,290 --> 01:41:04,390
Team Gold's most likely move...

2516
01:41:04,390 --> 01:41:07,630
would be to start a war.

2517
01:41:07,630 --> 01:41:09,730
They need some breathing room...

2518
01:41:09,730 --> 01:41:12,830
and space to play their own game.

2519
01:41:12,830 --> 01:41:15,100
If diamonds aren't a burden to them,

2520
01:41:15,100 --> 01:41:17,870
they won't consider taking them by force.

2521
01:41:18,210 --> 01:41:20,940
I think you already know...

2522
01:41:20,940 --> 01:41:22,640
- where I stand.
- Yes.

2523
01:41:22,640 --> 01:41:26,650
Since we distribute diamonds,

2524
01:41:26,750 --> 01:41:28,520
if there are two currencies...

2525
01:41:28,520 --> 01:41:30,050
There already are two, but...

2526
01:41:30,050 --> 01:41:31,890
if there are also two payment channels,

2527
01:41:31,890 --> 01:41:35,320
Team Gold would gain even more power.

2528
01:41:35,320 --> 01:41:38,530
Diamonds can't be traded directly.

2529
01:41:38,530 --> 01:41:41,860
All trades go through the Platform.

2530
01:41:41,860 --> 01:41:45,470
Gold can already be used
to trade resources directly.

2531
01:41:45,470 --> 01:41:47,870
If it's also allowed on the Platform,

2532
01:41:47,870 --> 01:41:50,640
I think Team Gold will gain more power.

2533
01:41:50,640 --> 01:41:52,070
Trades with Team Gold...

2534
01:41:52,070 --> 01:41:54,440
can already be made directly, so...

2535
01:41:54,440 --> 01:41:57,910
But here, you can't purchase
any basic necessities...

2536
01:41:58,180 --> 01:42:00,150
like food.

2537
01:42:00,150 --> 01:42:01,280
If you just make up your mind,

2538
01:42:01,280 --> 01:42:04,690
you can trade gold or diamonds
whatever you want.

2539
01:42:04,690 --> 01:42:07,120
You could buy gold
and switch it to diamonds.

2540
01:42:07,120 --> 01:42:08,820
Since you have the negotiation power,

2541
01:42:08,820 --> 01:42:11,230
I want you to be more careful...

2542
01:42:11,230 --> 01:42:14,530
and more conservative about this.

2543
01:42:14,860 --> 01:42:17,130
There is a war going on,

2544
01:42:17,130 --> 01:42:19,470
and things are becoming pretty extreme.

2545
01:42:19,470 --> 01:42:23,070
In that case, we shouldn't avoid
a competition...

2546
01:42:23,070 --> 01:42:25,010
through a virtuous cycle.

2547
01:42:25,010 --> 01:42:28,980
I believe that could actually reduce
the pressure.

2548
01:42:28,980 --> 01:42:33,520
In the end, everyone here
will obtain various resources,

2549
01:42:33,520 --> 01:42:35,320
and we will follow...

2550
01:42:35,320 --> 01:42:37,550
whoever has the power.

2551
01:42:37,550 --> 01:42:39,620
Since we've never tried the gold system,

2552
01:42:39,620 --> 01:42:42,790
there may be a little bit of resistance,

2553
01:42:42,790 --> 01:42:45,530
but if it's introduced,
we'll keep it transparent.

2554
01:42:45,530 --> 01:42:47,560
We'll do our best to continue...

2555
01:42:47,560 --> 01:42:50,900
what Vector has done until now.

2556
01:42:51,530 --> 01:42:53,900
From my perspective,
it has to be transparent.

2557
01:42:53,900 --> 01:42:57,070
But the thing is,
if we can trade gold from now on,

2558
01:42:57,070 --> 01:43:00,680
that gives Team Black a choice.

2559
01:43:00,680 --> 01:43:02,840
I was curious about Team Black's opinion
the most.

2560
01:43:02,840 --> 01:43:05,250
To him, an unexpected variable
suddenly appeared.

2561
01:43:12,750 --> 01:43:14,220
Actually...

2562
01:43:15,020 --> 01:43:17,290
It's been five days as of today, right?

2563
01:43:17,290 --> 01:43:20,300
For five days, I've received...

2564
01:43:20,300 --> 01:43:22,100
all kinds of suspicions and slander.

2565
01:43:22,100 --> 01:43:25,730
But just because I can't receive gold,

2566
01:43:25,970 --> 01:43:28,140
people are finally starting
to give me trust.

2567
01:43:28,640 --> 01:43:30,310
To gain more trust,

2568
01:43:30,310 --> 01:43:32,770
gold shouldn't be introduced.

2569
01:43:35,480 --> 01:43:36,480
But...

2570
01:43:38,180 --> 01:43:40,950
I believe we should do it...

2571
01:43:40,950 --> 01:43:43,050
because if it's not introduced,

2572
01:43:43,050 --> 01:43:46,490
the only thing Team Gold can do is...

2573
01:43:46,690 --> 01:43:48,120
a war.

2574
01:43:48,620 --> 01:43:50,330
What can we do by stealing resources?

2575
01:43:50,330 --> 01:43:53,700
If we steal lives,
people start dying one by one.

2576
01:43:53,700 --> 01:43:55,400
In the end,
a majority will join Team Gold.

2577
01:43:55,400 --> 01:43:58,230
Then without sharing...

2578
01:43:58,230 --> 01:44:00,270
any of their gold,

2579
01:44:00,270 --> 01:44:01,700
Team Gold will just win,

2580
01:44:01,700 --> 01:44:02,840
and the game will end.

2581
01:44:03,670 --> 01:44:04,670
Are you...

2582
01:44:05,510 --> 01:44:06,510
okay with that?

2583
01:44:06,780 --> 01:44:09,980
Of course, there are risks,

2584
01:44:09,980 --> 01:44:12,250
but I was very happy today.

2585
01:44:12,610 --> 01:44:14,820
- That's not the point.
- I...

2586
01:44:14,820 --> 01:44:16,990
- I can't give up on that.
- What are you talking about?

2587
01:44:16,990 --> 01:44:18,420
- I didn't realize...
- Why is he...

2588
01:44:18,420 --> 01:44:19,820
how important trust was until now.

2589
01:44:19,820 --> 01:44:22,020
You've been playing with logic until now.

2590
01:44:22,020 --> 01:44:23,890
Are you given a mission or something?

2591
01:44:25,130 --> 01:44:27,360
I had such an exciting day today.
I'm sorry.

2592
01:44:27,360 --> 01:44:29,930
But that's not how you've been playing.

2593
01:44:29,930 --> 01:44:31,600
This makes no sense.

2594
01:44:31,600 --> 01:44:33,700
Because you've changed so much today,

2595
01:44:33,700 --> 01:44:35,540
I'm suspecting you even more.

2596
01:44:36,100 --> 01:44:39,240
You've been playing with logic.

2597
01:44:39,240 --> 01:44:40,910
You have no reason to oppose this.

2598
01:44:40,910 --> 01:44:42,710
If that's introduced,

2599
01:44:43,040 --> 01:44:46,480
you can also handle gold.

2600
01:44:46,480 --> 01:44:48,650
It is true that it gives me
more possibilities...

2601
01:44:49,280 --> 01:44:51,220
if I handle gold,

2602
01:44:51,220 --> 01:44:53,320
but I'd lose trust in return.

2603
01:44:53,720 --> 01:44:57,590
Considering my relationship
with Team White,

2604
01:44:57,590 --> 01:45:00,130
I'd lose their trust
as soon as this is introduced.

2605
01:45:00,800 --> 01:45:02,130
- For that reason...
- Team Blue.

2606
01:45:02,130 --> 01:45:03,570
What's your opinion?

2607
01:45:03,730 --> 01:45:06,530
I'm not really sure...

2608
01:45:06,530 --> 01:45:10,810
about what's the best decision
for everyone...

2609
01:45:10,810 --> 01:45:12,310
or the decision I should make
for the community.

2610
01:45:15,540 --> 01:45:19,050
I believe the information imbalance is...

2611
01:45:19,050 --> 01:45:21,180
the biggest weapon in this game.

2612
01:45:21,180 --> 01:45:24,450
Between us,

2613
01:45:24,450 --> 01:45:26,790
we know how we can go after each other.

2614
01:45:26,790 --> 01:45:30,090
But we know nothing about Team Gold yet.

2615
01:45:30,090 --> 01:45:34,030
I didn't know we were revealing
the credits here today.

2616
01:45:34,030 --> 01:45:36,460
That's why I said I'd tell you tomorrow.

2617
01:45:36,460 --> 01:45:38,400
If we issue it,

2618
01:45:38,400 --> 01:45:40,500
you can still see it on the screen.

2619
01:45:40,500 --> 01:45:44,670
Our information is revealed real time.

2620
01:45:44,670 --> 01:45:46,310
So you have to admit
that information we have...

2621
01:45:46,310 --> 01:45:49,240
is more reliable and credible.

2622
01:45:49,240 --> 01:45:52,210
We currently have a limit on issurance.

2623
01:45:52,710 --> 01:45:54,280
But no one knows...

2624
01:45:54,280 --> 01:45:57,420
how much Team Gold can issue.

2625
01:45:57,420 --> 01:45:59,920
If you're talking about the possibility
of us increasing the amount...

2626
01:45:59,920 --> 01:46:02,220
to drop the value,

2627
01:46:02,220 --> 01:46:05,290
that also applies to diamonds.

2628
01:46:05,290 --> 01:46:08,160
If we were to backstab you like that,

2629
01:46:08,160 --> 01:46:10,430
it can be punished immediately.

2630
01:46:10,430 --> 01:46:12,330
- That's nothing to worry about.
- Let me ask you something.

2631
01:46:12,330 --> 01:46:14,370
Do you have a limit on issurance?

2632
01:46:14,700 --> 01:46:17,110
From what I've heard,

2633
01:46:17,110 --> 01:46:19,240
there's no limit.

2634
01:46:22,340 --> 01:46:25,080
If they can issue gold without a limit,

2635
01:46:25,080 --> 01:46:26,880
how would count on gold?

2636
01:46:26,880 --> 01:46:29,950
Thank you so much
for sharing the bad news.

2637
01:46:30,590 --> 01:46:32,690
I'm just telling you the rule.

2638
01:46:32,690 --> 01:46:35,920
That gives us even more reason
not to trust gold.

2639
01:46:35,920 --> 01:46:37,990
I'm against the idea of introducing it.

2640
01:46:37,990 --> 01:46:39,530
Raise your hand if you're against it.

2641
01:46:39,530 --> 01:46:41,030
- Raise your hand.
- I'm against it.

2642
01:46:41,030 --> 01:46:42,100
I'm in favor.

2643
01:46:49,370 --> 01:46:53,680
Casting vote itself focuses on Team Red.

2644
01:46:54,540 --> 01:46:56,680
These three are the casting voters.

2645
01:46:56,680 --> 01:46:58,780
What about me?

2646
01:46:59,110 --> 01:47:02,980
(Team Blue had no influence
when it came to Team Red's opinion.)

2647
01:47:04,350 --> 01:47:06,320
Just because Team Red was in,

2648
01:47:06,320 --> 01:47:08,720
I couldn't just say,
"Since I teamed up with Team Red,"

2649
01:47:08,720 --> 01:47:10,530
"I'll go with whatever they say."

2650
01:47:10,530 --> 01:47:13,130
In the end, Team Black is...

2651
01:47:13,130 --> 01:47:15,730
becoming my precious ally.

2652
01:47:15,730 --> 01:47:18,630
And they're going against each other.

2653
01:47:18,630 --> 01:47:22,000
Team Black is a precious friend.

2654
01:47:22,300 --> 01:47:25,070
I just focused on making
the best choice for the team.

2655
01:47:25,070 --> 01:47:27,240
Teams Blue, Black, and White are
against it.

2656
01:47:27,240 --> 01:47:28,810
(3 oppose)

2657
01:47:28,810 --> 01:47:31,810
Teams Red and Gold are in favor.

2658
01:47:31,980 --> 01:47:36,150
(The negotiation to introduce gold
broke down.)

2659
01:47:36,850 --> 01:47:39,090
I'm not asking them...

2660
01:47:39,290 --> 01:47:41,190
to count gold as currency.

2661
01:47:41,190 --> 01:47:43,220
I'm saying we should help
a majority benefit...

2662
01:47:43,220 --> 01:47:46,690
through a competition.

2663
01:47:46,690 --> 01:47:50,100
And if gold has no value later,

2664
01:47:50,100 --> 01:47:53,700
we can always choose diamonds at the end.

2665
01:47:53,700 --> 01:47:56,540
But instead,

2666
01:47:56,540 --> 01:47:59,610
by blocking the use of gold,

2667
01:47:59,610 --> 01:48:03,950
they want to strengthen
what's already happening...

2668
01:48:04,150 --> 01:48:07,380
in the market.

2669
01:48:07,380 --> 01:48:09,080
This isn't an invisible hand.

2670
01:48:09,080 --> 01:48:11,350
This is a definitely visible hand.

2671
01:48:11,350 --> 01:48:13,460
They're blinded by the diamonds
before their eyes.

2672
01:48:13,460 --> 01:48:15,390
To avoid a war...

2673
01:48:15,390 --> 01:48:17,190
as much as possible,

2674
01:48:17,190 --> 01:48:18,290
they should've opened the supermarket.

2675
01:48:18,290 --> 01:48:21,030
They only want to play safe.

2676
01:48:21,030 --> 01:48:23,530
In fact, we can't discuss this again..

2677
01:48:23,530 --> 01:48:25,530
after today.

2678
01:48:25,530 --> 01:48:27,140
It's a shame.

2679
01:48:31,670 --> 01:48:33,270
The second agenda item.

2680
01:48:33,710 --> 01:48:37,280
This concerns the decision
to provide aid or impose sanctions.

2681
01:48:37,950 --> 01:48:38,950
This is pointless...

2682
01:48:38,950 --> 01:48:40,920
- with the three of you taking sides.
- It's his first day.

2683
01:48:40,920 --> 01:48:43,490
There's nothing to provide or impose.

2684
01:48:43,490 --> 01:48:44,820
Then let's skip it.

2685
01:48:44,820 --> 01:48:47,720
We'll pass the second agenda item.

2686
01:48:48,590 --> 01:48:50,590
Negotiation failed.

2687
01:48:52,690 --> 01:48:54,130
This game is going nowhere.

2688
01:48:54,860 --> 01:48:57,670
We don't know what skills Team Gold has.

2689
01:48:57,670 --> 01:48:59,270
That's not what I'm saying.
This game is going nowhere.

2690
01:48:59,270 --> 01:49:01,000
We can't play like this.

2691
01:49:01,470 --> 01:49:02,570
What's so hard to understand?

2692
01:49:02,570 --> 01:49:05,170
- This isn't going anywhere.
- All negotiations are complete.

2693
01:49:05,170 --> 01:49:08,480
We'll move on to today's life submission.

2694
01:49:08,840 --> 01:49:11,950
All leaders except the ones
submitting the lives...

2695
01:49:11,950 --> 01:49:14,150
must leave the center.

2696
01:49:32,730 --> 01:49:34,400
I understand what you mean, but...

2697
01:49:34,400 --> 01:49:36,910
Isn't that the only way to enter the game?
And do something?

2698
01:49:36,910 --> 01:49:38,710
But if you don't let them,

2699
01:49:38,710 --> 01:49:39,870
the only choice left is war.

2700
01:49:39,870 --> 01:49:41,280
That's the only option.

2701
01:49:41,280 --> 01:49:44,180
There's an alternative
to exchange the resources.

2702
01:49:44,180 --> 01:49:46,110
This will benefit you too.

2703
01:49:46,110 --> 01:49:48,420
When gold is introduced,
you can cash it out.

2704
01:49:48,420 --> 01:49:50,720
It's nice to have more options,

2705
01:49:50,720 --> 01:49:52,820
but I have no choice to win trust.

2706
01:49:52,820 --> 01:49:53,820
What are you...

2707
01:49:54,720 --> 01:49:56,120
What's up with the trust issue?

2708
01:49:56,120 --> 01:49:57,690
You're not getting notarized.

2709
01:49:58,730 --> 01:50:00,560
This is all verbal consent.
Why is trust so important?

2710
01:50:00,560 --> 01:50:01,900
If you're turned down, you're turned down.

2711
01:50:06,230 --> 01:50:08,240
Please check the contents
of the central box...

2712
01:50:08,240 --> 01:50:12,140
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

2713
01:50:12,570 --> 01:50:13,580
Gosh.

2714
01:50:13,580 --> 01:50:14,980
(Everyone in Team Red survives.)

2715
01:50:18,480 --> 01:50:21,120
Your life submission is complete.

2716
01:50:21,520 --> 01:50:23,750
You may leave now.

2717
01:50:49,040 --> 01:50:51,980
Day Five has officially come to an end.

2718
01:50:52,350 --> 01:50:53,880
Goodnight.

2719
01:50:54,050 --> 01:50:56,250
We voted on introducing gold...

2720
01:50:56,250 --> 01:50:58,350
to the platform and the supermarket.

2721
01:50:58,350 --> 01:51:00,420
And Team Red was strongly against it.

2722
01:51:00,420 --> 01:51:02,820
They wanted to let us use it.

2723
01:51:03,120 --> 01:51:04,530
But Team Blue was the problem.

2724
01:51:04,790 --> 01:51:07,530
Team Blue obviously took
Team Black's side...

2725
01:51:07,530 --> 01:51:09,300
Why did Team Blue take his side?

2726
01:51:09,300 --> 01:51:10,670
- That's what I mean. That makes no sense.
- I don't understand why...

2727
01:51:10,670 --> 01:51:11,970
She's taking it personally.

2728
01:51:11,970 --> 01:51:14,140
It's her decision. We have to respect it.

2729
01:51:14,140 --> 01:51:15,800
So it was voted down in the end.

2730
01:51:15,800 --> 01:51:17,170
What I realized is,

2731
01:51:17,170 --> 01:51:21,580
we must support Team Red's lifeline
with all we have starting tomorrow.

2732
01:51:21,580 --> 01:51:23,710
In the worst-case scenario,

2733
01:51:23,710 --> 01:51:26,410
even if it means a sacrifice of one of us,

2734
01:51:26,410 --> 01:51:28,650
we should think
about giving our lives to them...

2735
01:51:28,650 --> 01:51:31,020
to keep them alive.

2736
01:51:32,750 --> 01:51:34,290
This is going to be tough.

2737
01:51:34,290 --> 01:51:35,790
- Good work today.
- Thank you.

2738
01:51:47,270 --> 01:51:49,200
The code on the wall. I deciphered it.

2739
01:51:50,710 --> 01:51:53,240
The truth of a weapon dealer?

2740
01:51:53,240 --> 01:51:55,040
Is it right? A weapon dealer?

2741
01:51:55,410 --> 01:51:57,080
You can't tell me, obviously.

2742
01:51:57,080 --> 01:51:58,580
(Ugong)

2743
01:51:58,580 --> 01:51:59,580
So...

2744
01:51:59,810 --> 01:52:00,920
My team doesn't know yet.

2745
01:52:01,580 --> 01:52:03,850
To see whether I can activate it alone...

2746
01:52:03,850 --> 01:52:05,790
or possess it alone,

2747
01:52:05,790 --> 01:52:08,090
I'll have to open it first.

2748
01:52:08,090 --> 01:52:11,890
I'm thinking about shouting that word
in the center.

2749
01:52:11,890 --> 01:52:14,400
I know I may look dogmatic.

2750
01:52:14,400 --> 01:52:16,230
But then it'd be a waste
to bring anyone with me...

2751
01:52:16,230 --> 01:52:18,170
when I could use it alone.

2752
01:52:18,170 --> 01:52:19,570
I'm going to give it a try.

2753
01:52:19,570 --> 01:52:21,670
I'll go try it first.

2754
01:52:21,670 --> 01:52:23,240
I hope no one finds out.

2755
01:52:23,240 --> 01:52:25,410
I'm kind of worried about that.

2756
01:52:25,410 --> 01:52:26,810
If the whole town finds out...

2757
01:52:26,810 --> 01:52:29,280
something about the weapon dealer,

2758
01:52:29,580 --> 01:52:31,850
it's not exactly a favorable situation
for me.

2759
01:52:32,310 --> 01:52:34,380
But, yes. That is...

2760
01:52:35,220 --> 01:52:36,220
what's happening so far.

2761
01:52:36,220 --> 01:52:38,690
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)

2762
01:53:13,890 --> 01:53:15,260
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)
